[336]={"Noriel has retreated to the Elf-ruins of Haldirith in Thinglad, at the centre of the forest, upon a hill.\
\
You should speak with Noriel.","Noriel wants you to frighten away the fishermen who have set up nets along the banks of the Anduin in Thinglad.","From a hiding place, <rgb=#FF0000>whistle</rgb> at the nearby fisherman to scare him","Wait a few moments","Find the Elf-outpost of Haldirith","The fisherman's nerves seem shaken","This is a good place to hide","Wait a few moments before continuing.","From a hiding place, <rgb=#FF0000>roar</rgb> at the nearby fisherman to scare him","The fisherman trembles with fear","The fisherman seems frightened","Eso pareció dar resultado","'I think it is much better if the Rohirrim find these lands haunted; do you not agree? They will not disturb us again for two, maybe three generations. Then perhaps we will have to frighten them away once more.'","From a hiding place, <rgb=#FF0000>mumble</rgb> at the nearby fisherman to scare him","A Gentle Nudge","'The Rohirrim have always believed our kind are evil, and that Lothlórien is a haunted place. We feel that this is not entirely a bad belief for them to hold, as it will frighten them away from our borders.\
\
'I had the idea that you could crouch hidden near their camp and make strange noises to frighten the fishermen away. Hopefully, we will not need to resort to more force than simple manipulation.'","The fishermen's camp can be found along the banks of the Anduin in Thinglad.\
\
You should sneak to the camp, crouch in some undergrowth nearby, and perform tricks to try to frighten away the men.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest uses emotes. You must target the intended recipient of the emote in order for quest emotes to work.</rgb>","Wait a few moments before trying again.","From a hiding place, <rgb=#FF0000>clap</rgb> at the nearby fisherman to scare him"},
[337]={"'Los Elfos jamás harían daño a una musaraña. Jamás. Ni siquiera consideraríamos una idea tan horrible. Las musarañas son criaturas buenas y nobles.'","Recoge ramas de madera de cerezo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las ramas de madera de cerezo pueden encontrarse en los campos al sur de Duillond, junto al camino hacia Celondim, probablemente cerca de las bases de los árboles.\
\
Debes recoger madera de cerezo para reforzar las suelas de las botas usadas en el pisoteo de musarañas.","Deluraw se encuentra en Duillond, cerca de los hornos.\
\
Debes llevarle las ramas de cerezo que recogiste a Deluraw.","Lleva las ramas de madera de cerezo a Deluraw","'¡Estas son justo las ramas que necesito! Muchas gracias, ${PLAYER}. Esto garantizará que las musarañas reciban exactamente el grado de disuasión adecuado para su terrible comportamiento.'","Un Arma Suave","'Estoy casi sin la madera de cerezo que uso para la parte más importante de las botas..... ¡la suela! La suela se refuerza con esta madera suave, de densidad moderada y muy resistente.\
\
'Es la madera perfecta —sí, perfecta— para sacar de combate a una musaraña enorme y molesta sin hacerle daño de verdad. Los Elfos no gustan de herir criaturas, ¿ves? Bue...o... supongo que las musarañas nos tientan a usar más fuerza que la mayoría de los animales salvajes, pero hemos encontrado un justo compromiso.\
\
'Las ramas de cerezo crecen alrededor de grupos de árboles en los pastizales junto al camino hacia Duillond. Estoy seguro de que habrá muchas ramas en el suelo para reponer la provisión de hoy.'","Has recogido una rama de madera de cerezo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El zapatero del evento de Aplastamiento de Musarañas necesita más madera para las suelas especiales de las botas.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el festival actual. </rgb>"},
[340]={"Habla con Radagast","'Ah here it is! This is a special food I have crafted to calm frenzied animals. I want you to take these and feed them to specific creatures. The food's calming effects should make any animal befriend you. With their friendship, the animals shall return to Rhosgobel with you where I will tend to them and keep them safe in the dark times ahead.\
\
'This food can take a while to make, but I will work on another batch for you.'","Radagast can be found in Rhosgobel.\
\
Wait for Radagast to find what he is looking for.","Radagast can be found in Rhosgobel.\
\
You should talk to Radagast.","Radagast pulls out a small pouch from his robes","'I have seen much conflict the realm over. It pains me to see innocent beasts caught in the battles of monsters and Men. If I do not take action, there will be no animals to tend to once the fog of conflict has lifted.\
\
'${PLAYER}, you have shown me a great will to explore and preserve the beauty of these lands. I have a gift for you.... Hold on just a minute....'","Radagast the Brown invited you to his hidden dwelling in the southern end of Mirkwood to ask for your help in a vast undertaking.","Wait for Radagast","A Gift From Radagast"},
[341]={"Look for a young rider named Sithgar in Ost Rimmon, in the Beacon Hills.","Return to Guthláf","When you return to the Rohirrim bivouac, you should let Guthláf know that you found Sithgar in Ost Rimmon and helped him to ready his horse for travel again.","A Gift Gone Astray","Help Sithgar","Look for Sithgar","You should help Sithgar recover his horse and return to his Éored.","In the Rohirrim bivouac, Guthláf asks you to look for a young rider named Sithgar who fell behind.","'Ah, there you are! I have seen Sithgar returned with my own eyes. And I understand we have you to thank. My heart is glad for what you have done, friend.'","'I feel a responsibility for the young man, as I gave him the un-broken horse that ran away. If you find him in Ost Rimmon, I would ask that you do what you can for him.'","'You found Sithgar? And he is well? As well as a lad may be who has lost his horse, at any rate. Ha ha! I hope he is able to return before we move on. We cannot tarry for him, I am afraid.'","'Old Guthláf sent you? Ha! Well, he was not wrong to be worried and I must confess, I am in need of some help.'","'We rode hard through the land to our west, and fast. Misfortune may fly swift as an arrow though, and in the briefest of rests, a young rider of my Éored, Sithgar by name, had his horse run off on him and was forced to stay behind.\
\
'The thought pains me some. The horse he rode was not fully broken in, and, I confess, I provided her to him. He had arrived at the muster with his late father's steed, half lame and half blind, and in all honesty, I thought he would have bonded with his new steed by now. I thought he would have caught back up with us, as well, and that has not happened either!\
\
'If you are heading that way, would you look for the young man? He will be in Ost Rimmon, most likely, unless he is still out hunting for his horse.'"},
[342]={"'¿Ese... té huele a arándanos? Eso fue muy... dulce por parte de Celandine, y muy bueno de tu parte traerle los ingredientes. Lamento decirlo, pero no puedo beberlo ahora. No... no me siento lo bastante bien en este momento.\
\
'Fingiré beberlo. Debes decirle a Celandine que disfruté su té. Por favor... ¡no le digas que su amabilidad fue desperdiciada en mí!'","Amdir solo finge beber el té; se ve aún más pálido que antes...","'¿No huele delicioso este té de arándanos? Aún me recuerda a mi Abuela, que me hacía esto cuando estaba indispuesta, aunque hace mucho que mi Abuela ya no está.\
\
'Fuiste tan amable al recoger esas bayas silvestres para mí, ¡así que no me quedaré con todo el crédito! ¿Por qué no llevas esta buena infusión a Amdir para que pueda agradecerte él mismo?\
\
'¡Asegúrate de que se lo beba todo!'","Amdir está sentado al otro lado del camino de Celandine, en el centro de Archet.\
\
Debes llevar a Amdir el té restaurador de arándanos de Celandine para ayudarlo a recuperar su fuerza y su claridad.","Asegúrate de que Amdir beba el té de arándanos","'¿Ese té lo animó? ¡Sabía que lo haría! El té de arándanos siempre me levanta el ánimo, y sé que sería especialmente dulce si viniera de parte de los dos, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Sé que Amdir estará de pie pronto — ¡es tan valiente!'","Esta misión no puede completarse fuera de la introducción.","Un Regalo para Amdir","Regresa con Celandine y miente por el bien de Amdir","Celandine preparó un té medicinal de arándanos para Amdir, con la esperanza de que lo fortaleciera y animara contra la sombra que ha caído sobre él.","'¡Rápido ahora! No debes dejar que el té se enfríe. ¡Espero que haga que Amdir se sienta mejor!'","Celandine está al otro lado del camino de Amdir, en el centro de Archet.\
\
Debes regresar con Celandine y mentir en nombre de Amdir. Él no bebió su té, pero no quiere que ella se desilusione...","'...'\
\
Los ojos de Amdir están ahora cerrados, y ya no hace esfuerzo por hablar en este momento. Su rostro está tan pálido como el hielo."},
[343]={"'Mi actuación debió ser muy convincente. ¡Demasiado convincente, creo!'","'¿Tienes algo para mí?'","Un Obsequio para la Doncella Elfa","'Listo, he terminado el collar, ${PLAYER}. Si se lo llevas a Narlinn, ¡te estaré en deuda! La encontrarás en Thorenhad, el campamento de los hijos de Elrond, al noroeste de aquí, al norte de las guaridas de osos.\
\
'Narlinn cree que la doncella por la que he estado suspirando es Faimir de Rivendel. Es encantadora, y por un tiempo creí amarla, pero mi tiempo aquí en lo salvaje me ha enseñado que Narlinn es quien hace cantar a mi corazón.\
\
'¡Llévale este collar con todo mi afecto! Me quedaré aquí cumpliendo con mis deberes, aunque espero reunirme con Narlinn en paz cuando pasen estos tiempos oscuros contra los que debemos velar.'","'¿Le has entregado el collar a Narlinn?'","'Arrod solía admirarme tanto, pero últimamente ha sido francamente indiferente.'","'Thorenhad está al oeste de aquí, al norte de las guaridas de osos en las Gargantas del Bruinen. ¡Lleva mi collar a Narlinn con todo mi afecto!'","Arrod está en su puesto de vigilancia, en lo alto de las Gargantas del Bruinen, junto a unas antiguas ruinas.\
\
Narlinn ha rechazado el obsequio de Arrod y te ha pedido que se lo devuelvas.","Lleva el collar de Arrod a Narlinn","'¡He convencido tan completamente a Narlinn de que no es la doncella por la que suspiraba! ¡Ay!'","'¡Nunca antes me habían acusado de ser demasiado sutil, ${PLAYER}! ¡Qué extraño!'","'Arrod debe estar distraído si no te dejó en claro sus intenciones.'","'¿Qué? ¿Por qué aún tienes el collar, ${PLAYER}? ¡No me digas que Narlinn lo rechazó!\
\
'Ya veo... ¡he sido víctima de mis propias sutilezas! Mi actuación fue tan convincente que Narlinn cree que Faimir es realmente la doncella Elfa por la que he estado suspirando.\
\
'Tengo una solución, ${PLAYER}. Mantendré mi vigilancia aquí, siempre alerta, y me reuniré con Narlinn en persona cuando mi deber haya terminado. Entonces le explicaré mis verdaderos sentimientos. No debería haberte dado esta tarea. ¡Esta tarea es para Arrod de Rivendel, y solo para Arrod de Rivendel!'","'Ese collar está muy mal hecho, ${PLAYER}. No lo quiero.\
\
'Estoy segura de que su creador está muy avergonzado de su apresurado trabajo.'","Narlinn está en Thorenhad, el campamento de los hijos de Elrond, en las Gargantas del Bruinen, al norte de las guaridas de osos.\
\
Arrod te ha pedido que entregues el collar a Narlinn, la doncella Elfa que es objeto de su devoción.","'¿Qué? ¿Este collar es de Arrod? Debes estar confundido... él solo está interesado en Faimir de Rivendel. ¡Él mismo me lo ha dicho!\
\
'Tienes buenas intenciones, ${PLAYER}, pero no puedo aceptar esto. Devuélvelo a Arrod y dile que no comprendiste bien su encargo.\
\
'No quiero oír más sobre esto. No deseo avergonzarte ni a ti ni a Arrod. ¡Has traído este hermoso collar a la doncella Elfa equivocada!'","Devuelve el collar de Arrod a Arrod","Arrod ha confeccionado un collar para la doncella Elfa Narlinn, de quien está enamorado.","'¿Le has llevado el collar de Arrod a Faimir?'","'No entiendo por qué Arrod ya no me presta tanta atención como antes.'","'¿Narlinn? ¿Por qué me preguntas por ella? Creo que está en Thorenhad con Elladan y Elrohir.\
\
'Mi Arrod también está allí, creo. Ha sido tan atento y admirador conmigo últimamente, que ha despertado la envidia de las otras doncellas.'","'Arrod está explorando las Gargantas del Bruinen, y me preocupa que, al pensar siempre en Faimir, no preste atención ni a su seguridad ni a su deber. Devuélvele este collar, pues ha habido un error. No era su intención que me lo trajeras a mí.'","'Últimamente, Arrod se ha vuelto distante. ¡No puedo imaginar por qué!'"},
[344]={"Return to Gôbezhir","You have invited Mêshaget to join you and Gôbezhir, so that the two of you can present him with a gift.","You went with Gôbezhir to present his masterwork axe to Mêshaget.","Complete Instance: A Gift for the Future","Completed Instance: A Gift for the Future","Gôbezhir has asked you to talk to Mêshaget and see if he will join the two of you. Mêshaget is in the courtyard of Jiret-menêsh.","'Well, ${PLAYER}, it seems that Mêshaget likes it! Thank you again for the role you played in its making. Semakéfë is a fitting name. I cannot say if us being attacked as I gave it to him bodes ill, or if a swift victory after receiving it bodes well! What we can be certain of is that Mêshaget will carve his own path in life, no matter what Châmelek Gêta says.'\
\
The old dwarf laughs and claps you on the arm before bidding you farewell.","'Now that I have the wood for the haft, I will be finished swiftly. A weapon such as this has no price, so I have decided to give it as a gift to young Mêshaget. Actually, I think it should be a gift from both of us! Without your help, I would still be standing here, lamenting that I don't have the needed materials.\
\
'Would you speak with him and invite him to join us? I think he may be found in the courtyard.'","A Gift for the Future","Gôbezhir Firmhand, master smith of Jiret-menêsh, has decided to give his life's masterwork as a gift to Mêshaget.","'He is on his way? Great! Come, I will show you the axe while we wait for him.'","'${PLAYER}, what can I do for you, my friend?'\
\
You invite Mêshaget to join you and Gôbezhir Firmhand. Gôbezhir has a gift he would like to give him.\
\
'A gift? That is unexpected! It would be rude to deny someone the opportunity to practice generosity, don't you think?'\
\
Mêshaget chuckles and looks excited to know what it is.\
\
'You go ahead and tell him I will be there shortly.'","You have invited Mêshaget to join you and Gôbezhir, so that the two of you can present him with a gift. Gôbezhir is in the crafting area of Jiret-menêsh.","Talk to Mêshaget","Talk to Gôbezhir"},
[345]={"Eigár can be found in Lake-town.\
\
You should talk to Eigár.","'What do you want? A small amount of wood? Not worth my time. You can go take something from the scrap pile. Be quick about it.'","Talk to Mervárth","Collect calamine ore","Mervárth would like to give a gift to Dagrun as congratulations for her new appointment. Help Mervárth gather the supplies needed.","Collect copper ore","Try to find an appropriate piece of wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Mervárth needs some wood? Why? No, nevermind, I don't want to know what he's up to. Unfortunately, we are out of wood. You're going to have to go get some from the forester north of here. Good luck, he can be a bit prickly.'","Talk to Víthog the Forester","Collected calamine ore","Málmi the Ore Trader can be found in Erebor.\
\
You should talk to Málmi.","Copper and calamine ore can be found nearby in Erebor.\
\
You should collect a chunk of copper ore and a chunk of calamine ore.","Dagrun can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town.\
\
You should talk to Dagrun.","A Gift for the Master","'Hail, friend. Here for a brass ingot? I can smelt you one right away. I will need you to choose one ore of copper and one of calamine from the table here.'","The scrap pile can be found near the forester's house.\
\
You should search the scrap pile for a good piece of wood.","Talk to Málmi","Málmi the Ore Trader can be found in Erebor, in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You should talk to Málmi.","'Mervárth stopped by earlier to congratulate me on my new position and asked for your help if you can spare a moment. He should be in the Trade Commission Headquarters if you would like to go speak with him.'","Rísta can be found in Dale.\
\
You should talk to Rísta.","Mervárth can be found in the Trade Commission Headquarters in Lake-town.\
\
You should talk to Mervárth.","This piece of wood will work!","Talk to Rísta","Talk to Dagrun","'${PLAYER}! Great to see you, as always! Listen, I want to get Dagrun something special in honour of becoming Master. If you're willing to do the work for me, we can say it's a gift from both of us! Keeping her on my good side is imperative to my success!\
\
'So, I have an artisan lined up for the job. Her name is Rísta and her shop is in Dale. You will need to bring her a brass ingot from Erebor and some wood for carving. Not a huge piece, about so big?'\
\
He holds his hands about three feet apart to show the size.\
\
'Try the docks here in Lake-town for that. Please hurry, I'm so excited to see the look on Dagrun's face!'","You realize that Mervárth forgot to mention what the gift is","'What is this? A gift from Mervárth?'\
\
You hand her the statuette. She looks confused until she reads the engraving and then bursts out laughing.\
\
'Mervárth! He likes to give me a hard time for being humble. \\qYou're Master of all of Lake-town now, throw your weight around a little!\\q This will go on my desk as a reminder of my station and a reminder that I should do something nice for Mervárth one of these days. Thank you for your part in this, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Málmi in Erebor, in the Hall Under the Mountain","Málmi takes the ore from you. You watch as he swiftly transforms the rocks into a bar of pure metal. He hands it to you.\
\
'Since this is part of a gift for the Master of Lake-town, I will not charge you for my services. Give her my regards and tell her Lake-town has friends in Erebor!'","Collected copper ore","'Ah, you must be Mervárth's friend. I just need the wood and brass to get started.'\
\
You hand her the brass ingot and the piece of wood, and then watch as she begins to transform them. The wood is carved into a likeness of Dagrun, in a particularly heroic pose, and the brass hammered into a base. To finish the piece, Rísta engraves the base to say \\qThe Greatest Master.\\q She sees your reaction as you read it and chuckles.\
\
'That was what Mervárth asked to be engraved! I believe that's just the kind of relationship he has with Dagrun. It is done and already paid for in full. You may take it to Dagrun.'","Víthog the Forester can be found in the Dale-lands west of Lake-town.\
\
You should talk to Víthog the Forester.","Talk to Eigár the Dock-worker"},
[346]={"Habla con Ulfar","'¡Que un enano pudiera soportar la presencia de un troll es impensable! No importa... ahora está muerto, y Olwir también.'","'Gracias por tu ayuda, ${RACE}. No sé qué travesura tramaban los Duramano, pero seguro que no era nada bueno!'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir?\
\
Asegúrate de que tu grupo también esté preparado, porque sin duda necesitaremos su ayuda para matar a ese troll de piedra.'","Ulfar ha regresado a Ojo de Aguja.\
\
Como has tenido éxito en tu misión, deberías volver con Ulfar para contarle lo sucedido.","'¿Quién hubiera pensado que el robo de una vaca destaparía un complot como este? ¡Debemos frustrar los planes de Olwir y, si ha capturado un troll, debemos matarlo!\
\
Por suerte, he averiguado dónde acampan Olwir y sus enanos. Se encuentran al norte del Pantano de los Juncos. Sin embargo, entrar en el campamento y matar a ese troll de piedra, si es que tienen uno, no será fácil. Necesitaremos ayuda.\
\
Reúne un grupo de guerreros —si es que puedes encontrar alguno en estas tierras— y vuelve aquí. Asegúrate de reunir guerreros robustos, porque la batalla que nos espera no será fácil.'","'Bien hecho. Sin duda mereces esta recompensa.'","'¡Esos Duramano son unos ladrones y traicioneros, pero me cuesta creer que incluso ellos dejarían vivir a un troll!'","Un regalo para el norte","El campamento de Olwir está en las zonas norte del Pantano de los Juncos.\
\
Ulfar ha decidido que el plan de Olwir debe ser detenido y te ha pedido que reúnas un grupo de guerreros para acompañarlo al campamento. Una vez allí, planea infiltrarse y matar a cualquier troll de piedra que los enanos de Olwir hayan capturado.","Por las órdenes que encontraste, Ulfar ha sabido que Olwir planea capturar un troll de piedra que merodea por el Pantano de los Juncos y entregarlo como regalo a los Duramano del norte. La vaca que robó a Filibert era el cebo para atrapar a la criatura."},
[347]={"Enfrenta a Olwir","Acércate a la puerta","Debes encontrar una manera de entrar en el campamento enano. Tal vez desafiar a los enanos a un combate los haga abrir la puerta.","'¡Bien hecho! Me impacienté esperando y vine a ver cómo te estaba yendo, pero parece que lo hiciste bien sin mí. Ese troll de piedra está muerto, y parece que Olwir también. Pagó un alto precio por su crimen, robar una vaca a Filibert. Con él fuera del camino, estos enanos no deberían molestar mucho más al Pantano de los Juncos.\
\
'Has hecho un buen trabajo hoy, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Tienes mi agradecimiento. ¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir?'","Espera a los Duramano","Has viajado a las afueras del campamento enano en el Pantano de los Juncos. Allí esperas poner fin al plan del enano Olwir de capturar un troll de piedra y dárselo como regalo al enano Skorgrím en el norte.","Desafía a los Duramano frente a la puerta","Los Duramano han abierto la puerta para responder a tu desafío. Deberías hacer algo que inicie el combate.","Has encontrado a Olwir y derrotado a los guardias que lo protegían. ¡Tiene un troll de piedra enjaulado! Deberías enfrentarte a Olwir.","Has encontrado a Olwir, y tiene un troll de piedra enjaulado. Deberías derrotar a los Duramano que lo protegen.","<rgb=#FF0000>Abofetear</rgb> al rastreador Duramano","Debes encontrar una manera de entrar en el campamento enano.","Los Duramano han abierto la puerta para responder a tu desafío.","Busca en el campamento a Olwir","Has encontrado a Olwir, junto con un troll enjaulado.","Has derrotado a los enanos que custodiaban la puerta. Deberías avanzar hacia el campamento en busca de Olwir o de un troll de piedra.","Derrota a los guardias de Olwir","<rgb=#FF0000>Desafía</rgb> a los Duramano frente a la puerta","Eh... está bien, ¡derrota al troll de piedra!","Parece que Olwir ya no es un problema, pero ahora tienes uno más grande: un troll de piedra que debe ser derrotado.","Derrota al troll de piedra","Un regalo para el norte"},
[348]={"The steed is packed and ready for its journey to Edoras","Collect Fastred's pendant","'Thank you for your continued aid, ${PLAYER}. We have to maintain our independence from the throne. I am a loyal Reeve, but the King's actions as of late are foolhardy. We should strike at our foes while we can, lest they unite and overwhelm all of Rohan.'","Talk to Fastred","Gather freshly-harvested grain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Having gathered your portion of Fastred's gift, you should load it onto the horse he mentioned earlier. \
\
The horse can be found outside the mead-hall.","Fastred wants to send a gift westward to distract Edoras from his blatant disregard for the King's decree. Grain, delicious cuisine of the Sutcrofts, and a pendant are the items he wishes to send.","Load Fastred's steed with the gifts","Collected Fastred's pendant","Gather well-prepared food (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gathered well-prepared food (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Food can be found in the Mead Hall and kitchens throughout Snowbourn. Grain can be found in the fields directly outside town. Fastred's pendant can be found in his home.\
\
Fastred wants you to help him prepare a gift of sorts to be sent to Edoras. He wishes for you to gather some portions of the gift while he handles his own preparations.","Gathered freshly-harvested grain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${PLAYER}, I require your aid on a private matter.\
\
'Edoras has decreed that we abandon our homeland and allow the Orcs to run rampant. Such a thing will never be abided by myself or my men.\
\
'Thus, I have decided to send a gift to Edoras. A gift of dissent... a gift of distraction. May it please the King so greatly that Snowbourn falls beneath notice.\
\
'I will defend this town to my last, and no Orc in my sight will ever escape. If that is treason, so be it, I will do what is right.'\
\
'Gather for me grain from the fields, prepared food from the kitchen, and a pendant from my home. Once gathered, pack them onto a steed outside the mead-hall. We will speak again soon.'","Fastred can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.","A Gift for the Westemnet"},
[349]={"'This is just enough! You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I wonder what the Dark Lord would think if he knew his own trolls were of great aid to the healers of Gondor!'","Sun-touched Morgul-trolls can be found in the hills surrounding Henneth Annûn.\
\
Ereblen has asked you to return to the sun-touched Morgul-trolls you found previously and scrape patches of moss from them.","'Do you remember the trolls we found in the wilds of Ithilien, ${PLAYER}? The ones that had turned to stone?\
\
'Some of our company have since returned to the sites where you discovered them, and they all appear to have encouraged the growth of a peculiar moss upon them! We harvested a small amount and were able to extract it into a healing salve.\
\
'It is unlike any of the mosses we have encountered in Ithilien... could a troll from the Dead City truly give way to something so helpful to my kinsmen?\
\
'Seek out the sun-touched trolls, my friend, and scrape the moss from them. Do not harvest it all - for I am certain we shall have further use of it in the coming days.'","Scrape moss from sun-touched Morgul-trolls in North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deliver the moss to Ereblen in Henneth Annûn","The trolls of Mordor and Minas Morgul that turned to stone in North Ithilien now serve as an unexpected source of a valuable moss.","A Gift from the Enemy","Scraped moss from sun-touched Morgul-trolls in North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ereblen can be found in Henneth Annûn.\
\
You have gathered a suitable amount of moss from the sun-touched trolls and should now deliver it to Ereblen."},
[351]={"'This cheese is a blessing. Thank you for bringing it so far.'","Speak with Majâryan in the Court of Larinâsta","'These are perfect, thank you, and thank Majâryan for me.'","'Good shéra is a gift worth spreading, is it not? Not good shéra, what am I saying? The best shéra!\
\
'Take some shéra for yourself! It's only right for you to share in it!'","Deliver the cheese baskets to each of three customers in Zajâna.","Deliver the second cheese basket to the second customer","'Who has the best shéra in Zajâna? It's Majâryan, of course, of course!\
\
'But who has the time to spread the gift of cheese? Not Majâryan! She has to make the cheese. She has to sell the cheese! You can help Majâryan, can't you?\
\
'Deliver these baskets of cheese to our needy customers. Do it quickly, or the cheese will melt in this heat! I've put the addresses on the baskets. You will help Majâryan, won't you?'","Return to the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna and speak with Majâryan.","Pick up the cheese deliveries from Majâryan's table (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pick up the cheese deliveries from Majâryan's table in the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna.","Picked up the cheese deliveries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deliver the third cheese basket to the third customer","Deliver the first cheese basket to the first customer","Majâryan, a merchant in the Court of Larinâsta, has asked you to help with her cheese deliveries to local customers.","A Gift of Cheese","'Perfect timing. I was about to start cooking. Thank you for this.'"},
[352]={"'Have you been to see Menassiel yet? She can be found near Cerin Amroth in Lothlórien.'","'¡Has vuelto! Me alegro. Déjame ver qué nos ha dado Menassiel.'","Lleva el esqueje de mallorn a Nífdir","'Menassiel stands near Cerin Amroth, in Lothlórien. You should go to her and see if she will help us.'","'You indeed tell a sad story, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for offering to return to that dangerous place for so generous a deed. Not many outsiders love the trees as much as we Galadhrim do.\
\
'I only hope that I do not send this child to its death in that forsaken swamp. Please see that it is cared for, if you pass it by. It has some power to spread its light and dispel the cruel corruptions of Mirkwood, but...nay, I will trust to hope. The power of Galadriel is in the very sap of this young one.\
\
'Return to the glade if you dare, ${PLAYER}, and plant this seed. See that none disturb it.'","Nífdir is at his camp in the Drownholt, west of the Malledhrim outpost of Estolad Mernael.\
\
You should return to Nífdir to show him the seedling donated by Menassiel.","'Bring this little seedling to Nífdir, mellon. It is my gift to the aged trees who live in despair. I hope it brings them light, as the mallorns have done for us also.'","Menassiel can be found at Cerin Amroth in Lothlórien.\
\
You should speak with Menassiel and see if she will gift the Huorns of Mirkwood with a young mallorn, a light to dispel the shadows upon their wretched existence.","'I can think of one small gesture that might do some good. The mallorn trees of Lothlórien, thriving under the power of Galadriel and the care of the Galadhrim, inspire all who harbour love for the wilderness. The mallorns will resist stain as long as the Elves are here to tend them.\
\
'I want you to go to my friend Menassiel in Lothlórien, at Cerin Amroth. Surely her heart will be moved by your tale, as mine is. I would like to plant a mallorn sapling here, in this glade. It will give hope to the Huorns. I do not think it will fully quell their wrath, but it has been long since they have seen any light. They deserve a glimmer of hope, for someday the shadows of Dol Guldur will trouble this place no more.\
\
'Go to Menassiel now, ${PLAYER}, and see if she will help you.'","The Elf Nífdir is moved by the unhappy state of the Mirk-huorns and the tale of their slow loss of hope. He wishes to do something to alleviate their sadness and despair.","Un regalo de oro","Habla con Menassiel en Cerin Amroth"},
[353]={"Isengard has moved some advanced siege-craft south to attack Helm's Deep. You should count the different types of siege-craft to learn more of the enemy.","A Gift of War","Loosen wheels on the siege-engines (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Saruman's interest in war machinery has grown of late, for he now employs many siege-weapons for his intended attack upon Helm's Deep.\
\
Hopefully you can help the defenders of Helm's Deep with your knowledge of the enemy.","Completado","Loosened a wheel (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Siege-craft and war machines can be found in Shatorthum.\
\
You should examine the different types of weapons to learn of the technology that Isengard harbours."},
[354]={"A Gift of Warmth in Winter","'Hail, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for this gift... but tell me: is this from Noriel? How does she fare? What can you tell me about her? Do you think she would agree to see me again?'","'Here are the hides that you gathered -- and now they should go to their proper home: the Rohirrim from Stangard. They have made camp at the bottom of the wood along the river before they make the remainder of their journey home.\
\
'You should bring them this gift from the Elves before they depart for good, for this will be our last chance to make contact with the trespassers.'","Renfaer has asked you to deliver Noriel's gift for the departing Rohirrim of Stangard.","Bring the gift of hides to Wynmar at his new camp","Wynmar and his men are at their new temporary camp on the southern river-bank of Thinglad.\
\
You should bring the hides to Wynmar as a final parting gift, a token of good will from the Elves."},
[355]={"Sharûla smiles confidently at you, but her eyes are cold","'Do not convey any discontent to any... interested parties; I am too happy to express my gratitude. Hármelak will find that I am most accommodating! Examine my ledger and these papers at your leisure!'","'We should not wish to disturb the honourable Sharûla overlong. She keeps a manor in the north-eastern area of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens. Speak with her there and consult her ledger. She will likely be expecting someone to call upon her on my behalf, for it is the regular time for her tithe to come due.'","Sharûla stands outside her manor in the north-east reaches of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens.","Hármelak is inside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, waiting for your report of Sharûla's accounts.","Sharûla has invited you to study the documents and ledgers she has provided for Hármelak's perusal.","Nothing in the contents of these papers seem out-of-place or suspect","Hármelak has kept a close watch upon Khôltekh's dealings in Umbar-môkh, and she wants to ensure that his power does not threaten her own.","Talk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja","'I thank you for your doubtless precious time, as I have little of my own. Can I count upon you to speak favourably of my situation to Hármelak?'","Talk to Sharûla outside her manor in the Upper Ward","Examine Sharûla's papers","'A wealthy noble free of suspicious secrets is a suspicious sort indeed. Sharûla is hiding something. I am certain of it.'","'And thus the one who gave aid to my esteemed friend Khôltekh... was you after all, ${PLAYER}. Many are my eyes and ears throughout Umbar Baharbêl and beneath the surface in Umbar-môkh, and they relayed to me the aid you provided him in the matter of Sêkhta. It was a messy business, I am told. He would be a dangerous foe, would he not?\
\
'But so it is with all of us within the Kindred, and it is important that any who think to oppose us realize it. There is a noblewoman of the city on whom I have kept watch, but of late she has had fewer coins with which to support the Kindred. Her name is Sharûla, and she keeps a manor in the north-eastern area of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens. Speak with her there and consult her ledger. She will likely be expecting someone to call upon her on my behalf, for it is the regular time for her tithe to come due.'","A Gilded Veneer, Part 1: Sharûla","'I am honoured to welcome an emissary of the Kindred! I expected your arrival, so I have had my servants bring my ledgers and these papers outside for your convenience. You are free to examine them, of course, but I can assure you that the Golden Queen will find all is in order, and my expected tithe is the correct amount. If anything I am giving more to the Kindred than others of my station... but it is my pleasure and I am not given to complain!'","'As she requires. Tell Hármelak that Sharûla is her patient servant, as always.'","Sharûla's manor can be found in the north-east reaches of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens.","The ledger records Sharûla's many business transactions, and seems above-board","Examine Sharûla's ledgers"},
[356]={"'I have ears and eyes everywhere. Word has come to me that Sharûla may have some connexion with smuggling activity in Tâkhdar. If you engage with some of those who participate in these unlawful activities, you may recover some clear records that will connect Sharûla with their smuggling operation. This will make it easier for us to move against her, ${PLAYER}.'","'We shall appear content, for a time. Then we will return to Sharûla and uncover her secrets.\
\
'Word has come to me that she may have some connexion with smuggling activity in Tâkhdar, the Cellars of Umbar-môkh. If you engage with some of those who participate in these unlawful activities, you may recover some clear records that will connect Sharûla with their smuggling operation. This will make it easier for us to move against her, ${PLAYER}.'","'Yes? Speak.'\
\
Hármelak studies the confused records you recovered from the smugglers in Tâkhdar. She looks up at you with disappointment on her face.\
\
'Nothing here connects obviously-enough to Sharûla, but this does not change the fact that she is keeping something from us. It simply means that she is better at hiding it than she appeared.'","A Gilded Veneer, Part 2: Confused Bookkeeping","Hármelak is inside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, waiting for you to return from Tâkhdar with proof of Sharûla's misdeeds.","Smugglers within Tâkhdar, the Cellars of Umbar-môkh beneath the city, may possess records that will shed light upon Sharûla's misdeeds.","Clear records collected (0/10), confused records collected (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect clear and straightforward records from smugglers within Tâkhdar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hármelak has asked you to procure clear records from the smugglers of Tâkhdar that might shed some light on Sharûla's misdeeds.","Bring the confused records to Hármelak in Dâr Laja"},
[357]={"'Perhaps, should you darken her door unannounced, any enshrouded secrets might come to light.\
\
'Earlier she was expecting an emissary from me, but now she is not. Let us see what Sharûla does when you make an unheralded call upon her, ${PLAYER}. She will not be prepared for you, and may let something slip.'","Return to Sharûla's manor unannounced and unheralded","'Forgive this servant's confusion, but the tithe is not yet ready. Is Lady Hármelak upset with us? Oh no, I hope we have done nothing to draw her ire!'\
\
You assure Zakhâz that as long as he speaks honestly, and has nothing to hide from the Kindred, that Hármelak will treat him and the lady of the house fairly.\
\
'I... I... I...' he says, clearly grappling with some unsaid worry.","'We must take care of this matter. Return to Sharûla's manor in the north-eastern corner of the Upper Ward, just west of the Tor-gardens. Let us see if she betrays her secret when you make an unheralded call upon her, ${PLAYER}.'","A Gilded Veneer, Part 3: An Unexpected Call","Zakhâz appears to be struggling with a difficult decision.","Wait for Zakhâz to make his decision","Hármelak has not given up on proving that Sharûla has committed some misdeed, and the Golden Queen wants your continued aid in service of that aim.","Hármelak wants you to return to Sharûla's manor in the north-eastern Upper Ward, on the edge of the Tor-gardens... but this time she wants you to return unannounced.","Talk to Zakhâz outside Sharûla's manor","'I beg your kind discretion, lest my lady's ire affect my stewardship. But I cannot remain silent any longer!\
\
'I fear that Lady Sharûla desires to inflict harm upon the people of the city and upon the Kindred of the Coins!'","Sharûla's steward, Zakhâz, guards the entrance to her manor in the Upper Ward.","Sharûla is nowhere to be seen, but her Steward guards the door inside"},
[358]={"Inside the lockbox you find papers to suggest Sharûla has funded Azagath's ventures","A lockbox in the middle of Sharûla's secret residence may contain evidence of her support for Azagath Sea-shadow.","Defeated Azagath loyalists (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","According to Zakhâz, the entrance to Sharûla's second, secret residence is located in Tâkhdar, south of the stairs to Dâr Laja.","'Once again, I beg your kind discretion, lest my lady's ire affect my stewardship. The entrance to her secret residence is in Tâkhdar, south of the Meeting-hall stairs. Please, my friend... please show mercy to my lady. She has been led astray by the venomous whispers of those who follow Azagath. I know she will repent of her misdeeds.'","Sharûla's secret residence is a hideout for supporters of Azagath Sea-shadow!","Supporters of Azagath Sea-shadow come and go frequently throughout Sharûla's secret residence.","'News of your perilous encounter and Sharûla's treachery fast reached Dâr Laja. It is precisely as I believed it to be: there are treacherous forces arrayed against us and against the city.\
\
'Azagath has fled, but his supporters remain, and they can do us harm. Khôltekh faced his own opponent, but Sêkhta was a single foe. My opponents endanger all of Umbar Baharbêl, ${PLAYER}. You will help me root them out and end their villainy.\
\
'But I must prepare, and make my plans. When next you return to me we will learn the extent of Sharûla's traitorous reach. She may not be the only member of her class whose wealth is a mask for the corruption beneath, a gilded veneer on something distasteful. Until then, keep watch. The shadow cast by Azagath has grown long in the city, and beneath it.'","Bring the incriminating documents to Hármelak in Dâr Laja","Find Sharûla's second, secret residence in Tâkhdar","Zakhâz pauses for a long moment, steeling his resolve.\
\
'You know that Azagath Sea-shadow has apparently revealed himself a traitor to the Kindred? I believe that Lady Sharûla has taken in with a crowd of supporters who desire that he be reinstated to a position of power in the city! She keeps a second, secret residence in Umbar-môkh where she meets with these loyalists and plots to overthrow the remaining members of the Kindred, including Lady Hármelak! I can keep silent no longer!\
\
'The entrance to her secret residence is in Tâkhdar, south of the Meeting-hall stairs. Please, my friend... please show mercy to my lady. She has been led astray by the venomous whispers of those who follow Azagath. I know she will repent of her misdeeds.'","A Gilded Veneer, Part 4: Another Residence","Defeat Azagath loyalists in Sharûla's secret residence (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sharûla's steward Zakhâz told you that the lady of the house possesses a second, secret residence in Umbar-môkh beneath the city.","Hármelak is in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja. She will be pleased to see the documents you recovered that suggest Sharûla has continued funding Azagath's assorted ventures.","Search the lockbox in Sharûla's secret residence"},
[359]={"Hármelak is inside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, waiting for your report that her swords have been delivered.","A Gilded Veneer, Part 5: Safety and Security","Bring the shiny swords to Jaith outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja","Jaith nods in recognition.","Concerned about the possibility that others among the residents of Umbar Baharbêl might seek to assist Azagath Sea-shadow, Hármelak wants her guards to be equipped with better weapons.","'You must not delay. Go now to the Swain's Guild-hall and retrieve the swords I have ordered. Once you have them, give them to Jaith outside Dâr Laja and he will distribute them among my guards.'","Collected shiny swords for Hármelak (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hármelak's order of fresh swords for her personal guardsmen is ready to be picked up inside the Swain's Guild-hall.","Talk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja","Collect Hármelak's order of shiny swords from the Swain's Guild-hall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The corruption might run deep, but we shall remain composed for the public. We know that Sharûla met with supporters of Azagath in her secret residence beneath the city, and funded some of the Sea-shadow's dealings; perhaps it was her wealth that enabled him to escape the Kindred's justice, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I did not remain idle during these past few days. If we are to remain safe here in the Meeting-hall, I need my guardsmen to have the finest equipment made for them. To that end, I ordered four swords to be made, and they are ready to be collected.\
\
'Go now to the Swain's Guild-hall and retrieve these swords. Once you have them, give them to Jaith outside Dâr Laja and he will distribute them among my guards.'","Jaith appraises the collection of shiny swords you have brought.\
\
'These swords seem well-made, but are they really any better than the ones already wielded by Lady Hármelak's personal guardsmen? The only difference I can see is that these are much shinier.'","Jaith stands guard outside the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja. He is waiting to receive the swords Hármelak ordered from the Swain's Guild-hall.","'What is it? You have collected the swords I commissioned from the Swain's Guild-hall? Good. It was a costly order, but the price of security is a price I will not balk at... not when treachery has taken root in my city, and beneath it.'"},
[360]={"'And at what cost to me do these kind favours arrive?'","'No, no, no, nothing needed, nothing desired, nothing hoped! I simply wish to not draw the attention of the Golden Queen, lest she take offence at me and send me to the gaols, or worse!'","'It is our duty to care for the people of Umbar. If we are to fulfil this duty, we must learn if Sharûla's corruption extends to the merchants of Kheb Hanût.'","A Gilded Veneer, Part 6: Inquiries at Kheb Hanût","Talk to Lashêm in Kheb Hanût","'If ever I needed a favour from Hármelak Golden-hand, have her douse me in water and face my body towards the sea. On that day it will be already too late for me!'","Talk to Okhmath in Kheb Hanût","Hármelak has heard there might be associates of Sharûla in the market of Kheb Hanût beneath the city, and she wants you to root them out.","Hármelak asked you to speak to merchants in the market of Kheb Hanût in north-west Tâkhdar and learn if any of them share Sharûla's loyalty to Azagath.","Talk to Dayêri in Kheb Hanût","Talk to Nagamûn in Kheb Hanût","'I am honoured to be thought of at all by a member of the Kindred! Just a few days ago I had the pleasure of speaking with one of the Temámir, a friend of Kinsman Khôltekh himself! And now to be greeted politely by an emissary of Hármelak, the Golden Queen? These are remarkable days indeed!'","'And at what cost to me do these kind favours arrive? The Golden Queen never does anything for free, or so it is said.\
\
'I will not be in her debt. Not for any sum!'","'No, no, no, nothing needed, nothing desired, nothing hoped!'","'If ever I needed a favour from Hármelak Golden-hand, have her douse me in water and face my body towards the sea.'","'Foes of the city will be dealt with... harshly. Now that my guardsmen are better-equipped, they will apprehend Sharûla and bring her to me. No, you do not need to wait, ${PLAYER}. I have something else for you.\
\
'I believe some of Sharûla's associates are vendors in the market of Kheb Hanût, beneath the city. Speak to these merchants and determine their loyalties, if you can. It may be they will let something slip that will connect them to Sharûla or to Azagath.\
\
'If anyone asks you to lend your aid to them, I suggest that you do. They may reveal their true hearts to you in a moment of gratitude.'"},
[361]={"Defeat smugglers operating in Tâkhdar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lashêm is waiting for you to deliver his misplaced parcels to him at Kheb Hanût, in Tâkhdar.","Lashêm smiles broadly as you approach.\
\
'You recovered my parcels! I thank you, friend. The dried squid contained within will bring me a fair profit, and I will raise a toast to the Golden Queen when I have a moment to do so.'","Recovered Lashêm's misplaced parcels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'In times of unrest, one must rely on healthy trade. Kinswoman Hármelak must know this as well, for she is the most wealthy merchant in all these lands, is she not?\
\
'I have become modestly successful in the trade of dried squid, a staple of the Umbari diet, but recently some of my parcels have been misplaced. Well, I say \\qmisplaced,\\q but in truth they have been stolen and carried into Sâl Bajat. The smugglers nearby must believe they can use my goods to great profit, which has left me in a predicament.\
\
'Will you help me deal with these villains and recover my misplaced parcels? I would not trouble the Lady Hármelak with this personally, of course, but you are here, after all...'","Bring the misplaced parcels to Lashêm in Kheb Hanût","The merchant Lashêm has a request to make of you concerning some of his parcels that were \\qmisplaced.\\q","Lashêm's parcels were \\qmisplaced\\q by a number of smugglers operating out of Sâl Bajat, and he needs you to recover them and teach the miscreants he will not be intimidated.","Recover Lashêm's misplaced parcels in Sâl Bajat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'In times of unrest, one must rely on healthy trade. Will you help me deal with those smugglers and recover my misplaced parcels? I would not trouble the Lady Hármelak with this personally, of course, but you are here, after all...'","A Gilded Veneer, Part 7: Lashêm's Request","Defeated smugglers in Tâkhdar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[362]={"Talk to Lashêm in Kheb Hanût","Lashêm stands in disbelief, surrounded by guardsmen.","Lashêm's smile fades as guards arrive and draw their swords on him","'¿Qué es esto?'","'Grab him! This man is wanted for questioning by the Kindred of the Coins, ${PLAYER}. He is a known associate of a traitor to the city who has confessed to their ill deeds; they used their mercantile connexions to transport weapons through Umbar-môkh and into the city above. Their plan was to arm dissidents with these weapons and to ambush Lady Hármelak and the other members of the Kindred!'","The sound of approaching footsteps!","'Poor timing for an ambush indeed, if these whispers of revolt prove true. There are eyes on us now.'\
\
You ask Hármelak why she sent her guardsmen to apprehend the merchant Lashêm, and tell her that he did not seem obviously guilty of the crimes. She stares back at you steadily.\
\
'Did you check the bottom of those crates, ${PLAYER}? Beneath the piles of dried squid, someone could have hidden anything. It is safer this way. After all, he admitted he spoke with a friend of Khôltekh only days ago. What might have been the topic of conversation, do you think?'\
\
You ask Hármelak if Sharûla's confession truly implicated the merchant Lashêm, and she waves a hand.\
\
'You have still not learned the way of things in this land, ${PLAYER}. There is gold here, it is true, but an outward appearance is not always the truth, as Sharûla's misdeeds teach us and I told you before. Sometimes a thing possesses only the veneer of wealth and status, the thinnest gilded surface, and it hides something much uglier.'\
\
As Hármelak bids you farewell, you consider the meaning of her words and think she may be right: there is something ugly at work in Umbar.","Talk to Hármelak's guardsman","Talk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja","'Grab him! Keep him from escaping!'","'On my life and livelihood, I did not know of any plan, any ambush! These are lies, lies! I know nothing about a conspiracy such as this! What villain claims to work with me? I have done nothing of the sort! I love Lady Hármelak, and the Kindred, with all of my heart!'\
\
Lashêm stares at you with wild eyes, desperate to escape the snare in which he is caught.\
\
'Search my parcels! Every one contains dried squid, and nothing else! Someone is seeking to destroy my good reputation! ${PLAYER}, my friend, tell Lady Hármelak I am innocent of this! Please, you must!'","Lashêm stands in stunned silence. Only the words of Hármelak can free him now.","A Gilded Veneer, Part 8: Hármelak's Order","Hármelak is in the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja. Perhaps she will explain to you why Lashêm has been apprehended.","Hármelak moves to maintain order in Umbar-môkh as she does in Umbar Baharbêl above.","The sound of approaching footsteps echoes throughout Kheb Hanût.","Hármelak's guards hold Lashêm at swordpoint."},
[363]={"Al enano Darri lo puedes encontrar en la Vigésimo Primera Sala, en Moria.\
\\Tras haber encontrado varios espejos intactos, debes regresar con Darri e informarle de tu éxito.","Encuentra el cuarto espejo","Has registrado una descripción precisa de este espejo","'Saludos,${CLASS:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} . Soy Darri y provengo de la Montaña Solitaria. Cuesta creer que estemos recorriendo de verdad los antiguos senderos de Khazad-dûm, ¿No te parece? Es algo capaz de encender una llama en el corazón del enano más testarudo.\
\
'Hay una cosa por la que siento un interés especial: los espejos que tal vez hayas visto por la Vigésimo Primera Sala. Creo que hay cuatro y tengo una teoría sobre su utilidad.\
\
'¿Podrías ir y registrar algunos datos sobre ellos, como su rotación, ubicación y demás detalles? Me gustaría estudiar lo que descubras.'","Encuentra el primer espejo","Vuelve con Darri en la Vigésimo Primera Sala","Un destello en la penumbra","Encuentra el segundo espejo","'¿Has encontrado los espejos que te envié a buscar?'","Darri se ha estado preguntando cuál era el propósito de los antiguops espejos de Moria.","Encuentra el tercer espejo","'Buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}! Ahora, déjame echar un vistazo a los registros que has hecho.'","Los cuatro espejos se encuentran en las esquinas de la Vigésimo Primera Sala, en Zelem-melek\
\
Debes encontrar los espejos y registrar su ubicación y rotación."},
[364]={"El espejo situado en las Fundaciones de Piedra es la única fuente de luz pura en estas profundidades estigias. Las cosas malvadas que se arrastran a menudo arruinan su alineación para restaurar la oscuridad.","Un rayo de esperanza","Drafli se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío, en las regiones occidentales de las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Deberías decirle a Drafli que has realineado el espejo.","'Gracias, ${PLAYER}. Estoy seguro de que no pasará mucho tiempo antes de que algo vuelva a jugar con él, pero por ahora, ¿no crees que está un poco más brillante aquí abajo?'","Este espejo se encuentra solo en un terrible pantano de pasajes corruptos, con el hongo extendiéndose a su alrededor. Deberías informar a alguien en el Refugio Sombrío sobre el espejo que encontraste en las profundidades.","Habla con Drafli"},
[365]={"'I hear her words, but I do not yet feel them. Perhaps in time I will.\
\
'Thank you, friend. Your presence has been a constant comfort, and one for which I am quite grateful.'","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír when you are ready to go","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír when you are ready to go.","'Everything is so calm in this moment, I scarcely recognize it. These past few days have been a whirlwind. I have not had a chance to stop the winds and listen, to find peace.\
\
'I would have words with Amalíbi. She said many things in that hall, and I agree with all of them. Many of the things I said I do not agree with, but such is passion. I have many mistakes for which I must atone. Would you accompany me to see her?'","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír.","'Let us go then, to Amalíbi's encampment, to mend what wounds we can.'","A Glimpse of Daylight","A small moment of peace has given Mizâdi time to speak with Amalíbi, to see the consequences of her decisions."},
[369]={"'It cannot be! No, surely you were mistaken. Wargs in Pren Gwydh? Never. You must be mad.\
\
'This... this is terrible. My poor, poor friend. He was a great use to Galtrev, venturing out each morning and returning with goods for the people of this village. But no more....'","'It really is unlike him to be so late, ${PLAYER}. You travel often... is it dangerous beyond the walls of cities?'","Talk to Luned at Galtrev","Search for Leolin","Leolin, a friend of Luned, is late to return from his early morning venture onto Pren Gwydh's road.\
\
You should search for Leolin and encourage him to return to Galtrev to put his friend's fears to rest.","Luned worries about a friend who ventured out into Pren Gwydh to gather supplies for Galtrev. Like many other stout folk during these trying times, he has not yet returned.","The Warg that did this evil deed has been defeated, but revenge cannot bring back the dead","Luned is at Galtrev, worriedly awaiting news of her late friend.\
\
You should break the news that Leolin met an untimely end at the hands of a Warg.","'Where could he be? He has never been this late before....'\
\
Luned suddenly seems to notice your presence.\
\
'You -- duvodiad! Are you going east out of Galtrev any time soon? If you are, could you look out for my friend Leolin? He ventured out onto the road early this morning and has not yet returned. His excursions to gather supplies never take this long....'","A Gnawing Worry"},
[371]={"'Slower you say? Drowsy even?\
\
'Yes, well... hoom...\
\
'That is unexpected, but not wholly so. There must be something of ancient wood in them after all.\
\
'To think that trees might have been bent so, it only makes me angrier... the Entmoot must know of this. Ta-rum....'","'Hoom. I once spoke with one of the Wise who believed that trolls were indeed Ents! Ta-rum! Perhaps the Wise are not as wise as they would like to believe, hoom. But it did get me to thinking... what if they are a bit Ent-like?\
\
'You see, we have a draught we give to the trees when they become upset. It slows them down, makes them more tree-like, less dangerous. So if the Wise are to be believed, and trolls are just a bit Entish, then perhaps it would work on them?'","Defeat Stone-trolls in the uruk-encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Stone-trolls in the uruk-encampment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tell Quickbeam how the draught affected the trolls.","Quickbeam has heard musings among the Wise that trolls might have once been Ents, twisted to dark forms. He is doubtful that this is the case, but if their twisted nature is in some manner similar to that of the Ents, then he believes it might be worthwhile to try an ancient draught upon them, meant to still the stirrings of maddened or fearful Huorns.","Stone-trolls patrol the uruk-encampment in eastern Nan Curunír.\
\
Quickbeam asked you to take the strange draught he provided and try splashing it upon the Stone-trolls. It may serve to soothe them or render them sleepy, as it is meant to do with the Huorns.","Talk to Quickbeam","A Good Draught"},
[372]={"Andreg is taking you to meet with Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp; however, he needs help with his own mission first.","Andreg has asked you to collect leaves and bark covered in the strange corruption so that Saeradan might be able to examine it.","'Aye, this should be enough. We should bring this to Saeradan as soon as possible.'","Una grave corrupción","You should bring the corrupted materials you collected to Andreg.","Collect piles of oozing corruption in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb> (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have not collected enough of the corrupted materials for Saeradan to examine.'","Bring the piles of oozing corruption to Andreg","'While returning here from the Rohirrim scout-camp, I thought I saw some strange form of corruption in the wood... like none I have ever seen. Unnatural, it seemed to me.\
\
'Saeradan knows more of this sort of corruption than I. Perhaps we should collect some as we journey back to the scout-camp and bring it to him.\
\
'Will you help?'","Collected piles of oozing corruption in the <rgb=#FFFF00>South Gravenwood</rgb> (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[373]={"'¿Qué es esto, entonces? Una especie de polvo incendiario... ¡qué extraño! ¿Quién haría algo así?'","Busca en Puente de Caballetes la causa de la explosión (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el polvo al Capitán Pasolargo","Has encontrado un barril explotado entre los escombros, cubierto de una fina polvora negra","'No me atrevo a abandonar mi puesto de guardia para investigar la carnicería, pero ¿te gustaría ayudar? Podrías buscar en el pueblo y averiguar cómo pudo haber sucedido esto.\
\
'La explosión fue ensordecedora; ¿por qué no se despertó nadie? ¿Qué causó este caos? Nunca he oído nada igual en toda mi vida....'","Aggy Cavazaña recuerda una gran explosión en el pueblo, y que ningún guardia salvo ella se despertó por el ruido.","Un gran estruendo en la noche","El Capitán Pasolargo se encuentra en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Deberías llevar el polvo que Encontraste Al Capitán Pasolargo.","Una pista sobre el gran estruendo oído en Puente de Caballetes puede encontrarse en algún lugar del pueblo.\
\
Aggy cavazaña te ha pedido que busques la fuente del caos Que arruinó puente de caballetes la noche anterior."},
[374]={"Derrota al Gran Trasgo","Un Gran Trasgo","El Gran Trasgo derrotado","'Te estamos en deuda por tu derrota del Gran Trasgo, ${PLAYER}.'","El Gran Trasgo se encuentra en la sala del trono de la Ciudad de los Trasgos, al noreste del campamento de Glóin.\
\
Glóin habló con pesar del mal que acecha en el corazón de la Ciudad de los Trasgos. Luego te pidió que entraras en ese lugar maligno y derrotaras al Gran Trasgo antes de que su amenaza crezca demasiado como para contenerla.","'${PLAYER}, no hablo a menudo de nuestros viajes con mi señor Thorin, pero ahora siento que debo hacerlo. Hace mucho tiempo, viajábamos por estas montañas con el saqueador Bolsón y fuimos capturados por los trasgos de la Ciudad de los Trasgos. Nos arrastraron a la oscuridad durante lo que pareció una eternidad, hasta que finalmente llegamos al centro de aquel lugar y nos encontramos con el Gran Trasgo.\
\
'No teníamos esperanza allí dentro, pues era tan oscuro que incluso nuestra vista enana se veía mermada, y todo parecía perdido. El Gran Trasgo descubrió armas entre nuestras pertenencias, armas que se habían usado contra su gente en tiempos antiguos, y enloqueció de furia. La esperanza se desvanecía aún más de nuestros corazones. Thorin, mi señor y líder, se mantuvo desafiante e intentó apaciguar al trasgo, pero nada calmó su ira. Justo cuando todo parecía más sombrío, Gandalf el Gris apareció y mató al Gran Trasgo, liberándonos de la Ciudad de los Trasgos y de las garras de quienes allí moraban.\
\
'Esta noticia sobre un nuevo Gran Trasgo llena mi corazón de temor. Si es cierto, no tenemos otra opción sino destruirlo antes de que los trasgos estén lo bastante organizados como para marchar hacia el este contra Dáin Pie de Hierro y los enanos de la Montaña Solitaria, o hacia el oeste contra los Hombres de Eriador. Te pido que te adentres en la sala del trono con tus aliados, encuentres a este Gran Trasgo y pongas fin a su reinado antes de que su sombra crezca tanto que se cierna sobre todo cuanto existe. ¿Lo harás?'","'Este viejo enano ha recuperado la esperanza gracias a ti, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Todos los enanos, en cualquier lugar, conocerán tu nombre cuando la amenaza que se alza sobre el mundo haya sido contenida; tienes mi palabra. Y la palabra de un enano es más fuerte que las montañas sobre las que nos alzamos.\
\
'Ashûrz ya no existe, y te lo debemos a ti.'","'Tu valentía es mayor que tu estatura, ${PLAYER}.'","Habla con Glóin en su campamento en las Montañas Nubladas.","Glóin recordó su experiencia junto a Thorin y la Compañía cuando se enfrentaron al Gran Trasgo durante su viaje con Bilbo Bolsón.","Glóin está en su campamento, justo fuera de la entrada a la Ciudad de los Trasgos.\
\
Entraste en la Ciudad de los Trasgos y exploraste lo más profundo de ese lugar hasta hallar la sala del trono. Allí derrotaste a Ashûrz, el Gran Trasgo. Con su caída, has quebrantado la fuerza de los trasgos de la Ciudad de los Trasgos y reducido la amenaza que representan para los pueblos del este y oeste de las Montañas Nubladas. Debes regresar con Glóin para informarle.","'Recuerdo que los túneles parecían no terminar nunca. Nos arrastraron durante días hacia la oscuridad antes de llevarnos a un gran salón donde el Gran Trasgo se sentaba sobre una enorme piedra y gobernaba a los trasgos de la Ciudad de los Trasgos.\
\
'Busca a este nuevo y miserable líder y acaba con su reinado antes de que realmente comience.'"},
[376]={"Elaglar of Dol Amroth fears that the Corsair forces under Azruthor's rule in Tarlang's Crown will soon grow beyond control.","Harnion can be found off the side of the road leading through Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond.\
\
Elaglar has asked you to seek Harnion in Tarlang's Crown and investigate the Corsair forces massing there.","Talk to Harnion in Tarlang's Crown","'A great threat rises to the north, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'What I have heard of the forces in Tarlang's Crown has grown more and more unbelievable with each account. This much remains clear... we cannot allow the Corsairs or their leader in the Crown, Azruthor, to gain any more of a foothold in our lands.\
\
'Once you have readied yourself and your allies, travel to Tarlang's Crown and find Harnion. He is a scout of mine and can guide you and your allies through our plans. I would prefer you keep this a quiet matter, for I do not wish to frighten the people.'","A Greater Foe","'Keep your voice down, traveller....\
\
'The Corsairs have seized the road through Tarlang's Crown and foul things are afoot. We shall need more than you or I alone if we are to drive them out.'","DNT"},
[378]={"Las cajas de Gadaric se encuentran en las ruinas de Minas Eriol, al sureste de la Posada Abandonada, donde Gadaric espera tu regreso.\
\
Para ayudar a Gadaric y a los Eglain, aceptaste recuperar las mercancías que quedaron en Minas Eriol tras el ataque de los trasgos.","Lleva los paquetes de mercancías a Gadaric Mascador","Un robo importante","Paquetes de mercancías recuperados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ten cuidado al entrar en Minas Eriol, al sureste, porque los trasgos son feroces.'","'Se agradecen mucho tus esfuerzos, ${CLASS}. Hace mucho tiempo, mi pueblo dejó atrás el bullicio de la vida en la ciudad y eligió vivir aquí, en el lugar de nuestros antepasados.\
\
'Nos llamamos Eglain, los Abandonados, y vivíamos en paz con la naturaleza, tomando solo lo que las ruinas nos ofrecían. Había paz, y no pensábamos que debíamos temer por ella. Pero entonces... un Montaraz y algunos otros cruzaron el Último Puente hacia el Bosque de los Trolls, y el mal se ha extendido a su paso.\
\
'Del norte vinieron trasgos y enanos aliados con orcos, algo inaudito pero cierto. Desde el sur, orcos portando un símbolo de una Mano Blanca se extendieron por Annunlos. Todos estos enemigos arrasaron la tierra y nos expulsaron de las ruinas donde una vez vivimos en paz.'","'Tus acciones han sido de gran ayuda para los Eglain.'","Recupera paquetes de mercancías (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Soy Gadaric Mascador, miembro de los Eglain. Comerciaba con artefactos encontrados en las Tierras Solitarias a coleccionistas de Bree a cambio de comida y otros artículos de primera necesidad. Hasta hace poco, nuestro comercio era muy activo, pero la oscuridad se ha apoderado de estas tierras y nuestro pueblo, los Eglain, se enfrenta al hambre y al asesinato.\
\
'trasgos se han infiltrado en las Tierras Solitarias y han dificultado el comercio; nos atacaron, asesinaron a muchos de los nuestros y se apoderaron de gran parte de nuestras mercancías. Las ruinas de la antigua Arnor dominan un gran valle al sureste de la Posada Abandonada. Ese lugar se llama Minas Eriol, y durante mucho tiempo fue muy querido por mi pueblo. ¿Podrías ir allí, recuperar nuestros paquetes comerciales de las cajas que quedan y traérmelos?\
\
'Las cajas son todo lo que queda de nuestra última colección.'","'Tú eres un amigo de los Eglain, ${PLAYER}.'","Gadaric Mascador es miembro de los Eglain, una tribu de Hombres que viven en las Tierras Solitarias. Se ganan la vida comerciando con los viajeros que atraviesan las Tierras Solitarias."},
[381]={"Talk to Doron","Collect sigils from brigands in Ost Celebrant (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","While venturing through Ost Celebrant, Doron has noticed grim standards flying among the ruins. Doron wishes for you to recover symbols of the brigands' allegiance so that he and your Rohirrim allies may better understand the foe that faces them.","Brigands are camped throughout Ost Celebrant.","Collected sigils from brigands in Ost Celebrant (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Doron is within Ost Celebrant. If he has left your side, he can be summoned with your horn.","'These men are vicious -- I saw the fury in their gaze as we battled. The symbols they hold are worn and hastily made, but inspire dread nonetheless. Keep those symbols among your belongings for now...you shall deliver them to your allies once we finish here.'","'${PLAYER}, halt! Do you see the banners that adorn these ruins? These men...they have been turned from tomb-robbers into an army. Could the Easterling be behind this?\
\
'We must bring the fight to these brigands before they are too many to stop! See if they carry any symbol of their true allegiance; I am certain your allies will want to know of this!'","Una lealtad sombría"},
[382]={"Collected diseased salamander stomachs (${NUMBER}/10)","Speak with Heshra, the herbalist, in the Khûtra Elder Hall","'I still need those stomachs to learn more about this disease.'","Elder Roshat has told you to speak with Heshra, the herbalist in the Khûtra Elder Hall, about the disease overtaking Khûtra.","'Yes, this is exactly what I need.'\
\
He examines the samples you brought him.\
\
'Just as I suspected! I don't think this will help the fish any, but I have plants here that can hopefully heal living versions of these animals. Give me a few minutes. Yes, honeywort in each....'","'I still don't trust you, but you've done more for us than any outsider ever has.\
\
'This disease... we have lost three of our own to it this week, and without the fishing....\
\
'Our village herbalist thinks something can be done about it. Perhaps even a salve created to reduce its effects. But first he needs more samples of the dreadful stuff, and from animals, not fish for some reason. He's in the Elder Hall at the end of this road. Talk to him, he knows better than I of what he needs.\
\
'Oh, and stranger – I've still got my eye on you.'","Heshra needs your help tracking down diseased salamanders west of Khûtra along the shore in order to find out more about this strange disease.","Return to Heshra in Khûtra","'Oh yes, more samples would be wonderful. I really need more animals that are afflicted, as I have plenty of fish. The fisher-folk just throw them outside my door. Dreadful smell. I've asked them not to anymore, but I suspect they do it for sport at this point.\
\
'Would you go west of here along the shore and bring me back samples of the diseased animals you find? I know the salamanders have been affected. It's the stomachs I need in particular.'","Collect diseased salamander stomachs (${NUMBER}/10)","Heshra, the herbalist needs your help collecting diseased salamanders outside of Khûtra in order to find out more about this strange disease.","A Grim Trail"},
[383]={"Warn Amalíbi in Ghalbûru about Bârshud's advance","'Oh now the Shâra will deign to meet with me? Now that my soldiers are bloodied, dead, scattered to the winds and lost in the Khûd? Where was this Shâra when I sent out my request for aid?\
\
'I will meet her in Iridír, if only so she knows the full weight of her mistake.\
\
'She will hear my fury, have no doubt in that.'","A Grim Warning","'Thank you, friend, for speaking with them and convincing them both to meet. We shall now gather in the hall, and quickly, as time is not our ally.'","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír","Warn Amalíbi at Ghalbûru's highest point about Bârshud's advance. Ghalbûru is located within Khûd Zagin, in the Ikorbân Valley.","Warn Girhâzi in Iridír about Bârshud's advance","'What a fool I was. Letting Bârshud cloud my emotions and stoke this fire. I should have seen his plan for what it was.\
\
'Quickly, you must warn Amalíbi in Ghalbûru and Girhâzi in Iridír. I have had some words with each and both are hearty and passionate fighters who want what is best for Shagâna.\
\
'I will finish here and then leave with Razâl and Numûru for Iridír. I will meet you there. We will have much to discuss, I'm afraid.'","Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír.","'Bârshud has just toed the line into fair Ambarûl. We were just about to convene a war council on our response to this aggression.\
\
'Of course we will meet with Mizâdi, and Amalíbi. We will accept all the help we can get in repelling this invasion.'","Warn Girhâzi in Iridír about Bârshud's advance. Iridír is located within Ambarûl, in the Ikorbân Valley.","The battle has been won, but this victory tastes bitter: Bârshud intends to cut through all of Khûd Zagin and Ambarûl with his army. Warn Amalíbi in Ghalbûru and Girhâzi in Iridír of his advance."},
[384]={"'Have you heard? Have you heard the news? It is dreadful, ${PLAYER}, dreadful!'","Fuirion is moved by Túmir's gesture, but refuses to give up his pursuit of escape by any means","A Growing Despair","Míreth and Túmir are in Gladion's home in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should see if the children can think of anything to cheer up their uncle, as they know him best.","Help Túmir try to cheer up Fuirion","Help Míreth try to cheer up Fuirion","Fuirion is moved by Míreth's gesture, but refuses to give up his pursuit of escape by any means","You should go outside of Gladion's home to give Fuirion some space to think upon his niece's and nephew's kind gestures.","Fuirion's situation with his family has grown so painful for him that he was willing to risk his life to escape the people he loves most in the world.","'I must leave this place as soon as I am recovered enough to stand. I tried already, but I fell back. I will keep trying.'\
\
You protest, asking Fuirion to stay abed and let his wound heal.\
\
'It does not matter, ${PLAYER}. Don't you see? I have no reason to heal, no reason to live. I have every reason to leave. I would take a hundred knife wounds before I stay another day so near to her.'","Go outside to give Fuirion some space and time to think"},
[386]={"Defeat Gríma's bodyguards (0/6)","After he was banished from Edoras, it appears that Gríma Wormtongue went north of the road to Isengard. He is either avoiding the road, has business to attend to elsewhere, or both.","You have encountered Gríma Wormtongue on the plains just north of Edoras, and he appears to be travelling west towards Isengard with a host of Orc bodyguards. You should deal with the bodyguards and confront Gríma.","A Grím Encounter","Defeat Gríma's bodyguards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Gríma's bodyguards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gríma would like to have a word with you after you defeated his bodyguards.","Talk to Gríma Wormtongue","'Well, are you not an annoying little ${RACE}? More like a maggot crawling in the carcass of this once great land. It is certain that you will die here...if not by my hand, then perhaps by your best friend's? A wise tongue can be stronger than the arms you bear....'\
\
'I have need of more Orcs, since you killed mine! Should you find me again, you will not be so fortunate.'"},
[387]={"'Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}, te mostraré tu puesto. ¡Todos debemos tomar las armas para defender el pueblo de los orcos saqueadores!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse en comunidad.</rgb>","'Deberías viajar al pueblo de Puente de Caballetes, en las Quebradas del Norte, y hablar con Severin Rodador. Ha solicitado la ayuda de guardianes capaces para defender el pueblo de los orcos que lo amenazan a diario.'","Habla con Severin Rodador y toma tu puesto en defensa de Puente de Caballetes","Un guardián debe endurecerse ante los peligros del mundo, pues se interpone entre esos males y toda la gente de bien.","'Puente de Caballetes es un pueblo sitiado. No lo confundas con otra cosa.'","'Me alegra que hayas venido, , pues los orcos nos presionan con gran crueldad. Algunos hombres han respondido a mi llamada, pero menos de los que esperaba.\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a tomar las armas en defensa del pueblo? ¡Dime cuándo lo estés y te mostraré tu puesto!'","'Harper me contó sobre tu defensa cuando regresé, ${PLAYER}, ¡y te agradezco! Me alegra informar que yo y algunos más pudimos rescatar a los granjeros atrapados en las Quebradas del Norte, un rescate que no habría sido posible sin tu ayuda aquí.\
\
'Los orcos se vuelven más audaces, eso está claro. Debemos resistirlos mientras podamos... Espero que sea suficiente.\
\
'¡Ah, no prestes atención a mis palabras sombrías! Hoy hemos ganado una victoria, ¡y eso basta! Tus habilidades mejoran con la práctica — cada ataque de los orcos nos hace más fuertes, hasta que un día los atacaremos y los derrotaremos por completo.'","'Siempre eres ${PLAYER:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} aquí, ${PLAYER}.'","'Los orcos se vuelven más audaces, pero los resistiremos mientras sea necesario.'","Severin Rodador está en el pueblo de Puente de Caballetes, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Severin Rodador espera escuchar que estás preparado para defender el pueblo de los orcos que lo amenazan.","'La guerra se gesta en muchas tierras y contra muchos pueblos, ${PLAYER}, pero pocos están tan acosados como los del pueblo de Puente de Caballetes. Uno de sus guardianes, un Hombre llamado Severin Rodador, ha enviado un mensaje a todo aquel que quiera escuchar: Puente de Caballetes debe ser defendido.\
\
'Los orcos cruzaron las Quebradas del Norte y presionan cruelmente contra la ciudad. Debes ayudar a resistirlos, ${PLAYER}, o no eres un verdadero guardián. ¡Ve a Puente de Caballetes y ofrece tu ayuda a Severin Rodador!\
\
'Si el pueblo cae, el camino hacia las Tierras de Bree quedará abierto para los orcos, y toda esperanza se perderá. Este es tu deber, ${PLAYER} — no puedes negarlo.'","Severin Rodador está en el pueblo de Puente de Caballetes, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Severin Rodador ha enviado un mensaje desde Puente de Caballetes: el pueblo está bajo amenaza de ataque por parte de orcos saqueadores y debe ser defendido.","Severin Rodador está en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Severin Rodador espera hablar contigo sobre tu defensa del pueblo durante el reciente ataque de los orcos.","El Deber de un Guardián"},
[388]={"'Even after so many attacks, we still know little of the plans of the Haradrim aside from their slow advance across the Erui to the East.\
\
'I have seen their captains, or however they are named among their people, bearing small missives during their assaults on Halach. I do not know if these are letters they have seized from settlements they have already razed or their orders from some unseen master, but I wish to know... for the good of all in Lebennin and beyond.\
\
'You are a hale ${CLASS}, and can stand against the Haradrim! If you seek out their leaders near the banks of the Erui, you might be able to relieve them of these missives... and shed some light on their designs for Gondor.'","'These are grim tidings, ${PLAYER}...\
\
'This missive fills me with dread, and I ask that you take it away from me. Do with it what you will, but remove it from my sight!\
\
'The Lady must be told of this... I only hope she can send word to the Steward in time!'","The leaders of the Haradrim forces in Upper Lebennin bear vile missives from the Enemy detailing their plans for Gondor.","The letter can be found in your inventory.\
\
You have discovered orders carried by one of the Haradrim war-leaders and should now read it.","Read the missive to the Haradrim","Irodon can be found in Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have uncovered the plans of the Haradrim in Upper Lebennin as well as Enemy's plans for Osgiliath. You should now return to Irodon in Halach.","You have found a missive and should now examine it!","Retrieve a missive from a Haradrim war-leader near the Erui","Haradrim war-leaders can be found along the banks of the Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
Irodon has asked you to seek out any orders the Haradrim war-leaders might bear.","The missive tells of a great host gathering within the ruins of Osgiliath!","Deliver the missive to Irodon","A Guiding Blade"},
[389]={"Defeat goblins at Khoblún Utot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Have you delivered that offering yet, Duvodiad?'","A Half a Threat","The Hobbits of Maur Tulhau believe there is a nearby village of hobbits turned wild from years of separation from their kin. Iolo Brochtû is interested in making peace with them.","Iolo Brochtû is at Maur Tulhau, north of Khoblún Utot.\
\
You should return to Iolo Brochtû with news of your discovery at Khoblún Utot.","Deliver the peace offering to the hobbits of the neighbouring village","The 'hobbits' are actually a kind of goblin","'What say ye? Those are no hobbits at all? What ye describe sounds like bugan to me! We've had trouble with them in the past, or so our old tales say....'","'So, you've been a great help to my folk, so perhaps you will aid with another task. A while back, our hunters discovered a village of hobbits to the south-east of here. They've gone wild -- I suppose from too many years apart from us civilized folk.\
\
'We thought to send a peace offering to them, as they've been none too friendly to us when we've come across them in the forest, but Gwin Cuthonon went missing. Perhaps you would take this peace offering to the village?\
\
'Perhaps they've gone too wild, but we should try nonetheless, as we're neighbours.'","The 'hobbit'-village south of Maur Tulhau is inhabited by a strange variety of wild goblin.\
\
You should do your best to remove the threat of the goblins.","Talk to Iolo Brochtû at Maur Tulhau","The neighbouring village lies to the south of Maur Tulhau.\
\
Iolo Brochtû has asked you to deliver the peace offering to the hobbits of the neighbouring village."},
[390]={"Tamindur can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn.\
\
After returning to Abkân'aban, Thrástan revealed himself to be a servant of the First Crafter named Tamindur the Forge-servant. You should approach Tamindur.","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Abkân'aban","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn.\
\
After gathering your allies and speaking with Tamindur, you are ready to depart for Watchers' Roost. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Talk to Spall at Abkân'aban","You can't be certain, but Tamindur appears to smile at your gesture","Despite his stony gaze, Tamindur appears to be pleased at your approach","Spall can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn.\
\
After repelling the Iron Crown from Abkân'aban and the revelation of Thrástan's true identity, your allies remain gathered at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Spall.","A Hallowed Return","Hersegg can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn.\
\
After repelling the Iron Crown from Abkân'aban and the revelation of Thrástan's true identity, your allies remain gathered at Abkân'aban. You should talk to Hersegg.","'What an adventure, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'From the Lonely Mountain to Elderslade and now to the very heart of Mount Gundabad... I am grateful our paths crossed when they did. Perhaps I was a bit too eager to confront the Iron Crown, but it all worked out in the end, didn't it?'\
\
Hersegg smirks and looks to Tamindur.\
\
'A victory hard won... and secured with as near a miracle as I've ever seen! The First Crafter himself must watch over us here in Mount Gundabad!\
\
'I will be ready to depart in just a moment, my friend. Why don't you go and see if Spall is ready to set out?'","'I hardly know what to say, ${PLAYER}...'\
\
Spall gazes up at the White Stone Forge where Tamindur now stands watch.\
\
'I have seen more in one day than I dreamt of seeing in a lifetime.\
\
'As for me, my survey will continue unhindered now that the Iron Crown have been driven out of Gloomingtarn. Who knows what other secrets lie hidden for us to discover? I, for one, relish the chance to find them!\
\
'When Lord Stormhammer wishes to depart, I shall be prepared.'","Approach Tamindur at Abkân'aban","Talk to Tamindur","Tamindur can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn.\
\
After returning to Abkân'aban, Thrástan revealed himself to be a servant of the First Crafter named Tamindur the Forge-servant. You should bow before Tamindur before speaking to him.","After the revelation of Thrástan's true identity and the defeat of the Iron Crown at Abkân'aban, the Gabil'akkâ has won a lasting victory in their efforts to reclaim Mount Gundabad.","<rgb=#FF00FF>Bow</rgb> before Tamindur at Abkân'aban","'Is everyone prepared to depart? Very good, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Let us return to Watchers' Roost and, at last, we can set about undoing the damage the Iron Crown has done to Gloomingtarn!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You will swiftly travel to Watchers' Roost after advancing this quest.</rgb>","'In light of what has happened here at Abkân'aban, I shall soon have to speak to Prince Durin.\
\
'That a servant of the First Crafter would reveal himself to us is too unbelievable a tale to send by any missive! Only my voice might lend it any credibility... and even so, the Prince may have to see with his own eyes!\
\
'Let us not trouble our new benefactor, ${PLAYER}. Our gratitude is enough, I think, and there are greater matters in this world for one of such power to lend his aid.\
\
'You should speak to the others here and see if they are ready to depart. When that is so, come speak to me again!'","'You need not fear my wrath, ${PLAYER}. Approach, and let us speak!\
\
'Long ago, when the Shaper's work was finished, I was bidden to rest beneath Mount Gundabad. In time, I awoke as Thrástan; different in form, but alike in mind and spirit to walk among Durin's Folk. In my long years of solitude, the two diverged, but I am now restored.\
\
'At long last, my vigil nears its end and a new Age is soon to dawn. But fear not, I shall ward the Stone of Awakening from all evil that would seek to master it until I am called back to the Uttermost West.\
\
'Yet many trials lay ahead for you, little one.'","Hermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn.\
\
After departing from Abkân'aban, you have returned to Watchers' Roost. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.","Talk to Hersegg at Abkân'aban","Talk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Watchers' Roost","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, it seems our journey through Mount Gundabad shall have more than its fair share of surprises!\
\
'My expedition and I will see to repairing the damage left by the Iron Crown, and we shall set the echo-horns across this great cavern into alignment once more. The warding-runes may never again repel our foes, but when the Mountain-home is ours again and evermore, I hope we find we have no need for them!\
\
'I am certain Prince Durin and the others shall have need of your aid in the Clovengap and beyond, but I thank you for all you have done here, my friend. Without your aid, the secrets of our ancestors may well have been forgotten!\
\
'Baruk Khazâd! For Gundabad!'","Tamindur can be found at Abkân'aban in Gloomingtarn.\
\
After returning to Abkân'aban, Thrástan revealed himself to be a servant of the First Crafter named Tamindur the Forge-servant. You talk to Tamindur."},
[391]={"Defeat Half-trolls at Lang Boha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Herion can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have defeated many of the Corsairs and Haradrim in Lang Boha and should report your success to Herion.","Lang Boha can be found far to the west of Linhir in Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Herion has asked you to weaken the forces at Lang Boha to keep them from advancing to the north.","'Far to the west, the Enemy holds a camp on our beaches. We cannot allow this intrusion to stand!\
\
'Each day, they work to gain more ground in Dor-en-Ernil and surely, it shall not be long until they breach the vale to the north.\
\
'I would ask that you travel to their camp and weaken their forces as best you can. I do not expect one to stand against so many, but it is my hope that your assault will delay their advance another day.'","A Halted March","Talk to Herion in Linhir","Defeated Corsairs and Haradrim at Lang Boha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Half-trolls at Lang Boha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have done well to weaken them so, ${PLAYER}. Our work is not done, but your efforts shall delay them long enough for us to plan our next assault.'","The Haradrim and Corsair forces have advanced northward in Dor-en-Ernil and now pose a great threat to the people of Gondor.","Defeat Corsairs and Haradrim at Lang Boha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[392]={"'¡Bueno, parece que vuestro jueguecito funcionó! ¡Pamplinas!   \
\
'Otra fiesta arruinada, y no precisamente gracias a ti. ¿Por qué no vas a contarle a tu buen amigo Hamfast lo que has hecho aquí? No me cabe duda de que él te incitó a todo esto, con su querida Caléndula enviada aquí solo para avergonzarme de esa manera.'","El Tío Gamyi se encuentra delante de su agujero en Bolsón de Tirada.\
\
Deberías ir a decirle que has frustrado los planes de Lobelia","Habéis desbaratado el plan de Lobelia, quería quedarse para ella los mejores alimentos del banquete de Yule.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu diario de misiones cuando el festival actual haya finalizado.</rgb>","La alegría vuelve a Hobbiton","'¿Así que Lobelia pensaba guardarse toda la mejor comida para ella y los suyos? Me alegra que hayas podido poner las cosas en su sitio; y el resto de la gente aquí en Hobbiton piensa lo mismo.\
\
'Simplemente nos pareció correcto traerte algo. Lobelia tenía razón, en cierto modo: no tenemos mucho que ofrecer, ¡pero compartimos lo que podemos, especialmente con aquellos que nos han dado tanto como tú!\
\
'Nos gustaría que te quedaras con este árbol de Yule. Es un trasplante; mi sobrino Halfast lo trajo de la Cuaderna del Norte. Íbamos a plantarlo en el patio, pero viendo cómo nos has ayudado... bueno, Caléndula pensó que lo mejor sería que te lo quedaras para tu casa.'"},
[393]={"Collect the swords Nukûsh has forged for deliver to Numûru.","The flames leap to greet the dry crackling wood","'There you are. Well you've gathered plenty of both at least. Leave them there, I'll take care of the ore. Add the wood to the fire, it's getting low. Then you can bring these swords to Numûru. Hope you don't mind sweating, there's no loafing here.'","Speak with Nukûsh in Urmâkh","Speak again with Nukûsh in Urmâkh.","Feed the wood into the fire in the forge.","Acquire iron ore and wood from outside Urmâkh to the east for Nukûsh, the blacksmith in Urmâkh.","Deliver Nukûsh's swords to Numûru in Urmâkh","'Ah, that's enough to get me ahead for once. You move quick. You remind me of myself at a young age. Nice enough for you to help an old man with his tasks. I appreciate it. Anytime you want to come back, there's a spot at the forge for you.'","A Hard Day's Work","Collect Nukûsh's newly forged swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Picked up wood for Nukûsh's forge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deliver Nukûsh's newly forged swords to Numûru in Urmâkh. Numûru can be found by Urmâkh's eastern gate.","Collected Nukûsh's newly forged swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring gathered wood and ore to Nukûsh in Urmâkh.","Mined iron ore for smithing (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring gathered wood and ore to Nukûsh in Urmâkh","Feed the wood into the fire in the forge","Nukûsh the blacksmith has asked for your help in accomplishing his daily tasks, as his apprentice has joined Mizâdi's warriors.","'My thanks to you. It's been fair too long since we had fresh blades. These will cut the Barkhûshim quite well, and any others who draw Mizâdi's ire. Give my regards, and that of the Subuzûri, to Nukûsh.'","Mine iron ore for smithing (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pick up wood for Nukûsh's forge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The fires are hot and there's work to be done! My apprentice ran off, off to join Mizâdi's band, he did. I don't mind a good war, but not when it hurts the forge. How am I supposed to make blades for Mizâdi when there's no one to help gather ore for the swords and collect wood for the fires?\
\
'You want to help? Well there may be some good left in this world after all. You can start by gathering some wood and ore, we have plenty of both outside of Urmâkh, to the east. Watch out for the jackals, they've been roaming closer and closer to the city proper.'"},
[394]={"Have dinner with Gladion's family","'Please help my brother!'","The healer can be found in the apothecary's shop in Dínadab.\
\
You should hasten to the healer to get help for Fuirion.","'Fuirion, please tell us what happened to you? Oh, why will you not say? Why will you not look at me?'","'It is almost time for dinner, and you have certainly earned it. Go on inside, for Limril is waiting. But where is my brother Fuirion? He should have been back quite some time ago.\
\
'Go ahead in, ${PLAYER}. I will wait here for Fuirion. You may tell Limril that we will be in shortly, I hope.'","You hurriedly tell the healer that Fuirion has been grievously wounded, and bleeds alarmingly onto his brother's floor.\
\
'Fuirion wounded! What could that young man have been up to, to get himself so hurt? I will go right away.'","A Hard-earned Meal","Gladion has invited you for a home-cooked meal at his family's table.","Summon the healer to help Fuirion","'Hello -- you must be ${PLAYER}. Gladion told me you would be joining us for dinner tonight. So my husband's brother Fuirion is late? Odd... he is usually on time when we sit down as a family.\
\
'I wonder where he could be!'","Limril can be found inside her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should go into Gladion's home and speak with his wife Limril."},
[397]={"Túmir saw Fuirion disappear earlier that day on a secretive adventure of sorts","Pick fresh kingsfoil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Follow the healer to Fuirion","'This is a peaceful town. How could he have gotten so injured?'","Bandage linens can be found hanging outside the shop. Kingsfoil grows wild in the fields around Dínadab.\
\
You should collect kingsfoil and bandage linens while the healer works on Fuirion.","Fuirion's family -- brother, sister-in-law, niece, and nephew -- are in Gladion's home in Dínadab, anxiously looking on.\
\
You should speak with the family members.","Míreth has noticed that her uncle has been more sad and distant than usual of late","Collect bandage linens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Well, that doesn't give us any answers. But I have gained a little knowledge: this is a knife wound. A clean cut, easy to stitch up. It will take a little time.\
\
'While I take care of Fuirion, would you be so good as to mind my chores at the shop? I was about to pull down the linens for bandages. Also, we are always needing more Kingsfoil. It grows wild in these parts... a lovely plant, with great healing qualities.'","Collected bandage linens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Limril stares intently at Fuirion, brows knit in concern.","Gladion is shocked by his brother's injury; he has no information for you","Ask the family if Fuirion told them anything (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","A Healer's Aid","You feel as if you are missing something to Fuirion's tale...","The healer is in Gladion's home in Dínadab in order to assist the wounded Fuirion.\
\
You should speak with the healer again.","Limril is white and shaken as she expresses her worry for her husband's brother","'Come, come! Let us make haste!'","Limril, white as a ghost, does not speak. Her eyes are fixed on her brother-in-law, alarmed and concerned.","'A nasty wound, this. He won't seem to say a word. You should ask his family if he's said anything to them, and I will have a look at Fuirion's wound.'","Fuirion is in Gladion's home in Dínadab.\
\
You should question Fuirion about his wounds.","The apothecary shop is in southern Dínadab in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should bring the supplies to the shop.","'My uncle Fuirion has been strange lately. I do not understand. Why is he bleeding?\
\
'Is this because of his adventure? I saw him leaving town this morning, and he said he was going on an adventure, but would be back for dinner. He wasn't supposed to get hurt!\
\
'He told me not to tell anyone about that....'","Speak with the healer again","Picked fresh kingsfoil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the supplies to the shop","'My uncle is hurt badly, isn't he? I don't like it.\
\
'He has been very sad lately. I don't think anyone notices, but I do, because he never wants to play or read with me anymore. He does not eat as much as a farmer should. But nobody notices but me.\
\
'Do you think he will be all right?'","'I will hasten to Gladion's home at once, dear. Follow me, please! I might need your aid when I arrive, depending on his condition.'","The healer has made for Gladion's home in Dínadab in order to assist the wounded Fuirion.\
\
You should run after the healer to see if you can be of any help.","'You may leave those with me, dear. Fuirion is resting now, and should remain so for a fortnight at least. I stitched him up while you were out collecting goods for me.\
\
'He did not speak a word the entire time I was there. I suppose he is just in shock from the attack. It will pass.\
\
'Thank you for the supplies! I am tired after the excitement of this day. You saved me a good deal of work.'","Question Fuirion about his attack","Fuirion, pale from blood loss, his face drawn with pain, does not speak when you approach him.","'My brother! How could he have sustained such a wound, ${PLAYER}? We are but peaceful farmers here....'","You have urged the healer of Dínadab to rush to Fuirion's aid, as he lies grievously wounded at Gladion's home.","'He has not spoken a word, save what he said to you. It is unlike him. What could have happened? Why will he not speak?'"},
[398]={"'Have you found the herbs which I requested? We will need them and soon.'","Collect royal jelly (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Beehives, goat's rue, klamath weed, mistletoe, and sweet myrtle can be found throughout the Windfells. Look on trees for mistletoe and bee-hives. \
\
Saeradan has asked you to collect several herbs and bring them to him to be prepared for delivery to the Uch-lûth.","Collected royal jelly (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A Healing Hand","Collect sweet myrtle roots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Rangers of the Grey Company seek to acquire the good will of the Uch-lûth, the Dunlending clan inhabiting Enedwaith.","Collected goat's rue flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected mistletoe (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith.\
\
You should bring the herbs you foraged to Saeradan.","Collect klamath weed flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected sweet myrtle roots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect mistletoe (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'As I mentioned before, ${PLAYER}, our stores run low, and we must seek the good will of the Algraig to replenish them.\
\
'Herbs for medicines will benefit both us and the Algraig...will you forage some up for me? Search on trees for beehives...within, you may find the royal jelly the bees produce. This can be used to treat many illnesses. You should also seek out goat's rue...it can be used to treat ailments of the liver and to combat fever. Klamath weed fights many diseases. Mistletoe, which grows on tree-branches, may be used to treat cancers and strengthen the heart. Sweet myrtle has a property to relax the ill.\
\
'When you have found everything we need, bring them to me.'","'You may find the herbs we require throughout the Windfells...beehives will be found near trees, though, to be certain.'","Collect goat's rue flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected klamath weed flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah! The herbs I asked you to forage. These will aid us upon our journey and perhaps help to earn the good will of the Algraig.'","Bring the herbs to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan"},
[399]={"Derrota a los pollos de Khudi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Una comida abundante","Encuentra y derrota al pollo particularmente agresivo en Shegdush, en la cima de la colina.","Tu misión es viajar a Shegdush y recolectar huevos y reducir el número de pollos y jabalíes en la zona.","Jabalíes de Khudi derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pollos de Khudi derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Con un fuerte cacareo, un pollo particularmente agresivo ha aparecido para defender el rebaño.","Derrota a los jabalíes de Khudi (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoger huevos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hola. ¡Estos huevos son exactamente lo que necesitábamos! Regresemos a Iridír juntos.'","Huevos recolectados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota al pollo particularmente agresivo en la cima de la colina"},
[400]={"Found the camp that Angârmu mentioned","Find Angârmu's beloved pet, Ershûr","Return to Angârmu with his beloved pet, Ershûr","A Heavy Loss","Find the camp that Angârmu mentioned","'A visitor! A welcome sight! I ask of you to find my beloved pet. My beloved Ershûr. He wandered somewhere I know not.\
\
'He must be at the camping spot! Yes! That is his favourite spot. Ershûr must have ran off to go there. But I can not go, I must stay here.\
\
'You must go to his camping spot near the river to the south-east for me and find dear Ershûr. Find him, and bring him back to me so that I can keep him safe.\
\
'And tell him... tell him I miss him dearly.'","Found Ershûr","Look for Angârmu's pet, Ershûr, at the camp.","Angârmu has asked you to recover his beloved pet who has yet to come home.","Return to Angârmu in Malgâma near Zikrum-dûl with his beloved pet, Ershûr.","Angârmu has asked you to help him find his missing pet, Ershûr.","'You found him! My sweet Ershûr. I have missed you!'\
\
Angârmu takes the rock from you and hugs it with a wide smile on his face.\
\
'You are a true friend. To me and my dear Ershûr. Thank you. I can now be certain he is safe from harm.'"},
[401]={"Ruthless Tom guards the west gate.\
\
You should carry the shipment to Ruthless Tom.","Deliver the fourth box of supplies to the guard at the west gate","The package for Isengard has been delivered to the guard","The third Overseer is at the worksite just uphill and to the south from the second worksite.\
\
You should carry the first shipment to the third Overseer.","The first Overseer is at the worksite near the western gate of Galtrev.\
\
You should carry the first shipment to the Overseer.","Deliver the third box of supplies to the third worksite's Overseer","Gethin can be found recovering from a long day's work near the fourth worksite.\
\
You should return to Gethin and tell him that all of the boxes have been successfully delivered.","The package for Isengard has been delivered to the Overseer","Talk to Gethin at the fourth worksite","The second Overseer is at the worksite slightly up the hill from the first.\
\
You should carry the first shipment to the second Overseer.","'Ah, thank you, ${PLAYER}! What a kind soul you must be, to help the foolish people here in Galtrev.\
\
'Once, I might have been able to show you proper hospitality. Now, alas, all I can offer you is friendship, little though it is worth.'","A Heavy Task","Gethin is an old man, and no longer has the strength to lift the boxes he has been charged with delivering.","Deliver the second box of supplies to the second worksite's Overseer","Deliver the first box of supplies to the first worksite's Overseer","'Are you a visitor here in Galtrev? I wish you could have seen it before -- it was the greatest village in all of Dunland! Now it is naught but a labour camp for the White Hand.\
\
'But all the working men have gone, or perhaps they were taken. The old and the women are left to bear heavy burdens. For myself, I cannot even lift the boxes I am supposed to carry. I am much too slow for this, and I am always falling behind....'","'If I lift another box, I fear my back will give out completely....'"},
[403]={"'Antes de decirle dónde está ese tonto de Tuk que busca, necesito que me haga un pequeño favor. Verá, mi hierba para pipa es conocida en toda la Comarca, y un poco más allá, y eso significa que mucha gente viene a pedirme hojas.\
\
'Bueno, mi cosecha actual aún no está lista para la recolección, pero soy un hobbit listo, ¿sabe? Cuando los osos dormían en invierno, escondí un barril de hojas en una de sus guaridas, para días lluviosos como hoy.\
\
'Vaya a las guaridas de osos al sur de aquí y encuentre ese barril de hojas. Cuando me lo traiga, le diré lo que sé sobre ese Tuk.'","Lleva un barril de hierba para pipa a Longo Madriguera","'¡Oh, qué terrible! Ese Longo es un tipo grosero. Siento mucho que le haya jugado esa mala pasada. La próxima vez que lo vea, tendré unas palabras con él.\
\
'Ahora, volviendo al asunto de Gerebert. Creo que acabo de tener una idea sobre a quién más podríamos preguntar, si todavía estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a salir a buscarlo.'","'¿Por qué sigues ahí ${PLAYERNAME:parado[m]|parada[f]}? Te dije todo lo que sabía sobre ese Tuk que buscabas... ¡Y resulta que no sabía nada!\
\
'¡Ahora vete!'","El diario de Gerebert Tuk reveló que había aceptado un desafío para esconderse en uno de los carros de hojas de Longo Madriguera. Esilia Tuk te ha pedido que le ayudes a buscar a su primo.","El botín escondido","Esilia Tuk se encuentra en el centro de Alforzaburgo.\
\
Longo Madriguera aceptó decirte lo que sabía sobre Gerebert a cambio de un barril de hojas que había escondido en una guarida de osos. Sin embargo, cuando se lo llevaste, Longo te reveló que no sabía nada sobre Gerebert. Deberías volver con Esilia Tuk y contarle lo que ha pasado.","'¿Dónde está ese barril de hojas? Si quieres saber lo que sé sobre tu amigo Tuk, me traerás ese barril.\
\
'Escondí las hojas en una de las guaridas de osos al sur de aquí. No debería ser muy difícil de encontrar.'","'Está bien, has encontrado las hojas. Dámelas. Ahora cumpliré mi parte del trato. Ese Tuk que buscas... Gerebert era su nombre, ¿no? ¿Y se escondió en uno de mis carros de hojas?\
\
'Bueno, yo no lo he visto. ¿Eh? No dije que hubiera visto a ese Tuk tuyo. Solo dije que te diría lo que sabía. ¡Y eso es todo lo que sé! ¡Ahora vete!'","Las guaridas de osos se encuentran al sur de la granja de Longo Madriguera.\
\
Esilia Tuk te ha pedido que hables con Longo Madriguera sobre su primo Gerebert. Longo ha exigido que le hagas un favor antes de hablar. Te ha dicho que su hierba para pipa tiene mucha demanda, pero que su cosecha actual aún no está lista para la recolección. Te ha encargado que recuperes un barril de hierba para pipa que escondió en una guarida de osos durante el invierno."},
[404]={"'Be cautious as you make your way through these lands. You will find support in smaller numbers as you venture further from our holdings here. Remember, the bears and eagles are our allies. They will assist you should you come under attack.'","Talk to Ascwyn","A Hike Like No Other","Ettenmoors location visited","The Grimwood Lumber-camp is west of Glân Vraig. Lugazag is west of Glân Vraig, on the west side of the Hoarwell. The Isendeep Mine is far to the north-west of Glân Vraig. Tol Ascarnen is south of the Isendeep Mine, north-west of Glân Vraig. Tirith Rhaw is east of Tol Ascarnen and north-west of Glân Vraig. Observe your map to see who currently controls the location. Red locations are held by the Enemy, and blue by the Free Peoples.\
\
Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn explained that the contested locales throughout the Ettenmoors hold some manner of importance to the Free Peoples and the forces of Angmar and suggested that you visit each.","Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn is at Glân Vraig within the Coldfells.\
\
You have found your way through the Ettenmoors and located the Grimwood Lumber-camp, Lugazag Tower, Isendeep Mine, Tol Ascarnen and Tirith Rhaw. Now you should return to Glân Vraig and speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn.","'Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. Scouts reported that you visited each location. It is good to know that you were so diligent in accomplishing this task.\
\
'We have need of people like you. As promised, I have a gift for you. You will find that many here are willing to part with these tokens in exchange for assistance. Quartermaster Ash, in the stonework gazebo to the east of my location will exchange these tokens for keys to the chests we have at Glân Vraig.\
\
'These chests contain the odds and ends we find during the battles which occur throughout the Ettenmoors and are only a small piece of what we can offer you in exchange for your assistance. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. If you have a chance, speak with Captain-General Tordúr before heading back into the wild.'","'You will face a great many foes here in the Ettenmoors, some more dangerous than others. Specifically, the Uruks, Orcs, Wargs, and spiders. We have seen that their cunning is unmatched.\
\
'They bear the brunt of their commanders' derision and still attack without care for their lives, continuously crashing against the walls of the strongholds throughout the Ettenmoors. You must use caution once you leave the safety of this fortress... and yet, you must learn the paths available to you in this wild place.\
\
'You should strike out into the Ettenmoors and visit the locations which enhance our ability to fight on this front. In the south, deep in the Grimwood Forest, is the Grimwood Lumber-camp; once used by the hobbits in Hoarhallow, it is now a contested location with rich wood for constructing palisades. North of the lumber-camp, on the west side of the Hoarwell River, is Lugazag, a tower oft in the control of the Enemy. Deep in the hills at the base of the Misty Mountains in the lands called Arador's End, you will find the Isendeep Mine, where rich minerals and ore can be found. South from there, on an island in the centre of the Hoarwell, is Tol Ascarnen. The last location east from Tol Ascarnen and not far to the north and west of Glân Vraig is Tirith Rhaw. Make your way to these locations, and when you have visted them all, return to me. I will see that you are well rewarded.'","The Ettenmoors has several locations which allow for an advantage over the foe.","Visit the Grimwood Lumber-camp, Isendeep Mine, Tol Ascarnen, Tirith Rhaw, and Lugazag."},
[405]={"'¡Oh, hola!\
\
'Si tienes una queja que presentar contra el Servicio Postal Rápido, te pido que la pongas por escrito y la entregues a mi ayudante, Ebbo. Somos conscientes de que hay cierto número de problemas con correo retrasado o perdido que algunos hobbits nos han reportado en las últimas semanas. ¡Por supuesto, el Servicio Postal Rápido llegará al fondo de todo esto!\
\
'Con todo esto aclarado, ¿quién eres y cómo puedo ayudarte?\
\
Te presentas al carteor Cavada y le preguntas qué está pasando en el Servicio Postal Rápido.\
\
'Encantado de conocerte, ${PLAYER}. Soy Walto Cavada, y he sido cartero desde hace doce años. Diría que es mi vocación, ¡si es que crees en esas cosas! Sobre lo que está pasando con el Servicio Postal Rápido, me gustaría poder decírtelo. Como he comentado, el correo está llegando tarde o no llegando, y la gente de la Comarca Allende no está nada contenta. No sé si el jefe de correos está probando algo nuevo o cambiando rutas, pero no creo que sea eso.'\
\
El cartero Cavada mira alrededor y baja la voz.\
\
'Entre tú y yo, creo que alguien está manipulando el correo. Si crees que puedes ayudarme, reúnete conmigo dentro dentro del Servicio Postal Rápido.'","Los nudos de este paquete parecen estar atados a toda prisa, y lleva un curioso símbolo marcado en tinta","Examina las cartas y paquetes llegados desde la Comarca (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Debo disculparme por el desorden, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Mira, estamos un poco desbordados aquí en Nobotella con cartas y paquetes que deben ser entregados a la Comarca Aquende. La mayoría de la gente de Cavada Grande, Hobbiton y demás simplemente la llaman la Comarca. Me parece un poco raro, pero bueno. Hemos tenido unos cuantos carteros que han venido desde la Comarca Aquende con pequeñas entregas, pero ninguno de ellos está tardando tanto como debería para entregar el correo al resto de la Comarca. Es casi como si estuvieran intentando ralentizar todo el proceso. ¡Por todos los cielos, tenemos un paquete destinado a Cepeda que lleva aquí más de un mes!\
\
'Ebbo recibió una entrega del Servicio Postal Rápido de El Cruce esta mañana, y como de costumbre, era muy ligero. Desafortunadamente, después de inspeccionar las cartas y los paquetes, solo me ha hecho sospechar aún más que alguien está intentando maniuplar deliberadamente el correo.\
\
'¿Por qué no vas al mostrador y les echas un vistao, ${PLAYER}? ¡Tengo curiosidad por saber qué opinas de su estado!'","Las cartas y los paquetes se encuentran por todo el Servicio Postal Rápido de Nobotella.\
\
El cartero Cavada te ha pedido que examines las cartas y los paquetes entregados desde la Comarca.","El cartero Cavada se encuentra en el interior del Servicio Postal Rápido de Nobotella.\
\
Después de examinar cartas y paquetes entregados desde la Comarca, has encontrado pruebas de manipulación y un tipo extraño de firma. Debes reportarlo al cartero Cavada en el interior del Servicio Postal Rápido en Nobotella.","Parece que este sobre fue abierto y reabierto rápidamente con algún tipo de resina","El cartero Cavada de Nobotella ha empezado a sospechar que alguien está interfiriendo en el Servicio Postal Rápido, manipulando el correo y ralentizando su entrega a los habitantes de la Comarca Allende.","Habla con el cartero Cavada en el Servicio Postal Rápido de Nobotella","Aunque la carta no tiene signos de manipulación, está arrugada y manchada de té","Este paquete no está sellado y la tapa está apoyada sobre él sin ajustar","El cartero Cavada se encuentra en el interior del Servicio Postal Rápido en Nobotella.\
\
Después de empezar a sospechar que alguien está manipulando el correo que llega a la Comarca Allende, el cartero Cavada te ha pedido que reúnas con él en el interior del Servicio Postal Rápido en Nobotella. Habla con el cartero Cavada dentro del Servicio Postal Rápido.","Indicios de manipulación","Reúnete con el cartero Cavada en el interio del Servicio Postal Rápido en Nobotella","'¿Qué piensas, ${PLAYER}? ¿Qué has averiguado de esas cartas y paquetes? ¿Están mis preocupaciones mal fundadas?'\
\
Le cuentas al cartero Cavada que a menos que muchísimos hobbits hayan olvidado por pura coincidencia añadir posdatas tras cerrar las cartas, debes concluir que hay signos obvios de manipulación en todas las entregas recientes al Servicio Postal Rápido de Nobotella.\
\
'¡Lo sabía!'","El Servicio Postal Rápido está lleno de cartas y paquetes sin entregar","El Servicio Postal Rápido está en Nobtella.\
\
Después de sospechar que alguien está manipulando el correo que llega a la Comarca Allende, el cartero Cavada te ha pedido que te reúnas con él en el interior del Servicio Postal Rápido de Nobotella. Reúnete con el cartero Cavada en el Servicio Postal Rápido.","Parece que este sobre fue abierto y cerrado de nuevo con cera de un color diferente","Este paquete parece que ha sido marcado en tinta con un curioso símbolo"},
[407]={"Hay un laberinto de setos en los Campos de los Caballos durante la Plantación de Primavera en Bree, y Sorrel Nortuk quiere que hables con su hermana Ranúncula antes de lanzarte a la aventurada exploración.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Habla con Ranúncula Nortuk en los Campos de los Caballos, en Bree","'El laberinto de setos está en Bree, en los Campos de los Caballos.'","Una Hobbit entre los Setos","Ranúncula Nortuk se encuentra en los Terrenos del Festival, en Bree, disfrutando del laberinto de setos en los Campos de los Caballos.\
\
Deberías dirigirte al laberinto para transmitirle a Ranúncula los saludos de Sorrel.","¡Hola! ¡Oye, tú, joven ${RACE}! ¿Ya has visto el laberinto de setos? Parece que la mitad de quienes asisten a la Fiesta de los Campos Verdes se han ido al laberinto, en Bree. Si te encuentras allí esta primavera, deberías hablar con mi querida hermana Ranúncula, que emprendió un gran viaje para ver los setos. Siempre ha sido muy aficionada al follaje.\
\
'Parece que este año hay muchísima diversión en los Campos de los Caballos. Sé que terminarás pasando por allí antes de que acabe el festival; ¡no dejes de transmitirle mis saludos a Ranúncula mientras esté allí!'","'¡Hola! ¿Así que vienes directamente de parte de mi hermana Sorrel? Es una lástima que no haya venido ella misma a ver el laberinto; por desgracia, la distancia entre las Tierras de los Tuk y Bree es considerable, y no comparte tanto mi amor por la vegetación. Aun así, me alegra mucho que estés aquí.'"},
[408]={"Habla con el Alcalde Will Pieblanco fuera del Agujero del Agujero Municipal, en Cavada Grande","Tras un largo viaje desde las tierras del Valle de la Niebla que te condujo hasta la aldea fronteriza de Musgovilla, en la Ciénaga de los Cisnes, te has topado con un hobbit de lo más curioso. No es un hobbit ribereño de Lyndelby, ni uno de los Fuertes de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes, ni tampoco uno de sus escurridizos primos de los que se rumorea que habitan en Enedwaith: es un hobbit de una tierra llamada la Comarca.","'¡Hola, hola! ¿Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un[m]|una[f]} visitante que viene a la Comarca?\
\
'Entonces es mi deber y mi placer darte la bienvenida a nuestro gran país. Soy Will Pieblanco, Alcalde de Cavada Grande y de toda la Comarca. ¿Quién eres y de dónde procedes?'\
\
Te presentas ante el Alcalde Pieblanco, y él hace una reverencia a su vez. Le hablas de tu hogar, diciendo solo que se encuentra más allá de las Montañas Nubladas, y de tu largo viaje a través de incontables tierras que te llevó a la aldea de Musgovilla, en la Ciénaga de los Cisnes. Allí conociste a Fridolin Tuk, dices, y el Alcalde Pieblanco suelta una risita para sí.\
\
'Sería Fridolin, ¿no? Tss. ¡Siempre es un Tuk! Bueno, por mi parte, me alegra que hayas venido a visitarnos. Si tú y los tuyos son de verdad primos lejanos nuestros, ¡entonces digo que eres pariente mío! Eres ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} a permanecer en la Comarca todo el tiempo que desees, . Hay muchas villas y pueblos excelentes en la Comarca, así que te sugiero que los visites todos. Después de todo, ¡ya he oído más que suficientes quejas sobre mi supuesto favoritismo!\
\
'No obstante, estoy seguro de que la buena gente de la Comarca agradecería la ayuda de ${PLAYERNAME:un[m]|una[f]}un  de tu... estatura.'","El Alcalde Will Pieblanco puede encontrarse fuera del Agujero del Agujero Municipal en Cavada Grande, en la Comarca.\
\
A pesar de tus protestas, Fridolin Tuk cree que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un primo lejano[m]|una prima lejana[f]} y extraordinariamente ${PLAYERNAME:alto[m]|alta[f]} de los Tuk, y piensa que deberías visitar las tierras de la Comarca. Deberías hablar con el Alcalde de la Comarca, Will Pieblanco.","Un Hogar Hobbit Lejos del Hogar","'¡Vaya, vaya! Creo que ya hemos tenido más que suficiente emoción por hoy. No recuerdo haberte visto por Musgovilla, ${PLAYERNAME:viajero[m]|viajera[f]}. Aunque imagino que me habría sido difícil ver cualquier cosa mientras me escondía en el armario de alguno de estos buenos vecinos durante aquella incursión. He oído que ayudaste a poner fin a esos trasgos descomunales, y debo agradecértelo. ¿Cómo te llamas?'\
\
Te presentas, y Fridolin Tuk se presenta a su vez.\
\
'....... un nombre curioso para un hobbit de lo más curioso. Caramba, tienes un parecido notable con el viejo Bandobras Tuk —el Toro Bramador, como lo llamamos los Tuk— sí, un gran parecido en efecto, al menos en lo que a la altura se refiere. ¿Podrías ser ${PLAYERNAME:uno de mis primos perdidos[m]|una de mis primas perdidas[f]} hace mucho tiempo? ¿No? ¿Quizá seas de los Nortuk, entonces?'\
\
Le dices a Fridolin que no eres uno de los Tuk, ni un Nortuk, ni un Toro Bramador —sea lo que sea eso— ni nada por el estilo. Dices que procedes de un lugar más allá de las Montañas Nubladas, y que has viajado a Musgovilla como solo uno de los muchos destinos de un largo periplo desde tu tierra natal.\
\
'Sí, sí, todo eso está muy bien, pero aun así podrías ser ${PLAYERNAME:un[m]|una[f]} Tuk de algún tipo. ¡Ja! Bromeo, por supuesto. Incluso si no eres ${PLAYERNAME:un[m]|una[f]} Tuk, digo que eres ${PLAYERNAME:primo mío[m]|prima mía[f]}, y sería terriblemente descortés por mi parte no invitarte a visitarnos en la Comarca. Tendrás que seguir el camino hasta Bree, y luego querrás dirigirte hacia el oeste. Una vez que cruces el río Brandivino, ¡estarás en la Comarca! Ah, pero antes querrás pasar por Cavada Grande para hablar con el Alcalde, el viejo Will Pieblanco. ¡Querrá darte una bienvenida adecuada a la Comarca!\
\
'Ah, y si alguno de los Fronteros te da problemas, ¡solo diles que Fridolin te ha invitado a tomar el té!'"},
[409]={"Reúnete con Annaethel en Sírlond","'El dolor de mi madre es algo peligroso. Toma, llévate mi caballito de juguete. He atado una carta a su brida, haciéndole saber a mi madre que estoy sano y salvo.\
\
'Grethron dijo que mi madre está en las ruinas al sur de aquí, pero no me deja ir a verla. ¡Por favor! Debes encontrarla antes de que pueda atraer a más niños.'","'¡Vi una luz en el cielo! Veo tantas luces, ¡pero el rugido de esta rasgó el aire!'\
\
Informas a Annaethel que Mellanion está vivo y bien, entregándole el caballito de juguete.\
\
'¿Mellanion? ¿Mi hijo? ¡Tenía un hijo! Pero huyó. ¡No, los orcos se lo llevaron! ¡Pero este es su juguete! ¿Y dices que hay una nota en la brida?'","Habla con Annaethel una vez más","El conocimiento del regreso seguro de su hijo a Sírlond ha disipado la locura que aquejaba a Annaethel. Está volviendo al campamento y te pide que la encuentres allí.","Un caballito de juguete llamado Esperanza","El juguete y la carta de Mellanion han despejado la locura de los ojos de Annaethel. Deberías hacerle saber que su hijo está a salvo en Sírlond.\
\
Annaethel está en el centro de Cardolan, al sur de Sírlond.","'Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:extraño[m]|extraña[f]}. ¡Traes muy buenas noticias! Mucho tiempo he vagado con una oscuridad siniestra cegando mis ojos, ¡pero ahora esa luz ha pasado y mis pensamientos son míos una vez más! ¡Mi hijo está a salvo y cerca! ¿Dices que está en Sírlond? ¡Iré allí enseguida!\
\
'¡Ven y encuéntrame en Sírlond, y te recompensaré por todos tus esfuerzos!'","Annaethel ha sido vista entre las ruinas al sur de Sírlond. Deberías llevarle el caballito de juguete y su mensaje de su hijo.\
\
Sírlond está en el centro de Cardolan.","Busca a Annaethel","Ella aprieta el juguete contra su pecho","Con Mellanion de vuelta a salvo en Sírlond, la búsqueda de Annaethel debe reanudarse, no sea que atraiga a otro niño.","'Me alegro de verte, ${PLAYERNAME:estimado amigo[m]|estimada amiga[f]}. ¡Has hecho tanto por mi familia y por mí! Te doy las gracias mil veces, y no es suficiente. Por favor, toma esto junto con mi gratitud. Me devolviste a mi hijo. Me sacaste de mi locura. ¿Cómo podría recompensarte lo suficiente?'"},
[410]={"Habla con Nate Hojafrágil en la Granja de Espinar","Una guarida de lobos","Nate Hojafrágil explicó que los lobos al oeste de la Obra de los Espinar, cerca de la alta elevación de las Colinas Brandigamo, se acercan cada vez más a la granja cada noche. No permitirá que los caballos se trasladen al establo hasta que los lobos sean controlados.","'¿Cómo va tu búsqueda de esa guarida de lobos? Todavía veo muchos de esos lobos por aquí.'","'Saludos, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, ¿la señora te envió a hablar conmigo? Le he dicho una y otra vez, y también al señor Espinar, que los caballos se asustarán si los traemos con lo que ocurre aquí por la noche.\
\
'Hay lobos por todas estas tierras y tienen una guarida al oeste, donde las Colinas Brandigamo comienzan a elevarse en la distancia. Hasta que reduzcamos el número de lobos, no podemos arriesgarnos a mover los caballos aquí.\
\
'Si reducimos su número, pensaré en traer los caballos a la granja. Incluso pagaré por la ayuda que necesitamos. ¿${PLAYERNAME:interesado[m]|interesada[f]}?'","'Es bueno saber que el número de lobos se ha reducido. Aun así, estas colinas parecen estar llenas de vida salvaje que normalmente no se ve tan cerca de tierras habitadas. Debe haber algo que los tiene a todos inquietos.'","Lobos derrotados en los campos del norte de Bree (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Nate Hojafrágil está en la Granja de Espinar.\
\
Debes regresar con Nate Hojafrágil y decirle que los lobos han sido eliminados.","La guarida de lobos está al oeste de la Obra de los Espinar.\
\
Nate Hojafrágil te pidió que redujeras el número de lobos que merodean cerca de la Obra de los Espinar.","Derrota a lobos en los campos del norte de Bree (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[411]={"One of the dwarves appears to notice your approach...","You have discovered a small company of dwarves at an encampment in the foothills of Elderslade.","'Well now... what brings you to the Slade, traveller?\
\
'For my part, I am Nagli Want-kin... a free dwarf like all of the others who dwell here at Khadâsh-gâra.\
\
'Come, let us talk.'","A Home on the Slade","The dwarf encampment can be found in the foothills of eastern Elderslade.\
\
After investigating the dwarf-encampment in Elderslade, your presence has caught the attention of one of the dwarves. You should speak to Nagli Want-kin.","Discover the dwarf encampment in Elderslade","Investigate the dwarf-encampment in Elderslade","While travelling through Elderslade, you have caught a glimpse of a strange sight. There appears to be a small dwarf-encampment in Elderslade, nestled in the foothills along the Greylin.\
\
None of your maps have such a location marked on them, and it appears to have been built much more recently than any of the ruins that remain in Elderslade.\
\
You should investigate the dwarf-encampment and attempt to learn why these dwarves have settled in Elderslade and so near to Mount Gundabad.","Nestled in the foothills along the Greylin, a curious company of dwarves has built a small encampment in Elderslade.","You have discovered a small company of dwarves at an encampment in the foothills of Elderslade. You should investigate the encampment and learn why these dwarves have settled in Elderslade.","Talk to Nagli Want-kin"},
[412]={"Busca al oeste más huellas","'Creo que las huellas llevan al noroeste.'","Habla con Bingo en Arboleda del Paso","'¡Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}!'","Al norte de Puente de los Tejones, mientras buscabas a Bingo y Crinloca, encontraste a Hunfredo Rebuscón.","Encuentras varias huellas del tamaño de un poney que llevan hacia el oeste","El rastro de Crinloca lleva hacia el oeste del lugar donde te atacó el Nazgûl, adentrándose en los Valles de Piedra.","'Hmm... todavía no veo buenas huellas, pero seguiré buscando.'","Habla con Hunfredo Rebuscón al norte de Puente de los Tejones","Egwylf te pidió buscar señales del paso de Crinloca cerca del lugar donde atacó el Nazgûl.","Willem Bigote parece haber captado el rastro y corrió cuesta arriba hacia un poblado en las alturas del sudoeste de los Valles de Piedra: Arboleda del Paso.","'¿Encontraste huellas hacia el oeste? ¡Debemos seguirlas enseguida!'","'¡Creo que Willem ha captado el rastro! ¡Corrió cuesta arriba! ¿Hay algún poblado por esa zona? Podría ser que Crinloca llevara a Bingo a uno... ¡esperemos que así sea!'","'Buscaré nuevas huellas.'","'Hay algunas huellas aquí, pero están muy borrosas.'","'¡Ah, hola de nuevo, ${CLASS}! Parece como si hubiese sido ayer cuando te encontré en las tierras nevadas de las Tierras Feroces, pero allí los negocios iban mal. Estoy llevando mis mercancías al sur en busca de un mercado más dispuesto. Voy hacia el Paso de Rohan. Puedes acompañarme si quieres.\
\
'¿No? ¡Tú te lo pierdes! Te deseo buena suerte, pero debo encontrar clientes para mis maravillosas mercancías, ¡y aquí no hay ninguno!\
\
'¿Un poney? Quizá vi uno apresurándose hacia el oeste, pero no le presté mucha atención. ¡Que tengas buen día, ${CLASS}!'","'¡Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}!'","El suelo está ennegrecido y humeante donde te encontraste con el Nazgûl","'Deberíamos volver al lugar donde fuimos atacados por esa criatura antinatural. Si examino el suelo allí, podría seguir su rastro. Vayamos al sureste enseguida. Si recuerdo bien, estaba en los Campos Amplios, justo al suroeste del asentamiento invadido de Bardh-dorám.\
\
'Los encontraremos pronto. ¡No te preocupes!'","Egwylf está buscando señales del paso de Crinloca en los Campos Amplios, donde atacó el Nazgûl.","Vuelve al lugar del ataque del Nazgûl, en los Campos Amplios","Busca a Bingo siguiendo una línea recta hacia el oeste desde el lugar donde atacó el Nazgûl","Egwylf está en el camino al norte de Puente de los Tejones, buscando huellas.","'Puede que haya visto un poney al oeste de aquí. Estaba oscuro y no puedo estar seguro, ¡aunque mis ojos son los mejores de toda la región! ¡Si yo no estoy seguro, nadie lo estaría!'","Habla con Egwylf cerca del lugar del ataque del Nazgûl","'Hmm... aún no veo ninguna huella útil, pero seguiré buscando. Tú también deberías examinar el suelo en busca de huellas de poney, ${PLAYER}. Puede que Crinloca haya dejado alguna pista sobre dónde llevó a Bingo.'","Las huellas están revueltas, pero Willem corre cuesta arriba hacia un poblado del sudoeste","Egwylf quiere regresar al lugar donde te separaste de Bingo y Crinloca. Fue al sureste de la Colina Boscosa, en los Campos Amplios, justo al suroeste del asentamiento invadido de Bardh-dorám.","Bingo y Crinloca llegaron a Arboleda del Paso, en los Valles de Piedra, y ahora te has reunido con ellos.","Busca a Bingo y a Crinloca en Arboleda del Paso","Un hombre de aspecto familiar te saluda al acercarte","'¡Oh, qué alegría verte, ${PLAYER}! ¡Y estoy muy orgulloso de Willem Bigote! ¡Qué buen chico y qué buen rastreador! Podrías enseñarle una o dos cosas a Egwylf sobre cómo encontrar a los perdidos, ¿verdad, W.B.?'\
\
Bingo ríe alegremente, pero una sombra cruza su rostro.\
\
'Esa era una criatura muy aterradora, . ¡Nunca vi algo así! Qué bueno que Crinloca me llevara lejos tan rápido. ¡Y me alegra que tú también hayas escapado ${PLAYER:ileso[m]|ilesa[f]} de esa aparición! Espero que no nos encontremos con más cosas como esa. Antes yo tenía miedo de los caballos, pero ya no... ¡no si existen criaturas aladas tan terribles como esa! ¡Cuesta creerlo!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Siguiente semana: 'Pensamientos del Hogar' (Nivel recomendado: 93)</rgb>","'Necesitamos encontrar hacia dónde huyeron Crinloca y Bingo, ${PLAYER}. Para lograrlo, debemos volver al lugar donde fuimos atacados por esa criatura antinatural. Si puedo examinar el suelo allí, quizá pueda encontrar su rastro. Vayamos de inmediato hacia el sureste. Si recuerdo bien, el lugar estaba en los Campos Amplios, justo al suroeste del asentamiento invadido de Bardh-dorám.\
\
'Los encontraremos antes de que te des cuenta. ¡Deja de preocuparte!'","'¿Un poney? Quizá vi uno apresurándose hacia el oeste, pero no le presté mucha atención. ¡Que tengas un buen día, ${CLASS}!'","'No logro entender estas huellas revueltas, ${PLAYER}. ¡Bingo y Crinloca podrían haber ido a cualquier parte!'","Crinloca está bajo un árbol cargado de manzanas, masticando satisfecho","Las huellas llevan hacia algún punto al oeste de la carretera a Puente de los Tejones, donde encontraste a Hunfredo Rebuscón rumbo al Paso de Rohan.","'Tú también deberías examinar el suelo en busca de huellas de poney, ${PLAYER}. Puede que Crinloca haya dejado alguna pista sobre dónde llevó a Bingo.'","Estas huellas no son claras, pero creo que continúan hacia el oeste. Creo que Crinloca llevó a Bingo por allí.'","Busca huellas de Crinloca cerca del lugar donde atacó el Nazgûl","Egwylf quiere intentar encontrar hacia dónde huyeron Crinloca y Bingo tras el ataque del Nazgûl.","Un caballo en un pajar"},
[413]={"'It seems to be settled then. I will be the most devoted of students, if only this Wose can teach me how to keep my horse! And I shall consider you a bearer of good fortune, ${PLAYER}. Every time you arrive, my poor luck turns to good!'","Lead Witherbreca back","'You got her back unharmed. Do the wonders never end? Well, let us get on with this Wose's bargain, shall we?'","'No horse, and the poor lad looks scared out of his wits!'","Sithgar's horse has run off again - this time into the Drúadan Forest.","Talk to Bhis-weni-Mâr","Return to defend Witherbreca","Find Witherbreca","'There you are, ${PLAYER}. Do not laugh at me, but my luck is as bad as ever. No sooner was I back among my Éored when Witherbreca ran off again. But now we are not among the pleasant grass-hills, we are in a forest! I'm sure the poor animal has been eaten by a bear.'","Search for Witherbreca deep in the Drúadan Forest.","Bhis-weni-Mâr looks at you with sad and frightened eyes. \
\
'Horse. Run.'\
\
He gestures off deeper into the woods.\
\
'Bad Ghûrdhos come. Horse run. You help?'","'Horse,' the Wose says, looking up with kindly eyes at the great animal, 'friend.'\
\
Through a series of short words and gestures, you make the Wose understand that you want to lead the horse back to its owner, although it is not clear that the 'owner' part is especially clear.\
\
The Wose folds his arms across his chest.\
\
'Shield. Bhis-weni-Mâr want shield. Good-bye horse.'\
\
Could it be that he wants to trade a Rohirric shield for the horse?","You should return to Bhis-weni-Mâr with Sithgar, and help negotiate the trade of a shield for the wayward horse.","A Horse in the Forest","'Ghûrdhos come. Horse run.'","Talk to Sithgar","Defeat the wood-trolls","'What is a Ghûrdhos? These woods are surely full of monsters and sorcery!'","Search for Witherbreca, who has run off into the Drúadan Wood.","Return to Sithgar","There is the horse, and she is surrounded by wood-trolls!","You discover Witherbreca standing close to a Wose","Now that you have defeated the wood-trolls, you should lead Witherbreca back to Sithgar and Bhis-weni-Mâr.","Defeat the wood-trolls surrounding Witherbreca in the Drúadan Forest.","'You found my steed - and it has befriended one of these... Wose-men, you say? Well, it sounds as if he was faring better at soothing the horse than I! Ha ha.'\
\
You explain that the Bhis-weni-Mâr seemed to want to trade a shield for the horse.\
\
'I - I cannot do that, ${PLAYER}. I would be punished, and not lightly....'\
\
He sighs.\
\
'Still, I would take the punishment if it meant I could ride with the host. Let us go and meet this Wose horse-friend.'","Talk to the Wose","You should talk to the Wose standing by Witherbreca in the Drúadan Forest.","You led the frightened horse back through the forest","'I have once more lost all hope, ${PLAYER}. My horse has run off into the forest, and I will be left behind once again!'","Sithgar stands in the Drúadan Forest, by Witherbreca and Bhis-weni-Mâr.\
\
You should talk to Sithgar and hear what he has to say.","You should talk to Bhis-weni-Mâr now that he, Witherbreca, and Sithgar are together in the Drúadan Forest.","Bhis-weni-Mâr looks both very serious and very sad.\
\
'No shield. Horse-man keep shield. Horse and forest... do not go... as one. Horse is good. Very good horse. Only must be calm. Must calm horse. Or horse run.'\
\
Bhis-weni-Mâr fixes his eyes on Sithgar, and through a sequence of words and gestures, makes it clear that he wishes to teach Sithgar how to calm and command Witherbreca, before he lets her go.","'Horse is good. I will show rider how friend to make with it.'","You should return to Sithgar in the Rohirrim bivouac, in Taur Drúadan, and tell him of the horse and the Wose."},
[414]={"Talk to Éorpwald outside of Thornhope","'Ah... I am satisfied then. You have my gratitude, ${PLAYER}.'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! I did not... have the time to properly thank you... for your assistance.\
\
'The affront against my Thane and my people is unforgiveable. Many died -- men, women, children, young and old alike -- butchered... by the Orcs. There were three of the creatures in particular that I would see slaughtered where they stand. They deserve no less.\
\
'These three -- Bidroi, Grish, and Rûkaz -- murdered Thane Wulfrad's family... and would have slain Béortnoth as well, had the giant not come and saved him. Aye, Béortnoth is not as mad as he seems.\
\
'Would you enter Thornhope and bring these three devils to justice?'","Derrota a Bidroi","You rescued Éorpwald, a wounded Rohirrim warrior, from Thornhope and helped him reach the relative safety of Béortnoth's camp.","Bidroi, Grish, and Rûkaz can all be found within the walls of Thornhope.\
\
Éorpwald asked you to take revenge upon Bidroi, Grish, and Rûkaz, three lieutenants of the invading forces, on behalf of Thane Wulfrad's family.","Éorpwald is encamped outside the walls of Thornhope.\
\
You should return to Éorpwald with news of your victory.","Bidroi derrotado","A Horse-lord's Revenge","Defeat Grish","Defeated Rûkaz","Defeated Grish","Defeat Rûkaz"},
[415]={"'He dibujado un mapa rápido con algunas de las vistas más notables de Rivendel. ¡Encontrad cada una de estas localizaciones y habréis visto algunos de los lugares más bellos del valle!'","Elrond te ha sugerido que presentes a Bingo Boffin a Bilbo Bolsón en el Salón del Fuego.","El rugido de las cataratas es ensordecedor, pero la vista es preciosa","Encuentra Imdolen en el camino al norte de Rivendel","'¡Siempre es un placer ver a un hobbit fuera de la Comarca, ${PLAYER}! Bingo parece ser un individuo interesante, ¡y me alegra verle probando sus límites!\
\
'He dibujado un mapa rápido con algunas de las vistas más notables de Rivendel. ¡Encontrad cada una de estas localizaciones y habréis visto algunos de los lugares más bellos del valle! Si tuviera más tiempo podría hacer un mapa más decente, pero es lo que he podido hacer con las prisas. ¡Ve, antes de que Bingo pierda su afán por explorar y vivir aventuras! ¡Es el miedo que tengo con todos los hobbits: que las ansias de aventura se marchen tan rápido como llegaron!'","Bingo Boffin está en el Salón del Fuego, conversando alegremente con Bilbo Bolsón.","Encuentra el Refugio de Orladion","'Deberías presentarle a este Bingo Boffin a Bilbo Bolsón, en el Salón del Fuego. Deben tener mucho en común; a pesar de mis bromas, los hobbits siguen siendo algo inusual de ver en Imladris.'","'Deberías presentarte ante el gran Elfo y decirle que hemos venido a hacerle una breve visita. No he oído hablar sobre la hospitalidad de los Elfos, ¡pero seguro que no carecen de ella! No nos cerrará la puerta, eso seguro.'","El lago de Hidhuinen es apacible y calmado","Encuentra las cascadas de Imladris en el puente sureste","'¡Mira quién es, ${PLAYER}! ¡Es Bilbo Bolsón, el famoso aventurero de Hobbiton! Le he estado poniendo al día de las noticias de la Comarca, ¡y él me ha estado hablando sobre su estancia con los Elfos de Rivendel!'\
\
Bingo te mira con aire conspirados y murmura rápidamente: 'Me parece un tipo ordinario, ¡y para nada un loco!' antes de continuar con tono normal.\
\
'Bilbo ha tenido la formidable idea de dibujarme un mapa para explorar mejor Rivendel y no perderme nada. ¡Es fantástico!'","Encuentra el mercado de Rivendel","'¿Podría ser que hayamos encontrado al mismo hobbit que dibujó el mapa que encontré en ese libro de cocina?'","Encuentra el lago de Hidhuinen","Bilbo está en el Salón del Fuego, en la Última Morada.\
\
Bingo se ha percatado de que el mapa de Rivendel dibujado por Bilbo tiene cierto parecido con el mapa que encontró en la Comarca.","Has encontrado a Bingo y Bilbo ya en plena conversación","'¿Más invitados? Esto es lo que pasa cuando permites que un hobbit se instale en tu hogar, ${PLAYER}: ¡no tardan en llegar más! No le diré a Bingo que se vaya, mientras sea un invitado educado y decente.\
\
'Deberías presentarle a Bilbo Bolsón, en el Salón del Fuego. Deben tener mucho en común; a pesar de mis bromas, los hobbits siguen siendo algo inusual de ver en Imladris.'","Habla con Bilbo en el Salón del Fuego","'Estoy emocionado por explorar el valle escondido de Rivendel, ¡pero mi estómago está rugiendo! Los Elfos deben tener un comedor o almacén para sus comidas. ¡Voy ir con W.B. en busca de algo que podamos comer!\
\
'Deberías presentarte ante el gran Elfo y decirle que hemos venido a hacerle una breve visita. No he oído hablar sobre la hospitalidad de los Elfos, ¡pero seguro que no carecen de ella! No nos cerrará la puerta, eso seguro.'","Esta aguja sirve como un popular lugar de reunión para la gente de Rivendel","'Ha sido muy divertido, ¡y en cada lugar me maravillaba de nuevo con la belleza tan pura de Rivendel! Espero que no fuéramos una molestia para los Elfos que viven aquí, ¡ya que a veces me quedaba embobado y tenía que retenerme para no darle a la lengua!\
\
'Gracias de nuevo por encargarte del mapa, ya que yo era incapaz de mantener mis ojos apartados del paisaje en vez de mirarlo. Es un mapa bastante bien dibujado, ahora que lo miro más de cerca.'\
\
Bingo para de hablar y coge el mapa.\
\
'Espera un momento, ${PLAYER}... ¡hay algo muy característico en este mapa! ¿Ves cómo el artista ha usado estas líneas de aquí para dar forma a las montañas? ¡Me es muy familiar, ya que las montañas de mi mapa están dibujadas de la misma manera! Recuerdas el mapa, ¿verdad? ¡Es el mapa por el que comencé mi aventura, hace ya tanto! ¿Podría ser que hayamos encontrado al hobbit que dibujó el mapa que encontré en el libro de recetas?'","Muchas mercancías de calidad se venden en el mercado de Rivendel","'Ah, ¿querías decirme que Bingo encontró mi mapa de Eriador? ¡Me alegra mucho, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Antes de dejar la Comarca, pasé algo de tiempo visitando mis rincones favoritos para grabarlos en mi memoria. Incluso ahora, puedo ver muchos de mis senderos soleados favoritos y mis bancos más tranquilos donde descansar. Pero algo trajo la tristeza a mi corazón: el que ninguno de los queridos hobbits que estaba dejando atrás no experimentaría nunca las mismas alegrías que yo al explorar el mundo. Oh, supe que Frodo estaría bien; siempre ha sido un chico con ganas de aventura, pero eso era algo inusual.\
\
'Concebí un plan, ${PLAYER}. Dibujaría un mapa del ancho mundo, y lo dejaría en un libro de recetas en la biblioteca de Alforzaburgo. Quizás lo encontraría un hobbit curioso, o alguno que solo necesitara un pequeño empujoncito para embarcarse en una gran aventura.\
\
'¡Y mira! ¡Tenía razón! ¡Gandalf estaría muy orgulloso de mi inventiza, ${PLAYER}! Espero, por el bien de Bingo, que no haya dragones involucrados, como pasó conmigo. Me sentiría responsable si fuera así, ¡aunque por ahora me parece una aventurilla y una alegría!'","'Antes de dejar la Comarca, pasé algo de tiempo visitando mis rincones favoritos para grabarlos en mi memoria. Incluso ahora, puedo ver muchos de mis senderos soleados favoritos y mis bancos más tranquilos donde descansar. Pero algo trajo la tristeza a mi corazón: el que ninguno de los queridos hobbits que estaba dejando atrás no experimentaría nunca las mismas alegrías que yo al explorar el mundo. Oh, supe que Frodo estaría bien; siempre ha sido un chico con ganas de aventura, pero eso era algo inusual.\
\
'Concebí un plan, ${PLAYER}. Dibujaría un mapa del ancho mundo, y lo dejaría en un libro de recetas en la biblioteca de Alforzaburgo. Quizás lo encontraría un hobbit curioso, o alguno que solo necesitara un pequeño empujoncito para embarcarse en una gran aventura.\
\
'¡Y mira! ¡Tenía razón! ¡Gandalf estaría muy orgulloso de mi inventiza, ${PLAYER}! Espero, por el bien de Bingo, que no haya dragones involucrados, como pasó conmigo. Me sentiría responsable si fuera así, ¡aunque por ahora me parece una aventurilla y una alegría!'","El Refugio de Orladion es silencioso y apacible","Habla con Elrond en su biblioteca, en la Última Morada","Encuentra a Bilbo Bolsón en el Salón del Fuego","Habla con Bingo en el Salón del Fuego","El aire de Imdolen, en lo alto de Rivendel, es puro y fresco","Bilbo os ha proporcionado a Bingo y a ti con un mapa de localizaciones importantes de Rivendel.","Bingo y tú habéis explorado varias de las vistas más notables de Rivendel, y ahora deberíais volver al Salón del Fuego, en la Última Morada.","'Apenas puedo creerlo, ${PLAYER}. Bilbo Bolsón, el gran autor y aventurero, ¡es el responsable de que me embarcara en este gran viaje! Tengo muchas cosas que preguntarle, ¡tanto sobre sus aventuras como sobre sus escritos!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La semana que viene: 'Notas del autor' (Nivel recomendado: 40)</rgb>","'¡Mira quién está aquí!'","Habla con Bilbo en el Salón del Fuego, en la Última Morada","Encuentra la Aguja del Encuentro","Bingo y tú habéis llegado al valle escondido de Rivendel, y el hobbit está emocionado por empezar a explorar.","Devuelve el mapa a Bingo en el Salón del Fuego, en la Última Morada","Bilbo Bolsón está en el Salón del Fuego, en la Última Morada.","Bingo está en el Salón del Fuego, en la Última Morada.\
\
Has averiguado que Bilbo Bolsón es el responsable de haber dibujado el mapa que fue dejado en el libro de recetas que provocó que Bingo comenzara su aventura.","'Bilbo ha tenido la formidable idea de dibujarme un mapa para explorar mejor Rivendel y no perderme nada. ¡Es fantástico!'","Elrond está en su biblioteca en la Última Morada, en Rivendel.\
\
Bingo ha ido a buscar algo de comida para W.B. y para él, y te ha encomendado la tarea de decirle a Elrond que otro hobbit ha llegado a Rivendel.","Un hogar hospitalario"},
[416]={"A House Divided","'Hold a moment, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'You surely saw as I did that some among the Stout-axes seemed unsettled by the King's command that we be cast out from the Spire. What will become of them? Shall they be met now with threats and curses? Perhaps they shall even be unfairly marked as traitors!\
\
'I cannot speak for King Dáin, but I would offer the Stout-axes a new home among my folk. We shall have need of hardy dwarves now that Sauron has fallen!\
\
'If you find any who still name themselves Stout-axes in the Oath-taker's Horn, aid them and offer them my promise that they shall find refuge in the halls of Durin's Folk.'","You have freed many of the intimidated Stout-axes from the Oath-taker's Horn.","Rescued intimidated Stout-axes from the Oath-taker's Horn (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Intimidated Stout-axes can be found throughout the Oath-taker's Horn.\
\
Gimli has asked you to rescue any of the Stout-axes that do not wish to follow King Greytooth in his quest to recover the dwarf-rings and offer them a new home as part of Durin's Folk.","It remains uncertain if all the dwarves within the Oath-taker's Horn wish to follow King Greytooth in his quest to recover the dwarf-rings, but Gimli holds hope that a few might instead wish to ally with Durin's Folk.","You have done well to free the Stout-axes from the Oath-taker's Horn. It is likely that King Váskmun Greytooth will lead the Firehorns to ruin in his search for the dwarf-rings.\
\
Instead, you have offered the few remaining Stout-axes a new chance at freedom among Durin's Folk.","Completado","Rescue intimidated Stout-axes from the Oath-taker's Horn (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[417]={"Talk to Spakorth on the plains of Dor Amarth outside Lûghash","'I am ashamed that I could not resist Zôreth, ${PLAYER}! I am ashamed that I could not even sense her deception—that she could spy upon the Stout-axes through my very eyes and work our ruin!\
\
'I have failed you and I have failed Gimli. Leave me if you wish—it is the fate I deserve!'\
\
Spakorth notices that you make no effort to leave, and smiles weakly.\
\
'What sort of dwarf is so easily swayed by the power of evil? I suppose that is a foolish question to ask now....\
\
'Zôreth may have planned to use me in her search of the Rings of Power, but now King Váskmun has forsaken us all for Manthríf!\
\
'If this is the way of the Firehorns, I want no part in it!'","Spakorth can be found along the causeway outside Lûghash.\
\
You have been cast out of Lûghash by King Greytooth and the Firehorns. You should speak to Spakorth.","Overjoyed by the return of their King, Váskmun Greytooth, the Stout-axes of Lûghash have asked you and Gimli to share your tales of valour among the Free Peoples that they might learn more of the world beyond Mordor.","'Tales of valour, eh? I think we have a few we could tell.... Hah!\
\
'Let's get on with it then!'","A House Forged Anew","Gimli can be found on the central level of Lûghash.\
\
King Váskmun Greytooth desires to hear Gimli's tales of valour. You should join Gimli in recounting your adventures in Middle-earth.","'This is a day of celebration, indeed! My people are united once more, and today we cast off the shackles by which Sauron himself bound us!\
\
'You and Gimli have done my people a great honour, and one that shall not soon be forgotten by my folk.\
\
'As a dwarf of the eastern mountains, I have always wished to learn more of the west. Ah, but such things could not be asked of the Dark Lord! I know not the reasons why, but Sauron was not over fond of dwarves, you see!\
\
'But, such questions can be asked now! How came you to Mordor, ${PLAYER}? What trials have you and Gimli faced and overcome?\
\
'Let us hear your tales of valour!'","Talk to Gimli in Lûghash"},
[419]={"Talk to Adalmód at the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Adalmód informed you that Reeve Ingbert and his son were closeted in discussion.","Assist Botulf with Reassuring Words","Assisted Goldwine with Preparing for the Siege","Assist Pedwin with Courage from a Keg","Adalmód stands guard at the entrance to the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should return to Adalmód now that you have done as he asked.","A House in Turmoil","Guards may be found throughout Eaworth.\
\
Adalmód has asked you to help the guards of Eaworth prepare for the coming siege.","Assisted Botulf with Reassuring Words","'You come from Faldham, seeking an audience with Reeve Ingbert? You have come at an inopportune time, ${CLASS}. Dark days are upon us, and the Reeve is wary of strangers.\
\
'As well, he is closeted in discussion with his son, Lord Ingmar. We expect to fall under siege by Orcs at any time, and they debate the best strategy to deal with them.\
\
'If you desire to help -- and perhaps to prove your friendship to Eaworth -- you may put your talents to use aiding with our siege-preparations. Many of our guards are overtasked and in need of assistance.'","'You have shown courage and kindness in your efforts, ${PLAYER}, but I still cannot allow you to pass.'","Assisted Pedwin with Courage from a Keg","Assist Goldwine with Preparing for the Siege","Assisted Offram with A City Under Siege","Assist Offram with A City Under Siege"},
[420]={"'Tú... he sido... ¡atacado por los Gauredain! Criaturas terribles...\
\
'Recoge mi bolsa... llévala... Ost Forod...'","Encuentra a Nat Rapkins","'Si el viejo Nat está en problemas, le encontrarás cerca de los Saltos del Crepúsculo en el extremo norte del lago. Ve hacia el noroeste de Ost Forod y cruza las aguas en su extremo norte, pero ten cuidado con el mal de donde proviniese ese terrible aullido... oírlo me heló la sangre.'","'Un cazador llamado Nat Rapkins a veces viaja lejos hacia el noroeste, cruzando las frías aguas de los Saltos del Crepúsculo que alimentan el lago, y caza por Emyn Uial. Nat conoce los bosques como la palma de su mano y debería haber vuelto. Su familia está muy preocupada.\
\
'No quería decirles nada, pero escuché un aullido terrible cerca de la costa la noche pasada. Se me había olvidado con todos nuestros quehaceres contra los saqueadores de tumbas, pero ahora me pregunto si esos aterradores aullidos tenían algo que ver con el pobre Nat.\
'Si pudieras ir hacia el noroeste, hasta el extremo norte del lago y cruzar los Saltos del Crepúsulo para buscar a Nat Rapkins, lo apreciaría mucho. Hace demasiado tiempo no aparece, y temo el fin que haya podido encontrar. Seguro que no ha perdido de vista el lago, si estaba en condiciones de hacerlo, así que no te alejes mucho de la orilla.'","'¡Debemos hacer algo con los Gauredain, ${PLAYER}!'","'¿Has encontrado a Nat?'","'Pobre Nat. Era un buen hombre.'","Nat Rapkins cruzó los Saltos del Crepúsulo en el extremo norte del lago, al noroeste de Ost Forod, y nunca volvió. Robin Sotopardo quiere que busques por el extremo del lago cerca de los Saltos del Crepúsulo al cazador desaparecido.\
\
Robin Sotopardo oyó un aullido aterrador cerca de la costa por la noche y está preocupado de que Nat Rapkins haya caído ante alguna bestia malvada. Quiere que intentes encontrar al cazador perdido.","'Temía que volvieses con estas noticias, ${PLAYER}. Nat era un buen cazador, querido por la gente de aquí, y le echaremos de menos. Devolveré la bolsa a su familia y les daré esta triste noticia.\
\
'¿Dices que habló de los Gauredain? Sí, es lo que temía. Siempre han sido un peligro para aquellos que frecuentan Emyn Uial, pero han pasado muchos años desde que no se mostraban tan atrevidos. Tenemos que hacer algo, ${PLAYER}.'","Robin Sotopardo te ha dicho que la gente de Ost Forod está preocupado por uno de los suyos, un cazador llamado Nat Rapkins, queien no ha vuelto de una cacería en el este de Emyn Uial.","Robin Sotopardo está en Ost Forod, al sureste de los Saltos del Crepúsulo, en la región de Tyrn Fornech de Evendim.\
\
Nat Rapkins te mencionó a los Gauredain en su último aliento y te dio su bolsa para que la devolvieras a Ost Forod. Debes llevarla a Robin Sotopardo.","Un aullido en las colinas","Lleva la mochila de Nat Rapkins a Robin Sotopardo"},
[421]={"Un aullido en el viento","Además del campamento orco de Ashúrz Maufulug, los exploradores elfos han descubierto unas perreras con huargos y sus cuidadores trasgos no muy lejos hacia el este de la fortaleza de los orcos.","'¿Había demasiados huargos como para destruirlos por completo? Es una lástima, ya que no podemos esperar atacar con éxito Ashúrz Maufulug con esas bestias rondando.'","Derrota a los huargos Taughâsh en Maudhul-ulur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${PLAYER}, estoy segura de que sabes que hay unas perreras de huargos, atendidas por varios trasgos, no muy lejos al este de Ashúrz Maufulug. Maudhul-ulur es como la llama el Enemigo.\
\
'Este campamento es con total seguridad de donde vienen los huargos que rondan las costas de los Lindes Oscuros, y es una amenaza de la que debemos encargarnos cuanto antes. Necesito que entres en Maudhul-ulur y derrotes tantos huargos como puedas.\
\
'Cuando hayas completado esta tarea, vuelve a verme.'","Huargo Taughâsh derrotado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Goldínwen está en Echad Glamodúd, al norte de Maudhul-ulur.\
\
Deberísa volver a ver a Goldínwen con la noticia de que has derrotado a un buen número de huargos en Maudhul-ulur.","Habla con Goldílwen en Echad Glamodúd","Los huargos se encuentran en Maudhul-ulur, al sur de Echad Glamodúd.\
\
Goldínwen te ha pedido que derrotes a un buen número de huargos en las perreras cercanas.","'¿No has eliminado a los huargos de Maudhul-ulur? Esa es una mala noticia... vuelve a verme cuando hayas completado esta tarea.'"},
[422]={"Culhuc está esperando oír tu opinión sobre su plato.\
\
Habla con Culhuc en Lhan Garan.","Estaba delicioso pero... algo duro","A Culhuc le gustaría que pruebes su plato más reciente.","'¿Sabroso pero un poco difícil de masticar? Yo también lo pensé. Estoy seguro de que mi próximo intento dará mejores resultados. ¡Me alegra haberte pedido que reunieras tanta carne!'","'¡Preparé un asado sencillo para ti! Al fin y al cabo, fuiste tú quien consiguió la carne para mí. Me gustaría oír qué te pareció el plato.'","Culhuc está en Lhan Garan, cerca del horno junto al sendero del paseo ribereño.\
\
Prueba el asado junto a Culhuc en Lhan Garan.","Prueba el avanc asado","Habla con Culhuc","Un Asado Humilde"},
[423]={"Talk to Hárskor at Hadhodiant","'So you return, outsider! I feared the Orcs would get the better of you, but I know now why Grimbeorn sent you on this errand.\
\
'I hope these provisions will be enough to keep the people of Hultvís from starvation. Once I return to the lodge, I will tell Grimbeorn what has happened and see that more provisions are sent to Hultvís. And in that time, let Durbkhat think on his cowardice. What he has done will not go unanswered by the line of Beorn!\
\
'Deliver what you have found to Ríkmar, outsider, and offer my apologies to the people of Hultvís.'","With sudden agility, Durbkhat rushes past you and flees Fil Sulmog!","Sealed provisions can be found at Fil Sulmog.\
\
Hárskor has asked you to salvage any sealed provisions you can find at Fil Sulmog.","A harsh voice echoes through the air as a large Orc rushes forth!","A Hunger for Vengeance","After being waylaid on the road to Hultvís, Hárskor unwittingly discovered a cunning plot devised by the leader of the Orcs seeking shelter in Woodsedge.","'Answer!'\
\
Hárskor is noticeably exhausted, but his stature is no less imposing. You sheathe your weapons and explain that you followed Hárskor's path at the behest of Grimbeorn, and that you encountered a number of Orcs in the woods who had laid traps in the form of the stolen provisions.\
\
'Indeed, there are Orcs in the hills, outsider, and they are an unusually cunning sort. I was waylaid on the road, and before I could overpower them I was rendered unconscious. When I awoke, I realized I had been borne away to a cave in the hills. In the darkness, I spied some of the Orcs feasting upon my horses. Deeper in the cave, I heard others prepare a fire and they shouted and cheered for a feast of Man-flesh. My senses returned, I rose from the ground in anger and changed my skin. All at once, the Orcs seemed to discover that they had not captured one of the Woodmen as they had thought. It was a mistake the survivors will not soon forget!\
\
'Yes, before I fled the caves I slew a few of their number... but I was forced to abandon what remained of the provisions. The Orcs appear to answer to one called Durbkhat, if such nonsense is even a name in their tongue! I think without him these Orcs would not seem so clever!\
\
'Slay him, outsider, and recover what he has stolen from us!'","Find and defeat Durbkhat at Fil Sulmog","Durbkhat can be found in the depths of the cave at Fil Sulmog.\
\
Determined to avenge the hurts done to the Beornings and Woodmen, Hárskor has asked you to find and defeat Durbkhat, a large Orc leading the Shapag-hai in Woodsedge.","Salvage sealed provisions from Fil Sulmog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Did you find Hárskor? What of the provisions?'\
\
You inform Ríkmar that Hárskor was waylaid by Orcs on the road to Hultvís, but he escaped his would-be captors. You also explain that while most of the provisions were tainted or spoiled, you did manage to recover a few crates and Grimbeorn will soon know to send more to Hultvís.\
\
'Oh, thank you! Our need is great, but this is more than enough for now, ${PLAYER}. I will see to it that none in Hultvís go hungry tonight!'\
\
Ríkmar shuffles uncomfortably for a moment, but seems to steady himself.\
\
'Ah, but I must admit, those Orcs sound more cunning than most! If we were meant to become their unwitting meals, I'm glad they've been driven out of our lands. Let the skin-changers and Elves see to them, I think!'","Hárskor can be found in the eastern ruins of Hadhodiant.\
\
You have driven Durbkhat from Fil Sulmog and salvaged a great deal of provisions. You should return to Hadhodiant and deliver the provisions to Hárskor.","Ríkmar can be found in Hultvís.\
\
Hárskor has returned to the Beorning-lands to prepare a new shipment of provisions for Hultvís. You should deliver the provisions you salvaged from Fil Sulmog to Ríkmar and assure him that the Beornings will deliver more provisions in the coming days.","Deliver the sealed provisions to Ríkmar in Hultvís","Salvaged sealed provisions from Fil Sulmog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[424]={"You have destroyed many Orkish provisions at Bagûd-mekhem.","Orkish provisions can be found at Bagûd-mekhem.\
\
It appears that Gorgar has ordered that provisions be brought to Bagûd-mekhem in an attempt to draw out the War of Three Peaks. You should destroy Orkish provisions at Bagûd-mekhem.","Destroyed Orkish provisions at Bagûd-mekhem (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Determined to outlast even the most concerted assaults of the Gabil'akkâ, Gorgar has ordered provisions be brought forth from the depths of Gundabad to maintain his hold on Bagûd-mekhem.","Destroy Orkish provisions at Bagûd-mekhem (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","You have destroyed many Orkish provisions at Bagûd-mekhem, depriving Gorgar's forces of much-needed rations during the War of Three Peaks.","Determined to outlast even the most concerted assaults of the Gabil'akkâ, Gorgar has ordered provisions be brought forth from the depths of Gundabad. In addition to aiding his forces in maintaining their hold on Bagûd-mekhem, it seems Gorgar intends to draw out the War of Three Peaks.\
\
You should destroy these Orkish provisions and put an end to Gorgar's plot.","A Hunger for War"},
[425]={"You have discovered a bucket full of fish","Langar is afraid his pet cat will starve if food cannot be provided.","Deliver food to Langar's cat and avoid Garsfeld guards","'Oh, thank you, thank you! I cannot tell you how much this means to me. The guards look at me as though I am crazy, but you... you trusted in the importance of my request! I fear what would have happened had you not aided me.\
\
'Here, take this... you deserve it for such a kind deed.'","'¡Te han visto!'","Delivered food to Langar's cat","Talk to Langar","'Hail! You came to speak with me? You have already done more than the others, as sad as it is to say. These are hard times, aye, but surely we can spare rations for my cat. Do they expect me to let him starve?\
\
'If you would, grab some rations for me from near the Mead Hall. The guards are not keen on allowing rations for animals -- aside from the horses of course -- so they might get in your way. Best to avoid them if you can, I think.\
\
'I will be waiting... and please, this would mean so much to me. You will be rewarded in kind.'","Langar can be found in west Garsfeld.\
\
You should speak with Langar about the task he set for you.","The food can likely be found near the Mead Hall of Garsfeld.\
\
Langar has asked that you find food for his cat in Garsfeld. However, he worries that the guards will not take kindly to giving rations to a pet.","A Hungry Inhabitant","Rations can be found outside the mead-hall.\
\
Langar wants you to sneak a ration for his beloved pet without being caught.","Find food for Langar's cat"},
[428]={"Gytha Lainey está en el Campamento de Adso, en las Tierras de Bree, en el camino entre la ciudad de Bree y Los Gamos.\
\
Gytha Lainey está esperando para hablar contigo sobre tu defensa de la aldea de Sobrecolina.","'Gytha Lainey ha solicitado tu ayuda con un asunto urgente, ${PLAYER}. Ve con ella de inmediato al Campamento de Adso, en las Tierras de Bree, en el camino entre Los Gamos y la ciudad de Bree.'","'Fue algo difícil, ${PLAYER}, pero logramos derrotar a los Huargos.'","Gytha Lainey está en el Campamento de Adso, en las Tierras de Bree, en el camino entre Los Gamos y la ciudad de Bree.\
\
Gytha Lainey te ha enviado un mensaje urgente solicitando tu ayuda.","Habla con Gytha Lainey y viaja hacia la Comarca","'Gracias a ti, la aldea de Sobrecolina está a salvo. Me alegra.'","Encargo de Cazadora","'No me equivoqué contigo esta vez, ${PLAYER}, pues sabía que estabas a la altura de la tarea, ¡y ahora los Huargos también lo saben! Aunque su compañero siga desaparecido, no creo que vuelvan a molestar a la Comarca... al menos por un tiempo.\
\
'Te encomiendo esto: mantén siempre tu enfoque, ${PLAYER} — un verdadero cazador no se desvía de su camino, sin importar la distracción.\
\
'Tienes mi gratitud,${PLAYER}.'","'Me alegra que hayas venido con tanta rapidez, , porque no sé en quién más podría confiar para ayudarme con esto — pocos cazadores se han ganado mi respeto como tú lo has hecho, pues la caída de Colmilloamarillo es prueba inigualable de tu valía.\
\
'Pero Colmilloamarillo no es más que un cachorro comparado con el peligro del que he oído hablar — una partida de caza de Huargos, una gran raza de lobos, ha salido del norte y ahora se adentra en las tierras del Pueblo Pequeño. Lo poco que pude averiguar de los asustados habitantes de las Quebradas del Norte me dice que estos Huargos están buscando a uno de los suyos que vino al sur y desapareció.\
\
'Esta búsqueda podría haberlos llevado a la Comarca, pero cuando encuentren tal abundancia de \\qvíctimas indefensas\\q, seguramente olvidarán su misión y se lanzarán sobre el pueblo. ¡Debemos encontrar y detener a estos Huargos antes de que alcancen alguna aldea, ! Avísame si estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir de inmediato, ¡y con urgencia!'","'¡Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un excelente cazador[m]|una excelente cazadora[f]}, , y los habitantes de Sobrecolina te lo agradecen!'","Gytha Lainey está en el Campamento de Adso, en las Tierras de Bree, en el camino entre la ciudad de Bree y Los Gamos.\
\
Gytha Lainey está esperando para hablar contigo y luego viajar hacia la Comarca para interceptar a la partida de caza de Huargos que ha venido del norte en busca de uno de los suyos.","'No he olvidado que nos ayudaste, ${PLAYER}. ¡Gracias de nuevo!'","En tiempos de peligro, un cazador entrenado puede ser el único capaz de encontrar y derrotar una amenaza antes de que ataque.","'¡Vámonos, ${PLAYER}, y deprisa! Si los huargos mantienen su rumbo, llegarán al pueblo de Sobrecolina; ¡debemos llegar antes que ellos!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una Comunidad.</rgb>","'Un viajero me trajo noticias de que Gytha Lainey está buscando tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Recibió el mensaje hace poco, y me transmitió la urgencia de la tarea, aunque ella no le reveló su naturaleza.\
\
'¡Debes ir con Gytha Lainey de inmediato! Debe ser algo serio para haber preocupado a una cazadora tan renombrada como ella.\
\
'Búscala en el Campamento de Adso, en el camino entre la ciudad de Bree y Los Gamos.'"},
[430]={"'Though we do not always agree, my brothers and I must stick together. We are stronger as one than when we are apart.\
\
'I thank you again for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. We could not have reunited without your help. If only my father Comeldir were alive. I could use his guidance in these dark times.'","'Let us pay our respects before returning to Garvir in Linhir.'","Speak with Erchar","Speak to Herion","A Just Burial","'The time has come to return to Linhir for Erchar and I. Come with us, ${PLAYER} and we shall all return victorious thanks to your deeds. Garvir will welcome us back with open arms. Together we can repair Linhir and defend it from the Corsairs.\
\
'First, we must pay our respects to those who have fallen in battle during this noble protection of Dor-en-Ernil. Let me know when you are ready and we shall begin our journey.'","Herion decides to return to Linhir with Erchar who has waited for him.","Erchar can be found in the town of Linhir.\
\
You have finished your journey from western Dor-en-Ernil to Linhir, and should now speak with Erchar.","Herion can be found in his encampment in western Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Herion asks you to travel with him back to Linhir."},
[431]={"Complete A Just Reward - Spoils of War","Jarl Gurthilm can be found to the south-east of Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
Jarl Gurthilm has offered you payment for the aid you gave to him and his men. You should discuss your choice with him.","A Just Reward","With their foes slain and the wealth of the Khundolar in their grasp, the Variags have decided to return to Khand once their final errand is finished.","'With that sorted, I think it is best for my men and me to return to Khand now.\
\
'Our battle is finished and our vengeance done, and we desire no greater role in this War. You keep the company of many great warriors, but do not underestimate the Dark Lord's power. In victory or defeat, I hope that you can escape his wrath.\
\
'Off with you, ${PLAYER}. Your allies might think less of you if you continued to travel with men such as us... and rightfully so!'\
\
With a smirk on his face, Jarl Gurthilm gestures for you to leave.","'It is done, ${PLAYER}. They have paid the price for our service, and more still for their betrayal!\
\
'Lord Zarhal Kôz shall send no more men after us, and any among the Khundolar who would dare to track us will not soon find us in these lands again.\
\
'My dealings with the Dark Lord are finished, as are those of my men. We shall not fight for a Master who does not honour our way.'\
\
Jarl Gurthilm's eyes turn to the Mountains of Shadow and a scowl flashes across his face before he turns back to you.\
\
'However, there remains the matter of your share.... You are free to take it, should you so choose. I understand if you would prefer to keep our dealings secret, so you may also refuse it and I shall send you on your way with basic supplies for your troubles.\
\
'I would be a fool to turn down a larger cut, but I'm a man of principle.'\
\
'I leave the choice to you.'","Talk to Jarl Gurthilm","Complete A Just Reward - Honour Alone","Jarl Gurthilm can be found to the south-east of Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
You have made your choice and should now speak to Jarl Gurthilm before parting ways."},
[433]={"'So what shall it be, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Jarl Gurthilm that you would be glad to accept your share of the Khundolar's gold.\
\
'You surprise me, ${CLASS}... perhaps we're more alike than I thought. There was a light in your eyes during the battle with the Khundolar, and not all of it came from the shimmering gold...\
\
'If that is your wish, consider it done! Blothára has divided the shares, and yours is in his keeping. Speak to him, and it is yours!\
\
'If our paths are so strange and winding as to cross again, you would be welcome among our company.'","A Just Reward - Spoils of War","Talk to Blothára","With their foes slain and the wealth of the Khundolar in their grasp, the Variags have decided to return to Khand once their final errand is finished.","Blothára can be found to the south-east of Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
You have chosen to accept your share of the gold, and Blothára can deliver it to you when you are prepared.","'You'll take your gold?\
\
'I must admit, I wagered a small portion of my share that you would refuse it. I suppose there's more sorting to be done then... Gurthilm must be delighted.\
\
'We do not battle without the promise of rewards, and with all you have done, you should consider doing the same!'\
\
'As promised, here is your share.'"},
[434]={"Free Múta from her cage at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate","'Well, any luck?'\
\
You show Múta the single, small key you retrieved from the Iron Crown key-warden.\
\
'I must admit, ${PLAYER}, I'd hoped you'd return with a whole key-ring. I guess we'll have to hope this one does the trick!'","The Dourhands' summoning horn can be found along the road at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
You have discovered the Dourhands' summoning horn and you should now sound it in an attempt to summon the Iron Crown key-warden.","You hear someone approach...","The Dourhands' summoning horn can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
Múta has asked you to seek out the Dourhands' summoning horn at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate and summon an Iron Crown key-warden. You should find the summoning horn at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.","A Key to Freedom","Talk to Múta at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate","Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
You have collected a single, small key from the Iron Crown key-warden. You should use it to attempt to free Múta from her cage.","'Ha! I was beginning to think I was going to have file one of these bars down.\
\
'Well done, ${PLAYER}. Now, let's get out of here!'","Find the horn used by the Dourhands to summon the Iron Crown key-warden","Use the Dourhands' summoning horn and confront the Iron Crown key-warden","Beneath the arches of the Witch-gate, you discover a crude horn hanging from a post","Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
You have collected a single, small key from the Iron Crown key-warden. You should return to Múta.","Múta can be found at Mur Shatraug, the Witch-gate.\
\
You have managed to unlock Múta's cage. You should talk to Múta.","As the Iron Crown key-warden falls defeated, you collect a small key from his belt","Despite the efforts of the Dourhands, Múta believes she may have discovered the key to her escape from the Witch-gate.","'Subtlety has served me well in the past, but from what I have learned, the Iron Crown answer only to two things: their self-styled masters... and force!'\
\
'Within the orders you found, there was mention of a jailor dispatched to the Witch-gate to deliver me to the Iron Crown at the Drearspire. As I am swiftly learning, the Iron Crown seem fond of bestowing fanciful titles upon themselves and their followers. For instance, they call this would-be jailor a \\qkey-warden\\q. If one needs for so many keys, I wager they do not trust their locks.\
\
'Unless my ears have deceived me, the Dourhands use some sort of summoning horn to communicate with the Iron Crown. Perhaps if you were to greet the key-warden in the Dourhands' stead, you might find the key to this cage!'","To your and Múta's surprise, the lock on her cage disengages!"},
[436]={"'Hah! It is as I'd hoped, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Ambassador Spakorth and his folk will be so grateful. They will understand what a King of the dwarves ought to be!\
\
'Now then, as for earning their place....'","A King Lost, A King Gained","King Thorin III can be found at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
Gimli has offered an impassioned plea for the Stout-axes to be accepted as friends and kin to Durin's Folk. You should hear King Thorin's judgment on the matter.","'Gimli, son of Glóin, I have known your father and your family for many years.\
\
'I have heard your words, and I will bear my judgment. As you well know, the Dale-lands are filled with refugees of the East -- and among them, the unfortunate cousins of the hated Jangovar. Regardless of their heritage, I see their plight for what it is.\
\
'I trust your words, Gimli, and I would not deny those oppressed by Mordor. The Stout-axes shall have shelter within Erebor, and be welcome as friends of Durin's Folk. However, these are difficult times. Sacrifices have been made by each of the Kingdoms of the North, and more still will have to be made before we have healed the ills of the War. If the Stout-axes are to dwell among us, they must earn their place among our folk and share their knowledge of the Enemy and the lands beyond.\
\
'You may inform the Stout-axes that they have found a new home in Erebor, but see to it that they offer their skills to all in need.'","Habla con Gimli","Gimli, son of Glóin, has returned to Erebor from the lands of Mordor and now seeks to ensure peace between the Dwarves of Durin's Folk and the Stout-axes of Dor Amarth.","Gimli can be found near King Thorin's throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
King Thorin III has passed his judgment on what is to be done regarding the Stout-axes. You should now speak to Gimli.","'Well, then.'\
\
Gimli approaches King Thorin III and begins to speak.\
\
'Hail, Thorin III, King Under the Mountain! I come before you today to ask for your wisdom and mercy. In my adventures beyond the Black Gate of Mordor, I discovered a clan of dwarves known as the Stout-axes. They are a hardy folk, but they have been beset by tragedy at many turns. They have lost their ancestral home, much as we of Durin's Folk have in the past, and they have suffered under the Dark Lord and his servants. Their leader of old, King Greytooth, succumbed to what power lingered in the Rings once wielded by the greatest Kings of the dwarves and led the remainder of his folk down a dark path to ruin.\
\
'The Stout-axes were thus sundered, but I have come north with those who survived and they did not lose hope that kindness could be found beyond the mountains of Mordor. Their number is small, and they have no home beyond these lands. I beg you, King Thorin, offer them a place among us and they will offer their knowledge, compassion, and skill to Durin's Folk.'\
\
Gimli finishes speaking and looks to King Thorin.","Hear King Thorin III's judgment"},
[437]={"King Elessar can be found in the Hall of the King.\
\
Arvedui has asked you to talk to King Elessar on his behalf.","With the coronation of Elessar, a king who has lingered in Middle-earth for far too long can finally rest.","Talk to King Elessar","A King's Rest","'Hail, ${PLAYER}. I have little time. I am pulled to that which lies beyond.'\
\
Arvedui is barely visible, and fading away with each passing second. You do not think anyone else has noticed him.\
\
'I have followed thy adventures since last we spoke, and I must thank thee for everything thou hast done to aid my heir in reclaiming the throne. My curse has been lifted and I feel I can move on with hope for the future of Men, and all free people.\
\
'I have but moments more. Please greet Aragorn, no, Elessar, on my behalf, and wish both he and his kingdom well.'","'${PLAYER}, what troubles you?'\
\
You point to Arvedui, who is now barely a shadow in the grand hall. Elessar seems to disbelieve the sight.\
\
'Is that... Arvedui?'\
\
You nod, and deliver his message of good tidings. Elessar smiles and bows deeply before his predecessor. Arvedui nods solemnly, his spectral eyes filled with tears of joy, and vanishes completely.\
\
'He is gone. You did find a way to ease his spirit!'\
\
You tell Elessar that the final thing he needed to pass on was a new king on the throne.\
\
'Have you known this since your time in Forochel? And he had you promise not to tell me, to spare me the additional pressure? Of course.'\
\
He chuckles and shakes his head.\
\
'${PLAYER}, thank you for your part in putting my ancestor's spirit to rest. My heart swells with pride knowing that he was here to witness my coronation. I only hope I am able to rule with wisdom and a just heart, as Arvedui and those who came before him did.'","Arvedui fades away, his eyes brimming with tears of joy"},
[438]={"Lleva el hacha a Inufileg en Gwingris","Este hacha fue portada por un dunlendino, pero ves marcas que claramente no son obra de dunlendinos. Aunque no puedes determinar el origen, quizá uno de los elfos de Gwingris sepa algo más.","El hacha de un trabajador","Gwingris está en el extremo norte de Glâd Ereg.\
\
Deberías llevarle el hacha a los elfos de Gwingris.","Has encontrado un extraño hacha de los dunlendinos cerca de Gwingris, pero no reconoces la factura.","'Esto es extraño. ¿Dices que la portaba un dunlendino?\
\
'Este hacha es de una calidad que no corresponde normalmente a estos bandidos, lo que es preocupante. Parece que lo que habría sido una fuerza independiente está organizada bajo el estandarte de otra persona.'","'¿Tienes algo para mí, ${PLAYER}?'"},
[439]={"Landroval can be found at the clearing of trees in the north-east section of Wailing Hills.\
\
Landroval must be informed of the results of your search for the sneaking creature.","Cocoons of spider-webbing may be found to the west of the hidden clearing, among the northern hills.\
\
Landroval has asked you to search among the spider-cocoons for any sign of the creature he was tasked with following.","The cocoon contains no evidence of the creature you are seeking","Talk to Landroval about what you have found","'I have found no trace of the creature we were tracking. Our eyes could still follow him through the shadows, but we cannot see into the depths of every crag and cave in these hills, and we may have lost his trail.\
\
'If the creature came this way, it is possible he may have succumbed to the large spiders that dwell in these parts. Would you search some of the spider-cocoons for the creature? If you find him, do not harm him... simply return to me with news.'","Search the spider-cocoons in search of the strange creature (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Landroval has been following the trail of a small shadowy creature and is uncertain if his mark has been ensnared by the spiders native to the region.","'It is as I feared, we have lost the trail. I shall take this news to Gwaihir, perhaps we will be able to track our target again with his help.\
\
'Nevertheless, it is worth knowing that his path did not end at the fangs of a spider. Your help has been most appreciated.'","'Have you discovered something? The spiders have spun several webbed cocoons to the west. I fear that one of them contains the small creature we have been tracking.'","A Lack of Evidence"},
[440]={"Collect bear-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Herubrand is in the cellar of the farmhouse.\
\
You should bring the ill news of the mismanagement of the city's monies, as it may help explain why the situation in Woodhurst is growing worse.","Carne de ciervo conseguida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A Lack of Support","Collect hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Elda","'The guards have not received monies for some time now, and I can barely pay the men. I cannot purchase arms or supplies! Why is it that Reeve Heremond thinks a city can be protected with nothing? I have brought this to his advisors and was dismissed.\
\
'Perhaps you can help. My men are busy with their duties to Woodhurst, but I could use someone to gather supplies from the wildlife around the city. I need hides, bear-claws, goat-hooves, and venison.'","Talk to Guard-captain Thurferth","Herubrand is in the cellar of the farmhouse.\
\
Herubrand should know what Elda had to say about the funds for the city guards.","Collected goat-hooves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected bear-claws (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Elda said that he diverted monies elsewhere? But who else is protecting the city, if not the city guard? My father trusted this man and paid for it with his life....\
\
'He either kept that money and is a thief, or he gave it to someone, as he said, and is a traitor.'","Collected hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Guard-captain Thurferth is near the centre of the city.\
\
You should return to Guard-captain Thurferth and inform him of the misplacement of funding that was intended for him.","Elda has not been seen since the council-meeting, but he should be somewhere in Woodhurst.\
\
You need to speak with Elda about the funding for the guards that has not been delivered.","'Begone, I have nothing to say to you. Are you accusing me of thievery? You have no evidence and are fortunate that I do not dispose of you right now.\
\
'I was instructed to fund the city's protection. I diverted funding to those who could actually protect us. The guards do naught, and I am not afraid to say it. Tell him what you want. I do not fear him... or you.'","Collect venison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect goat-hooves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Guard-captain Thurferth has not received funding from Woodhurst's leadership. His plea for assistance to the advisor responsible for the funds has fallen on deaf ears.","Talk to Herubrand","'That is not possible. I know for certain that my father set aside a considerable portion of the city's monies to fund the guard. It is vital for any city.\
\
'Where did the money go if not to the guards? Elda has been involved in the planning for some time, and perhaps he knows what happened. Please find him and speak with him about this.'","'The advisor responsible for funding the protection of the city put those funds elsewhere? He should hope that I never see him again. However, if anyone is truly to blame, it is Reeve Heremond for entrusting someone like that to handle such important affairs.\
\
'You have my thanks for uncovering this plot.'","'${PLAYER}, you have my thanks. Collecting these supplies was no small task, but I am afraid that I have not much to repay you with.\
\
'I still find it difficult to believe that the Reeve would not set aside funding for the city guard. You seem to be in good standing with his advisors. Could you speak with them for me to determine why we are receiving so little support?'","Wild beasts roam the lands around Woodhurst.\
\
Guard-captain Thurferth asked that you collect hides, bear-claws, goat-hooves, and venison to supply the garrison.","Return the supplies to Thurferth, near the centre of Woodhurst.\
\
Guard Captain Thurferth will be thankful for these supplies."},
[441]={"Lady Tóla summoned you to her house so that she could express her gratitude for your kindness and make a request of you.","'Alas, ${PLAYER}, you have no doubt learned that we are facing a siege by Orcs from the Misty Mountains. Théoden King has decreed a ban on the hunting of Orcs in Rohan, which my husband's father is rightly hesitant to break.\
\
'Nevertheless, Ingmar, my husband, desires to earn glory in battle and counsels his father to defend our lands by allowing him to lead an assault on the Orcs. I fear that if he does this thing, he will not return, and I will be left a widow, only newly married.\
\
'Ingmar's grandmother is Reeve Ingbert's chief counselor and speaks wisdom on behalf of Théoden King's decree. Perhaps if you speak with her, she can help to convince the Reeve of the wisdom of preparing our defences here at Eaworth, rather than send my husband to meet the enemy on the open field. Will you do this?'","Talk to Adalmód outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Adalmód stands guard outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should speak with Adalmód to gain access to the Mead Hall of Eaworth.","A Lady's Fears","'Hold, ${CLASS}. Did I not say the Reeve was not to be disturbed?'"},
[443]={"Scout the causeway to ruins of Barad-dûr","Gimli can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth due south of the Isenmouthe in Dor Amarth.\
\
You have found evidence of dwarves in Mordor and collected one of their shields. You should bring the shield to Gimli and see what he makes of it.","The fallen dwarf and his goat can be found to the north of the causeway to Barad-dûr.\
\
You have found a fallen dwarf and his goat. You should examine them and collect his shield.","Deliver the dwarf-shield to Gimli at the Ruins of Díngarth","A Land of Ash and Shadow","The dwarf lies slain in armour of finer make than that of the Orcs...","Collect the fallen dwarf's shield","In Dor Amarth, the toppled ruin of Barad-dûr still looms over the wracked plains of Mordor, casting its shadows over unseen foes.","Examine the fallen dwarf","You notice what appears to be a dwarf and a goat lying still beside the causeway...","'What is this?'\
\
You tell Gimli of the slain dwarf you found and offer him the shield.\
\
'By your description of his wounds, the dwarf you encountered must have been caught by a stray stone thrown from the depths of Mount Doom. A poor dwarf, indeed, but not one slain by malice. The Dark Lord must not have brought my kin to ruin after all!\
\
'Ah-ha! Look at this, my friend. This shield is newly-forged... and crafted by skilled hands!\
\
'So dwarves still dwell in Mordor, but where have they made their home?'","Wrought of dark steel, the shield remains unblemished despite the fate of its wielder","Far from wild, the goat is saddled and laden with various trinkets and supplies...","Examine the fallen dwarf's goat","'Gimli and I have not ventured overfar into these lands, my friend, and I am not certain I wish to. The Men of Gondor call this place Dor Amarth; the Doomfold in the Common Speech.\
\
'Its name was wisely chosen by those Men, for I feel a deep shadow looming over us even so far from the ruins of the Dark Tower. Gimli has found old tools of dwarf-make in this ruin, and though he will not speak of it, unease has crept into his mind. If ever dwarves dwelt within Mordor, it seems their fate was not a pleasant one and that their line is long ended.\
\
'This causeway forks some distance to the south. One path leads southward and appears less well-kept by the Orcs, while the other rises and continues east to Barad-dûr. I would ask that you follow the causeway south to the fork and then beyond to the east. Search for foes or those still held as slaves, and perhaps we shall find something to raise Gimli's spirits and draw his thoughts from those of his distant kin.\
\
'Do not stray far from the road, my friend, for we have much still to learn of the hidden evils of Mordor.'","The causeway extends to the south-east from the Isenmouthe, eventually leading to the foot of Barad-dûr.\
\
Legolas has asked you to scout the causeway leading to the ruins of Barad-dûr as he desires to learn what foes still lurk in the shadows of its toppled heights."},
[444]={"Malthellam can be found outside his house near the entrance to Morlad.\
\
You have delivered Lord Duinhir's notes and spoke to Lady Rosfin about providing counsel for the good of the vale, and should now return to Malthellam.","Lord Duinhir's notes can be found inside Malthellam's home in Morlad.\
\
Malthellam hopes to repair his friendship with Lady Rosfin, and has asked you to return her husband's notes to her.","Gather Lord Duinhir's notes","Talk to Malthellam","Bring Lord Duinhir's notes to Lady Rosfin","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! Lady Rosfin has already come to speak to me.\
\
'I cannot thank you enough for convincing her to aid me in protecting the vale. Her insight will no doubt help us to push the Orcs and our other troubles from these lands.\
\
'Rosfin informed me that she would like to speak to you further before we take action, but please... keep me informed.'","Lady Rosfin can be found outside Malthellam's home in Morlad.\
\
Lady Rosfin has honoured Malthellam's request and has arrived to serve as his counselor. You should now speak to her.","Lady Rosfin can be found atop Morlad outside her home.\
\
You have gathered Lord Duinhir's notes and should now return them to Lady Rosfin.","'No... it is not Lord Duinhir's insight I require. Only Rosfin knows enough of these lands to aid me now....'\
\
Malthellam lets out a long sigh.\
\
'These notes will no sooner help me lead my people than a blade of grass can fell an Orc. I made the terrible mistake of sacrificing Tingobel for the safety of Morlad, but too many fell... and I saved too few. The guilt weighs on me far heavier than any could understand.\
\
'Lady Rosfin must see reason, and if not to help me, she must help her people. I beg this of her.'","DNT -- will not be seen","Talk to Lady Rosfin outside Malthellam's home","A Lapse in Judgement","Malthellam seeks to heal his once strong friendship with Rosfin in light of his recent failures as steward.","'Do not mistake my apprehension for hatred, ${PLAYER}. Malthellam has long been a friend to my family, and there is no wiser counsel in the vale.\
\
'However, I am not fond of his leadership since becoming steward, but I will aid him as best I can so my husband and sons shall have a home to return to once this war is over.'","'Back so soon? Were you even able to show him the notes before he turned you back around?'\
\
You tell Lady Rosfin of Malthellam's impassioned plea.\
\
'Very well, I shall serve as his counsel. Malthellam is determined, I will grant him that. I do not have time to continue swatting away his attempts to sway me, and perhaps by working with him, I can prevent another tragedy like Tingobel from occurring. \
\
'I will meet you at his home... and I hope I do not regret this.'"},
[445]={"Meneldir dice que el ataque de los uruk contra Musgovilla es una señal de que no puedes evitar los peligros que se ciernen sobre la Ciénaga de los Cisnes. Te has convertido en parte de un mundo más grande.","Habla con Eleri sobre la Marca de la Mano Blanca","Un Mundo Más Grande","'Por ahora deberíamos ayudar a la gente de Musgovilla a recuperarse de este ataque. ¿Prestarás tu ayuda? Te has visto envuelto en esto, igual que yo. Si lo que buscas es una vida de aventura, te aseguro que parece que la has encontrado... ¡o que ella te ha encontrado a ti!\
\
'Te has convertido en parte de un mundo más grande, ${PLAYER}, y puede ser distinto del que conocías hasta ahora. Deben afrontarse peligros y oponerse a amenazas, y superarlas, si tienes predisposición a luchar contra ellas. No todos lo tienen... pero juzgo que tú no estarás muy lejos al triunfo y la victoria.'","'No, no he visto este símbolo antes.'","Meneldir luce una expresión preocupada.","Eleri se alza sobre los cadáveres de los uruk saqueadores, pensando en los acontecimientos del ataque.","'¿Qué significado podría tener esta marca? ${PLAYER}, ¿preguntarás a Eleri si ha visto este símbolo antes de hoy?'","'¿Ha visto Eleri este símbolo antes?'","'¿La Mano Blanca? No, no he visto este símbolo antes... y eso me inquieta. ¿Qué nuevo peligro podría significar?'","Habla con Meneldir"},
[446]={"Meneldir dice que el ataque de los uruk contra Musgovilla es una señal de que no puedes evitar los peligros que se ciernen sobre la Ciénaga de los Cisnes. Te has convertido en parte de un mundo más grande.","Habla con Eleri sobre la Marca de la Mano Blanca","Un Mundo Más Grande","'Por ahora deberíamos ayudar a la gente de Musgovilla a recuperarse de este ataque. ¿Prestarás tu ayuda? Te has visto envuelto en esto, igual que yo. Si lo que buscas es una vida de aventura, te aseguro que parece que la has encontrado... ¡o que ella te ha encontrado a ti!\
