\
Debes hablar con Skardi Doblafilos para aprender más sobre su oferta.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Esta es una misión tutorial para acceder a la tienda web.</rgb>","La Tienda de LOTRO ofrece cosméticos, potenciadores, acceso a contenido y una variedad de otros artículos. ¡Asegúrate de visitarla a menudo para ver qué hay de nuevo!\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Aceptar y completar esta misión solo puede hacerse una vez por servidor. Si cierras sesión antes de completarla, será eliminada de tu registro de misiones y deberás aceptarla nuevamente. Esto te dará acceso a una misión tutorial especial para presentarte la Tienda de LOTRO.</rgb>","Un Poco Extra Nunca Hace Daño — Parte 1","Habla con Skardi Doblafilos en su tienda."},
[469]={"Habla con el otorgador de la misión para completarla. <rgb=#00FF00>Debes comprar esta misión en la Tienda Web de LOTRO antes de poder completarla.</rgb>","Un Poco Extra Nunca Hace Daño — Parte 2","Habla con el otorgador de la misión para completarla.","Esta misión está pensada para mostrarte cómo interactuar con la Tienda de LOTRO.","'Excelentes noticias. Acepta esta montura. Te llevará hacia y desde la batalla, pero no es apta para combatir.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Esta misión debe desbloquearse una vez por tu cuenta y puede adquirirse en la Tienda de LOTRO. Completar la misión 'Un Poco Extra Nunca Hace Daño — Parte 1' no es obligatorio para continuar, pero proporcionará suficientes Puntos LOTRO para cubrir esta compra. 'Un Poco Extra Nunca Hace Daño — Parte 1' solo puede completarse una vez por cuenta.</rgb>\
\
Para comprar esta misión, haz clic en el botón en la parte inferior izquierda de la ventana de Diálogo de Misión que dice Desbloquear Misión. Esto te llevará a la interfaz de la tienda web. Desde allí, puedes elegir gastar Puntos LOTRO para obtener acceso a la misión.\
\
Puedes usar la tienda para una multitud de compras, incluyendo acceso a zonas de aventura, objetos consumibles, expansiones, recetas de artesanía, objetos cosméticos, monturas y mucho más.\
\
Aunque 'Un Poco Extra Nunca Hace Daño — Parte 1' solo puede completarse una vez por cuenta, esta misión, 'Un Poco Extra Nunca Hace Daño — Parte 2', puede ser completada por cada personaje.","<rgb=#00FF00>Esta misión debe desbloquearse una vez por tu cuenta y puede adquirirse en la Tienda de LOTRO. Has recibido suficientes Puntos LOTRO para cubrir esta compra gracias a 'Un Poco Extra Nunca Hace Daño — Parte 1'.\
\
Para comprar esta misión, haz clic en el botón en la parte inferior izquierda de la ventana de Diálogo de Misión que dice Desbloquear Misión. Esto te llevará a la interfaz de la tienda web. Desde allí, puedes elegir gastar Puntos LOTRO para obtener acceso a la misión.\
\
Puedes usar la tienda para una multitud de compras, incluyendo acceso a zonas de aventura, objetos consumibles, expansiones, recetas de artesanía, objetos cosméticos, monturas y mucho más.</rgb>"},
[471]={"A Little Piece of Home in Evendim","You have gathered a perfect cut of boar-meat, which brings to mind a tale of woe you overheard from a bard:\
\
'Poor Parr Chopley has left all he has known and struck forth into the world, finding himself in Evendim, in Ost Forod.\
\
'The sad little hobbit has been searching high and low for a little piece of boar to remind him of home.'\
\
Perhaps you should travel north to Ost Forod and seek out this hobbit. He may appreciate this prize piece of boar-meat.","Deliver the boar-meat to Parr Chopley in Ost Forod","This piece of boar-meat, while slightly discoloured, seems to be a wonderful cut of meat. Perhaps someone in Ost Forod might be really looking for something to hit the spot.","Parr Chopley is in Ost Forod in Evendim, far to the north of the Shire.\
\
You should bring the boar-meat to Parr Chopley.","'Oh me, oh my, what do you have there?\
\
'Could that possibly be a little cut of boar-meat found within the confines of Evendim. \
\
'Thank you so much, I will go and cook it at once.'"},
[472]={"Un pequeño toque de rojo","'Puedes encontrar salamandras en las dunas al norte y al este. Asegúrate de traer sus escamas.'","Lleva las escamas a Waldo Cerrohueco en Dwaling","Escamas cubiertas de arena conseguidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se pueden encontrar escamas cubiertas de arena en las salamandras de las dunas del sur del Barandalf, al norte y al este de Dwaling.\
\
Waldo Cerrohueco te ha pedido que recojas escamas cubiertas de arena de las salamandras, para poder hacer cristal rojo.","Waldo Cerrohueco está en casa de Hob Cimacolina, en el exterior de Dwaling.\
\
Waldo Cerrohueco querrá empezar a moler las escamas lo antes posible.","'Estas escamas servirán perfectamente. Empezaré a molerlas ahora mismo para que podamos usarlas en el siguiente lote. Gracias.'","Cuando se muelen, las escamas de salamandra pueden utilizarse para fabricar cristal rojo.","Utilizamos muchos materiales para dar distintas tonalidades al vidrio. Uno de los colores de los que me encargo es el rojo. No es muy un color muy difícil de obtener, pero requiere una buena cantidad de material conseguir un carmesí brillante.\
\
'Las escamas de salamandra son el mejor material que he encontrado por aquí para fabricar vidrio rojo. Desafortunadamente nuestros suministros son escasos, así que no podemos hacer más rojo o naranja.\
\
Puedes encontrar escamas cubiertas de arena en las salamandras de las dunas del sur del Barandalf, al norte y al este de aquí. Si me consigues un puñado, te estaría agradecido.'","Consigue escamas cubiertas de arena (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[473]={"Se pueden encontrar Uruks cerca de Tham Celechir, la Sala del Río Veloz, al norte de Idhobel.","Un Poco de Ambas","Lornel está junto a la fogata en Idhobel.","'Enfréntate a los Uruks que merodean Tham Celechir, al norte, y arráncales sus armas. Te estaré en deuda por esto, como sanador y como combatiente.'","'No soy solo un sanador y un herbolario, sino también un guerrero, y en ocasiones he tenido motivo para usar mis habilidades en combate. Conozco las heridas que pueden causar las espadas empuñadas por Uruks, tanto como quien las trata como quien las ha sufrido.\
\
'Enfréntate a los Uruks que merodean Tham Celechir, al norte, y arráncales sus armas. Te estaré en deuda por esto, como sanador y como combatiente.'","Lleva las espadas de Uruk a Lornel en Idhobel","Lornel quiere que sepas que no es solo un sanador, sino también un guerrero y un capitán.","Espadas de Uruks recolectadas cerca de Tham Celechir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Gracias por estas armas. Quizá esto dificulte los esfuerzos de los Uruks por amenazar a la gente de esta tierra y frene el daño que creen causar.\
\
'Ve con mis mejores deseos, y buena fortuna en tu camino.'","Recolecta espadas de Uruks cerca de Tham Celechir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[474]={"A Local Supply","Mírthel recoils as you hand him the meat. The smell is quite foul.\
\
'Ah... not so edible, then. A shame. The deer are too sickly for our consumption, and the goats have succumbed to a fell sort of corruption that enables them to survive in this evil place.\
\
'Thank you for your efforts all the same. I will dispatch one of our Rangers for more rations.'","Mírthel has asked you to hunt some of the local wildlife and assess whether their meat can be eaten by the Rangers.","Mírthel has asked you to hunt some of the wildlife in Cirith Ungol to assess the edibility of the meat.\
\
You should hunt deer and dire-horns for their meat.","Carne de ciervo conseguida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Mírthel","'Might I ask for your assistance while you are here?\
\
'As you may have guessed, supplying our small expedition has been difficult. We brought what we could carry up the Straight Stair, but it will not last long. Going forward, we must choose between finding a source of sustenance here among the darkness and corruption, or send someone to fetch more rations from Captain Faramir's camp, and that is a treacherous journey. Obviously, the former is preferable.\
\
'I have seen some deer and goats while scouting the area. Would you please hunt some of them, so I can assess if the meat is edible?'","Mírthel is waiting for you to return with the meat.","Collect dire-horn meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect venison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected dire-horn meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[475]={"Ask Khôltekh about his thoughts on the matter","Listen to Khôltekh's explanation.","A Lock with No Key","Listen to Khôltekh's thoughts on the key","Khôltekh has asked you back to his house once more, so he can think on the riddle of this key and access to Dâr Sêkhta.","Listen to Khôltekh's thoughts on the key.","Accompany Khôltekh to his study","Accompany Khôltekh to his study.","Listen to Khôltekh's explanation","'I have bad news, ${PLAYER}. I've solved our riddle.'","Ask Khôltekh about his thoughts on the matter."},
[477]={"Busca a Orthonn y habla con él","Un vigilante solitario","'¡Saludos, caminante! Ah, ¿Amarion te envía? ¿Qué noticias hay de Amon Raith?'","Orthonn se encuentra en su campamento cerca del río en Annúndir, no muy lejos del camino.\
\
Debes encontrar a Orthonn y hablar con él.","'¡De cuánta ayuda nos has sido, ${PLAYER}! Imagino que con los huargos dispersados, podemos volver a poner todo en orden por aquí.\
\
'Debo pedirte una última cosa. Mi amigo, Orthonn, vigila Annúndir desde un puesto de avanzada solitario. Muy poca gente va en esa dirección. ¿Podrías comprobar que se encuentra bien, y contarle noticias del oeste de las Quebradas mientras estás por allí?'","Amarion te ha pedido que ofrezcas tu ayuda y compañía a Orthonn, un Montaraz que tiene la misión de mantener un puesto de vigilancia en la espesura de Annúndir."},
[480]={"'Ha ocurrido algo de lo más extraño desde la última vez que estuviste fuera, ${PLAYER}. Escuché un eco muy largo... y sonaba como el grito de un enano.\
\
'El sonido venía del nordeste de aquí. ¿Podrías ir a explorar? Me gustaría regresar al Mirador de la Gran Excavación.'","'¡Qué eco tan extraño era! Escalofriante, a decir verdad. No debía de provenir de muy lejos.'","Completa el segundo objetivo del diario","Divisas una mochila en la esquina nordeste de la Gran Excavación, situada junto a una gran grieta en el camino.\
\
Deberías registrar la mochila.","Wigfast escuchó un grito con un eco extrañamente largo al nordeste de Gazatmur, y se pregunta qué pudo haber sido ese sonido.","Cerca de la mochila hay un libro, un diario, con los objetivos de un enano anotados.\
\
Deberías completar los objetivos que pretendía el enano que murió.","Slagvi se encuentra en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Deberías contarle a Slagvi todo lo que has encontrado en el lado oriental de la Gran Excavación.","Habla con Slagvi en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación","Esta mochila podría indicar la fuente del extraño eco que escuchó Wigfast. Parece haber pertenecido a un enano, pero el enano no se encuentra por ninguna parte.\
\
Sospechas firmemente que cayó por la peligrosa grieta del camino. Pero ¿qué hacía tan lejos de cualquier asentamiento establecido en Moria?","Un largo eco","Completa el primer objetivo del diario","La fuente del eco puede encontrarse siguiendo las escaleras tras el escondite de Wigfast y, desde allí, dirigiéndote al noroeste hacia los niveles superiores.\
\
Deberías buscar el origen del eco.","Encuentra la fuente del eco","Investiga la mochila cerca de la grieta del camino","'¡Desde luego has tenido encuentros de lo más extraños! Manos Blancas, uruks, trasgos, mochilas y profundas grietas... ¡mejor tú que yo, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Bueno, me alegra que hayas regresado sano y salvo. Descansa aquí, en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, donde la luz es brillante y el fuego cálido.'","Esta zona coincide con las descripciones de Wigfast...."},
[481]={"Fed horses (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The horses are now much less agitated thanks to your efforts.","This horse looks hungry","'We need to ensure these horses stay calm. They all had a long journey here from Woodhurst and now grow restless waiting up on this bridge. I could use your aid, for I must keep my place in this line.\
\
'Please gather some of the horse-feed from the bag at the end of the line and give a little to each horse. Hopefully, that will ease their spirits.'","A Long Journey for the Steeds","Gapholt has become a haven for the Rohirrim who sought a safer place to live than the dangerous streets of Woodhurst.","There is a bag of horse-feed near the refugee waiting at the end of the line on the bridge trying to get into Gapholt.\
\
You should collect horse-feed from the bag.","Feed horses (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The horses seem more calm now that you have given them a little food, and it seems they are less likely to become unruly and cause injury to themselves or others. Hopefully, whatever is delaying their entry will be resolved soon.","Completado","Collect horse-feed from the container","Many horses are agitated by the wait on the bridge after the long journey from Woodhurst.\
\
The refugee at the end of the line suggested that you feed them to help calm them down."},
[482]={"Talk to Dírion outside the Lower Stores, in the First Circle of the city","Merethien, the Master Foodmonger of the Council, is in the Dome of the Sun.\
\
Arodor told you that Merethien could use your assistance.","Mirudal, the Warden of the Stores, is in the Dome of the Sun.\
\
Arodor told you that Mirudal could use your assistance.","The Lower Stores are guarded to prevent unlawful access to the goods within","Go to the very back of the Upper Stores and use the Upper Stores Inventory","'I am glad you came back, ${PLAYER}. The Council has just heard Ingold's report of the situation in Talath Anor; the Captain of the Out-wall painted a picture, but it was not a rosy one!\
\
'Merethien and Mirudal have been working on a plan to assess the food-stocks and other supplies within the city, and they could use your assistance. They are right over there, and will be glad to have your help.'","Go to the very back of the Lower Stores and use the Lower Stores Inventory","'You are welcome to enter the Stores and compare its contents to your inventory, but remove nothing.'","Inside the Upper Stores, you should compare the inventory with the actual goods being stored. Only by knowing the exact count of the foodstuffs available can Mirudal and Merethien properly ration them during a long siege.","A Long Siege","Dírion is outside the Lower Stores, just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle.\
\
You have discovered that the inventory of the Lower Stores does not match their contents: some food is missing.","'Stop, friend. On whose authority do you seek to gain access to the Upper Stores?'\
\
You show Túlharil the inventory from Mirudal, and she recognizes the mark of the Warden of the Stores.\
\
'Aye, that is his mark. You are welcome to enter the Stores and compare its contents to your inventory, but remove nothing.'","'How do the inventories compare, ${PLAYER}? Do we have all the goods we expect?'\
\
You tell Mirudal that the Upper Stores are fully accounted, but Dírion believes that rats are to blame for a disparity between the inventory of the Lower Stores and the goods actually kept there. Mirudal nods.\
\
'Ah, I see. That is a shame, but it is not terribly surprising. Rats need to eat as well, and they can sense coming danger as well or better than we can! It makes sense to me that rats might covet our goods. I will set the total amount of food to be rationed slightly lower than I planned, in order to account for the rats. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","'You... you have come back? Did you tell Mirudal about the rats?'\
\
You tell Dírion that you do not believe his story about rats, and that you think he has been stealing food from the Stores. His brow knits with rage, and his eyes darken. When he finally speaks, his voice is desperate.\
\
'Have mercy upon me, ${CLASS}! I admit the deed. My family could not bear to leave the city, and when the order to evacuate came, they hid within the house; they are there still! This is their home, and they could not bear to leave it, or me! My wife Mundil, my son Cúnir, my daughter Fionel... they will not be accounted-for when Mirudal rations out the food! If I do not steal some of the food for them, they will go hungry! So I have set aside a small amount. Is that a crime? Have mercy!\
\
'What will you do? If you turn me in, you will doom my family! Help me, ${PLAYER}, or do nothing! Better that than have my family's lives upon your conscience!'","Arodor has asked that you help the Council of Gondor inventory the supplies in the city in order to prepare for a long siege.","'Yes? Are you finished?'\
\
You tell Dírion that some of the food appears to be missing.\
\
'I see. I should have mentioned this when you arrived, but I have had my suspicions for some time now that there might be a rat problem inside the Stores. They must have gnawed their way in and spirited away some of the food, especially the grains and cheeses. You should tell Mirudal. He may need to account for slightly lower totals of food for the coming siege.\
\
'It might be best if he lowers the tally of food he expects to ration. The rats will keep getting into it, I imagine. Nothing to be done.'","Inside the Lower Stores, you should compare the inventory with the actual goods being stored. Only by knowing the exact count of the foodstuffs available can Mirudal and Merethien properly ration them during a long siege.","The Lower Stores are located just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle.\
\
Something about Dírion's story does not convince you, and you think you should confront the guard about it.","'You should tell Mirudal about the rats. He may need to account for slightly lower totals of food for the coming siege. It might be best if he lowers the tally of food he expects to ration. The rats will keep getting into it, I imagine. Nothing to be done.'","'Stop, friend. On whose authority do you seek to access the Upper Stores?'","Talk to Mirudal, Warden of the Stores, in the Dome of the Sun","Find the entrance to the Lower Stores, just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle","A thorough comparison reveals that the contents of the Upper Stores are properly accounted","'I have given you two inventories, one for the goods of the Upper Stores and one for the goods of the Lower Stores. Speak to the guards outside each and show them my mark, and they will allow you inside. Compare the inventory with the actual goods, and ensure that we have all of the supplies we expect.\
\
'Only then will we be able to properly ration the supplies if the siege proves to be long.'","'Stop. Why do you seek to access the Lower Stores?'","'The burden of governance is heavy, but it is especially so in time of war. We have not seen Steward Denethor since Prince Imrahil carried his son back to the city, but we do not need to hear his words to know what awaits us: a siege, possibly a long one.\
\
'The greatest enemy during a long siege is not necessarily the foe outside the gates, ${PLAYER}! The greatest enemy is hunger. With the gates shut, we will not be able to resupply the city. The farms and fields that feed Minas Tirith during peace-time will be cut off from us by the lines of the enemy; they might as well be on the moon, for all the good they will do us.\
\
'The only food we will get is the food we already have. Mirudal can tell you more, but it is a worrisome fact that we might simply not have enough.'","The Lower Stores are located just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle.\
\
Mirudal gave you an inventory with which you can take stock of the goods within the Lower Stores.","'Stop. Why do you seek to access the Lower Stores? No one is supposed to be allowed inside.'\
\
You show Dírion the inventory from Mirudal and say that you are here to compare the record of the goods with the actual supplies within.\
\
'Why? Is there really a need for this sort of extra work? Shouldn't we be more concerned with bolstering the defences? Once the enemy is lined up outside the walls of the city, Mirudal may wish he had not wasted effort on the redundant task to which he has set you!\
\
'This is his mark. You may go inside, if you must. But I think it is a foolish waste of time and effort! Finish your task, quickly, and may you turn your eye on more important errands afterward!'","'I have taken stock of the flow of goods into the city over the past few days, and combined it with the existing lists of food and supplies we were storing. This has given me an inventory of our goods, ${PLAYER}, and I have divided it into sections for each of the main storage rooms of Minas Tirith.\
\
'I ask that you take these inventories, one for the goods of the Upper Stores and one for the goods of the Lower Stores. Speak to the guards outside each and show them my mark, and they will allow you inside. Compare the inventory with the actual goods, and ensure that we have all of the supplies we expect.\
\
'Only then will we be able to properly ration the supplies if the siege proves to be long.'","Talk to Túlharil outside the Upper Stores, in the north-east section of the Fifth Circle","'Merethien and Mirudal have been working on a plan to assess the food-stocks and other supplies within the city, and they could use your assistance. They are right over there, and will be glad to have your help.'","'It makes sense to me that rats might covet our goods. I will set the total amount of food to be rationed slightly lower than I planned, in order to account for the rats. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","'I have already said you may go inside, if you must! But I think it is a foolish waste of time and effort. Finish your task, quickly, and may you turn your eye on more important errands afterward!'","The inventory does not match the contents of the Lower Stores. Some food is missing.","Mirudal may be convinced, but your suspicions remain","Talk to Merethien, Master Foodmonger, in the Dome of the Sun","The Upper Stores are located in the north-east section of the Fifth Circle of the city.\
\
Mirudal gave you an inventory with which you can take stock of the goods within the Upper Stores.","'The greatest enemy during a long siege is not necessarily the foe outside the gates, ${PLAYER}! The greatest enemy is hunger. With the gates shut, we will not be able to resupply the city. The farms and fields that feed Minas Tirith during peace-time will be cut off from us by the lines of the enemy; they might as well be on the moon, for all the good they will do us.\
\
'The only food we will get is the food we already have. Mirudal can tell you more, but it is a worrisome fact that we might simply not have enough.'","The Upper Stores are guarded to prevent unlawful access to the goods within","Find the entrance to the Upper Stores, in the north-east section of the Fifth Circle","Confront Dírion outside the Lower Stores, in the First Circle","The Dome of the Sun is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Dírion told you that he suspects rats have gotten into the Stores, and that explains the missing food. He asked you to tell Mirudal about it. The Warden of the Stores may want to lower his expectations for the food-rationing to come, as a result of the rats.","Return the inventories to Mirudal in the Dome of the Sun, and tell him about the rats"},
[483]={"Talk to Dírion outside the Lower Stores, in the First Circle","Talk to Mirudal in the Dome of the Sun and tell him that Dírion will take care of the rats","'Ah, the guard of the Lower Stores plans to take care of the rats? Very good, very good. I will adjust my food-rationing plan to account for a slightly-lower inventory of foodstuffs, but perhaps his actions will help curb the gnawing little nuisances.\
\
'Thank you for your help with this, ${PLAYER}. Tell Dírion I am glad he has taken this effort upon himself, and the city thanks him for his duty.'","'I am so grateful for your efforts on my behalf, ${PLAYER}! Mirudal will not look into the matter of the rats any longer, and I will be able to take the food I need for my family to survive. You have made all this possible, my friend!\
\
'Know that my wife and children thank you as well: Mundil, and Cúnir, and Fionel. These are the names of the people you have saved this day. Remember them, for they will remember you, and fondly!'","Dírion has admitted to stealing food from the Stores he has been trusted with guarding.","'If you can go to the Dome of the Sun and tell Mirudal that I will do my best to take care of the rats, I will be forever in your debt. I thank you, noble ${RACE}, for your understanding!'","A Long Siege - Forgive Him","Dírion is outside the Lower Stores, located just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle.\
\
Mirudal, Warden of the Stores, has asked you to thank Dírion for his duty to the city.","'I am glad the guard of the Lower Stores plans to take care of the rats. Tell him that the city thanks him for his duty.'","Mirudal, the Warden of the Stores, is in the Dome of the Sun.\
\
You have agreed to help Dírion with his deception, so that his family can have the food he stole for them. He asked you to tell Mirudal that he will take care of the rats, and the Warden need not worry about them any longer.","'You... you understand? Oh, ${PLAYER}, I am relieved you can see this from my point of view! You have my family's thanks, and my own!\
\
'If you can go to the Dome of the Sun and tell Mirudal that I will do my best to take care of the rats, I will be forever in your debt. I thank you, noble ${RACE}, for your understanding!'"},
[484]={"Thalhír, the Warden of Laws, is in the Dome of the Sun.\
\
You have decided to report of Dírion's transgression to Thalhír, the Warden of Laws.","'A pox on you! I will not forget this! You are an uncaring, sorry excuse for a ${CLASS}!'","A Long Siege - Turn Him In","'Yes? What brings you to me, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Thalhír about Dírion's theft of food from the Stores he was charged to guard, and Thalhír nods.\
\
'That is an unforgiveable dereliction of his duty, especially in time of war when we face the possibility of a long siege. You have done a good thing for the city, my friend. I will send guards to apprehend him and put him in the lock-house for this transgression.\
\
'I do understand his motivation for this, however. I will send good men to find his family and ensure that they are provided-for, and that they are counted when the food-rationing begins. Still, let their father's sins be a lesson to the young ones that honestly carrying-out one's duties is the better way to serve the city, the Steward, and the Council. Perhaps the longest siege of all is that waged against a man's honesty and sense of duty by the events of these dark days.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for your role in this matter. We are lucky to have you!'","Talk to Thalhír in the Dome of the Sun","'A pox on you! A thousand poxes, ${PLAYER}! To think that one such as you could abandon your fellow man like this! I will not forget this! My hatred goes with you, cursed ${CLASS}!'","Dírion has admitted to stealing food from the Stores he has been trusted with guarding."},
[485]={"'Oh, that father could have seen this night... and that Boromir too could have shared in it.\
\
'Father fought for so long against the Shadow, and this would have been his greatest hope for Gondor and all of Middle-earth. Mithrandir's words at the ceremony did not go unnoticed, ${PLAYER}. Denethor was a proud man, and it was not his weakness, but the might of the Enemy that so twisted his mind in his final years. I do not think ill of him, nor shall I ever.\
\
'After I awoke in the Houses of Healing, I travelled to Rath Dínen. There, amidst the ruins of the House of the Stewards, I took a stone in remembrance of my father.\
\
'With the coronation of the High King and his wedding to Arwen Undómiel, my father should at last be at rest.\
\
'Here, ${PLAYER}. Take this stone and bury it in the soil beside the sapling. Let the memory of my father be joined with the very roots of the White Tree.'","The sapling of the White Tree can be found before the Tower of Ecthelion outside Merethrond.\
\
Faramir has asked you to bury a stone among the soil of the sapling of the White Tree.","As you cover the stone in soil, you consider the life of Denethor","With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits the Steward of Gondor and Prince of Ithilien -- Faramir, son of Denethor.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","Boromir's horn lies before Faramir in Merethrond.\
\
Faramir has asked you to inspect the horn of his fallen brother, Boromir.","Faramir can be found in Merethrond.\
\
You inspected Boromir's horn as Faramir asked. You should talk to Faramir.","A Long-awaited Banquet -- Faramir","'Let us dwell no longer on the past, but instead look to the days ahead.\
\
'I am parted from my love, but it shall not remain so. To bear witness such a union has emboldened my heart.\
\
'When next I see Éowyn, I shall know the words.'","Bury the stone in the soil beside the sapling of the White Tree","Faramir can be found in Merethrond.\
\
You have done as Faramir asked. You should return to Faramir in Merethrond.","Examine Boromir's horn","Cleft in twain after Boromir sounded it at Amon Hen, the horn remains an heirloom of Gondor","Talk to Faramir","'Never have I known such a joyous Midsummer's Day!\
\
'And yet, my mind is troubled. Here I sit, the Steward of Gondor, but the last of my line. When my brother fell in the lands of Rohan, his horn was broken in two. In time, it came into my father's keeping and now it is in mine.\
\
'It is a symbol of Boromir's sacrifice, ${PLAYER}, and one that shall not be forgotten to the Free Peoples of Middle-earth. You have done great deeds in service of my people, and I would allow you to examine it for yourself. \
\
'Let us reflect for a moment in remembrance of Boromir, son of Gondor.'"},
[486]={"Dark ink swirls inside the phial","Habla con Frodo","A Long-awaited Banquet -- Frodo Baggins","Frodo lets out a long sigh and chuckles to himself","Collect sheets of parchment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The quill is well-used, but kept in good care","Collect a writing-quill","Collected sheets of parchment (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Frodo Baggins can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You have collected the writing-quill, phial of ink, and parchment. You should deliver them to Frodo at the wedding banquet in Merethrond.","Deliver the quill, ink, and parchment to Frodo in Merethrond","Writing-quills, phials of ink, and sheets of parchment might be found in either the Houses of Lore or the Blue Theatre.\
\
Frodo has asked you to gather a writing-quill, a phial of ink, and some sheets of parchment that he might begin to write on his adventures.","Frodo Baggins can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
After delivering a quill, ink, and parchment to Frodo Baggins, he appears to have found himself unable to write. You should talk to Frodo.","With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many who have attended, there sits a hobbit of unequalled renown -- Frodo Baggins, the Nine-fingered.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>","'Good evening to you, ${PLAYER}! How have you been enjoying the banquet?\
\
'To my mind, it is hard to recall a more pleasant night in recent memory.'\
\
Frodo shifts in his seat.\
\
'Even so, I have been thinking on all that has happened since I left the Shire. I was wondering what Uncle Bilbo would make of all this business, and that has given me an idea. Uncle Bilbo kept a diary, so why shouldn't I write of my own adventures?\
\
'Could you find me a quill and a phial of ink? Oh, and a few sheets of parchment!'","Wait for Frodo to decide how to start his tale of adventure","Collect a phial of ink","'I suppose I should just enjoy the banquet tonight, shouldn't I?\
\
'I thought I'd so much to say, but the words just will not come to me right now.\
\
'Thank you all the same, ${PLAYER}. I hope you enjoy the rest of the banquet, and I will be sure to tell you when I finish my tale!'","'I must say, even such a grand feast makes me long for the comforts of the Shire.\
\
'Did you find what I asked for? Oh good, good. I do hope it wasn't too much trouble, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Now... where to begin?'","Frodo is deciding where to begin his tale of adventure."},
[487]={"'Now, listen to me.\
\
'No dwarf of good repute would allow a flagon of ale - even one so fine, mind you - to speak on his behalf!\
\
'Ha! Tonight that is what you are for, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Do you see the Lady Galadriel sitting at the wedding-table? Her radiance knows no equal! I have cherished the gift she granted to me since we parted in Lothlórien, and I would grant her one in return.\
\
'I ask only that the Lady Galadriel one day visit the Glittering Caves. It shall be years before my work is finished, but that is not so long a time by the reckoning of Elves.\
\
'Will you do this for me, ${PLAYER}?'","A pitcher of ale can be found at Gimli's table in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Gimli has again asked you to drink with him as he shares his plans for the coming days.","Galadriel can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Gimli has asked you to speak to Galadriel on his behalf and see if she might wish to visit the Glittering Caves or return to Minas Tirith once the city gates are repaired.","With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits a dwarf of the proud line of Durin's Folk -- Gimli, son of Glóin.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","Gimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You have shared a drink with Gimli and should now listen to him.","A Long-awaited Banquet -- Gimli","A pitcher of ale can be found at Gimli's table in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Gimli has asked you to drink with him as he shares his plans for the coming days.","Drink with Gimli again","<rgb=#FF00FF>Listen</rgb> to Gimli","Gimli gestures for you to listen to him","Drink with Gimli","Habla con Galadriel","Gimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Although seemingly flattered, Galadriel has politely declined Gimli's invitation. However, Galadriel did impart that she knows their paths shall cross once again.","'What had the Lady Galadriel to say, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Gimli of Galadriel's words. When you mention that Galadriel knows their paths shall cross once again, a smile spreads across Gimli's face.\
\
'There will be time enough tomorrow to talk of days to come, I think! For tonight, let us be merry!","As you tell Galadriel of Gimli's plans for the coming days and offer an invitation on his behalf, she begins to chuckle softly.\
\
'You may tell Gimli that I have not forgotten the manner of our meeting in Lothlórien, nor have I forgotten the manner of our parting. A gift given freely need not be repaid.\
\
'Although I must decline Gimli's invitation, do not think that I do so in unkindness. I look now to the West for that is where my future leads me. Yet, I know that our paths shall cross once more ere the end.\
\
'Do not let your hearts be troubled in times of such joy. Much still remains to be seen!'","Gimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You have shared another drink with Gimli and should again listen to him.","Gimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Gimli has finished telling of his plans for the comings days, but it seems he wishes to say something else to you.","'Aye, have you ever seen such beauty?'\
\
Gimli glances around at Merethrond, seemingly in awe of the Gondorian craft-skill needed for its construction.\
\
'Fine, indeed, especially for the hands of Men. But what of the hands of dwarves? What of MY hands? You see, it has set my mind on the future!\
\
'Drink with me, ${PLAYER}, and let me tell you of what I seek to do!'","Gimli excitedly gestures for you to listen again","Habla con Gimli"},
[488]={"Unquieted tables can be found throughout Merethrond.\
\
King Aragorn II Elessar has asked you to quiet tables in Merethrond that he might offer a toast.","'What more could I ask of one who has done so much?'\
\
King Aragorn II Elessar smiles at you.\
\
'My words fail me, ${PLAYER}. To be united with my love at last brings me greater joy than I thought knowable by Men. Even so, I must address my people and my honoured guests. Such is the duty of a King!\
\
'I would offer a toast to all in attendance this night. Would you quiet the tables that I might speak?'","With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. At the head of the table beside Queen Arwen Undómiel, sits the King of Gondor and of the High King of the Reunited Kingdom  -- King Aragorn II Elessar.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","Talk to King Aragorn II Elessar","Quieted tables in Merethrond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","King Aragorn II Elessar can be found in Merethrond.\
\
You have quieted all of the tables in the main hall of Merethrond. You should return to King Aragorn II Elessar.","'Allow me to offer a toast, my friend. Be seated if you wish.\
\
'You have my thanks and those of the High Queen.'","A Long-awaited Banquet -- King Aragorn II Elessar","Quiet tables in Merethrond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[489]={"Collected bottles of wine in Merethrond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Mae govannen, ${PLAYER}. It is good to see you!\
\
'Even just a short time ago, I could hardly have imagined sharing such a night with so many friends. Indeed, in the time of Elves, it has been but a moment since we battled together at the Hornburg.'\
\
Legolas smiles to himself.\
\
'Did you know that Gimli and I held a contest of sorts during that long night? Those we slew were counted in each of our favours, and by the dawn, Gimli had bested me by a mere Orc. Forty-two to my count of forty-one, as I recall.\
\
'It seems to me that we are overdue for a rematch. Let us consider it a contest of fortitude. Wine for wine, we shall see which of us is the victor!\
\
'Would you ask him on my behalf?","'I did not grudge him the game at the Hornburg. Perhaps Gimli fears a different outcome this time?'\
\
Legolas smiles wryly.\
\
'Ah, I fear I have chosen my words poorly to the mind of a dwarf. I think I know something certain to win Gimli's attention.\
\
'Will you go down to the kitchens of Merethrond and find some bottles of wine for us? Ten ought to do.\
\
'Once you have done that, challenge Gimli to 'battle' against me. If I have supposed correctly, I think he shall find himself unable to refuse!'","Legolas can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Gimli has politely declined Legolas's invitation. You should return to Legolas.","'Well, well. I suppose we shall see who is the victor by the end of Midsummer's Day!\
\
'Thank you for playing along with our little game, ${PLAYER}.'","Gimli raises an eyebrow appraisingly","Gimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Your challenge seems to have gotten Gimli's attention. You should talk to Gimli.","Collect bottles of wine in Merethrond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A Long-awaited Banquet -- Legolas","'A contest of fortitude? Have you any idea how much I've had already!?\
\
'No, no. You can tell Legolas I appreciate the offer, but this is not the time for such things!'","Gimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You have collected ten bottles of wine as Legolas asked. You should now challenge Gimli to 'battle' Legolas in a contest of fortitude.","With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits an Elf of Eryn Lasgalen -- Legolas, son of Thranduil.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","Bottles of wine can be found in the kitchens of Merethrond.\
\
Legolas has asked you to collect bottles of wine in Merethrond.","'Oh, that's how it's to be then? I'll show both of you!'\
\
Gimli takes five of the bottles you're holding and slides them over to his end of the table.\
\
'Do you see this, Legolas? I'll show you a thing or two about fortitude! Ha-ha!'","Gimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Legolas has asked you to invite Gimli to join him in a contest of fortitude at the wedding banquet. You should talk to Gimli.","Habla con Legolas.","Habla con Gimli","Legolas can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Gimli has enthusiastically accepted Legolas's challenge. You should talk to Legolas.","<rgb=#ff00ff>Challenge</rgb> Gimli to 'battle' Legolas"},
[490]={"Merry's pipe-weed might be found near the baths in the Southern Great Guest-house, among the High Stables, or near the end of the prow of Minas Tirith.\
\
Merry has asked you to find his supply of Longbottom Leaf in Minas Tirith.","Talk to Toldir","'You found it? Oh, wonderful!\
\
'Well, I can't speak for anyone else, but I hope this banquet never ends!'","Return to Merethrond","Among all the crates, barrels, and hay-bales in the High Stables, you find no pipe-weed","Merry's pipe-weed can be found at the base of the stairs to the kitchens in Merethrond.\
\
Toldir informed you that he left Merry's pipe-weed in the kitchens of Merethrond. You should collect it.","Deliver the pipe-weed to Meriadoc Brandybuck","Toldir can be found in Merethrond.\
\
Upon entering Merethrond, Toldir tried to get your attention. You should talk to Toldir.","Collect Merry's pipe-weed in Merethrond","Search for Merry's pipe-weed in the High Stables","A small portion of the stock in Saruman's keeping, but more than enough for a banquet","Merethrond can be found near the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You did not find Merry's pipe-weed in any of the locations he mentioned. You should return to Merethrond and inform him.","Scattered petals from the wedding of Aragorn and Arwen lie nearby, but that is all","'${PLAYER}!\
\
'You're not by chance looking for Master Meriadoc's pipe-weed, are you?\
\
'He gave it to me for safe-keeping before the ceremony, but it has been quite a busy day! If you'd like to bring it to him, I set it near the bottom of the stairs down to the kitchens.\
\
'Oh, and may I help you with anything else? No? Very good!'","The comfort of the baths would be ideal for pipe-weed, but you find no sign of it","Search for Merry's pipe-weed in the Southern Great Guest-house","'Hello, ${PLAYER}! Not getting tired so soon, are you?\
\
'I know just the thing to liven up this banquet! I... just don't quite recall where I left it.\
\
'Back when we were at Isengard, I packed away a bit of the Longbottom Leaf we found in the stores. After all, it's not like Saruman was going to use it stuck up in his tower!\
\
'Anyway, I can't remember if I left my pipe-weed near the baths in the Great Guest-house, by some of the horses in the High Stables, or over by the prow of Minas Tirith. It's got to be one of those!\
\
'If you go find it, I'd be happy to share it with you. Why, I'd be glad to share every last bit of it tonight!'","Merry can be found in Merethrond.\
\
You have collected Merry's pipe-weed and should now return it to him.","With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits a hobbit of some renown -- Meriadoc Brandybuck.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","'It was quite the ceremony, wasn't it? Nothing like a Shire wedding, mind you.\
\
'Have you found the pipe-weed?'","A Long-awaited Banquet -- Meriadoc Brandybuck","As you enter Merethrond, Toldir tries to get your attention","Search for Merry's pipe-weed on the prow of Minas Tirith"},
[491]={"Talk to Mithrandir","'Ah yes, ${PLAYER}. I suppose I owe you an explanation as to why I requested these particular tomes.\
\
'You see...'\
\
Mithrandir gestures to Frodo and Samwise and hands them the tomes. Frodo and Sam place the tomes on their seats, and hop back onto them. Mithrandir smiles at you.\
\
'Need I explain further?\
\
'After all, I cannot be everywhere at once. Not as you so often seem to be!'","Collect the 'Chronicle of Arnor' in the High Guest-house","'You've found them?'\
\
Mithrandir glances to his right and looks at Frodo and Samwise.\
\
'Yes, yes. These will do.'","With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits one of the Wise -- Mithrandir, the Wizard known beyond the lands of Gondor as Gandalf the White.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","Mithrandir can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Mithrandir has not revealed why he needed the tomes from his guest-chamber. You should wait and see if he will soon reveal their purpose.","This dense volume is bound in leather","Mithrandir can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You have found the tomes that Mithrandir requested and should now deliver them to him at the wedding banquet.","Collect 'On the Line of Kings' in the High Guest-house","Mithrandir appears to notice your gaze","'On the Line of Kings' and the 'Chronicle of Arnor' can be found in Mithrandir's guest-chamber in the High Guest-house.\
\
Mithrandir has asked you to collect two tomes from his guest-chamber in the High Guest-house and return them to him in Merethrond.","Deliver the tomes of lore to Mithrandir in Merethrond","Mithrandir can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Mithrandir seems prepared to discuss the purpose of the tomes he requested from his guest-chamber. You should talk to Mithrandir.","'Ah, and how are you enjoying this fine banquet? Quite a bit, I hope, for I most certainly am!\
\
'Although...'\
\
Mithrandir pauses and looks to the ends of the table.\
\
'I must confess that in my haste to take my seat here in Merethrond, I seem to have forgotten something in my guest-chamber. If it were of little import, I am certain it could wait until after the banquet. Unfortunately, it cannot.\
\
'In my keeping, there are two tomes from the Houses of Lore. The first is a treatise on the line of Kings in Gondor, and the other is a chronicle of the Northern Kingdom.\
\
'Will you fetch them for me?'","This heavy tome has been kept in remarkable condition","A Long-awaited Banquet -- Mithrandir"},
[492]={"Travel to the Old Guest-house","A Long-awaited Banquet -- Peregrin Took","Gathered food for the inhabitants of the Old Guest-house (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The children can be found just outside the Old Guest-house in the First Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You have arrived at the Old Guest-house with the platters of food you gathered in Merethrond. You should offer it to the children that they might share it with the other inhabitants of the Old Guest-house.","'See? We hobbits know a thing or two about bending the rules!\
\
'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'","Various platters of food can be found in the kitchens of Merethrond.\
\
Pippin has asked you to gather food from the kitchens of Merethrond that it might be give to the children and refugees seeking shelter in the Old Guest-house.","Deliver the sealed missive to Beregond","'It's a shame that all of our friends can't celebrate with us, but... the King and I came to something of an agreement.\
\
'You see, the King was quite fond of my idea to look after the children and refugees still dwelling in the Old Guest-house. That one did not take much convincing on my part, thankfully! However...'\
\
Pippin produces a sealed missive from his pocket.\
\
'...this proved to be a much more difficult discussion.\
\
'${PLAYER}, why don't you give this to Beregond?'","The Old Guest-house can be found in the First Circle to the south of the gates of Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Pippin has asked you to deliver the food you collected to the inhabitants of the Old Guest-house.","Beregond can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Pippin has asked you to give a sealed missive to Beregond.","A few of the children who dwell in the Old Guest-house appear to be waiting","Pippin can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
You successfully delivered the platters of food to the inhabitants of the Old Guest-house. You should return to Pippin.","'And here I thought we hobbits had feasts all sorted out!\
\
'Ah, but I suppose it's time to make good on a promise I made to some friends down in the Old Guest-house. I had intended to deliver some platters of food to them, but it seems I'm in no position to leave this banquet. After all, who knows what could go wrong if Merry and I weren't around to see that it goes perfectly?\
\
'Could you go down to the kitchens of Merethrond and collect as many platters of food as you can bear? After that, well, just stroll down to the Old Guest-house and I think my friends will be waiting for you!\
\
'I knew I could count on you, ${PLAYER}!'","With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits a hobbit of some renown -- Peregrin Took.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","'What is this?'\
\
Beregond opens the missive and begins to read it.\
\
'This is the same invitation that Prince Faramir received. It is the very invitation that allowed me to return to Minas Tirith for the High King's wedding... and to see my beloved Gilithel and Bergil.\
\
'This was your doing, Peregrin? I do not know what to say!'\
\
Pippin smiles at Beregond.\
\
'Thank you for allowing me the chance to be among my family in Minas Tirith, even if it is only for one night!'","Pippin can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer).\
\
Beregond has learned the truth of his invitation to the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar and Arwen Undómiel. You should talk to Pippin.","'Did Prince Peregrin send you? He told us he had something special planned for us!'\
\
You offer the platters of food to the children at the Old Guest-house.\
\
'Is all of this for us? I'll make sure we share it with everyone else.\
\
'Thank you so much! And tell the Prince we say thanks, too!'","Deliver the platters of food to the children at the Old Guest-house","Capítulo 14: La Puerta Negra","Gather food for the inhabitants of the Old Guest-house (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[493]={"Talk to Samwise Gamgee","Aided Samwise to dispel worrisome thoughts of the Shire (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Sam has found respite in a small alcove beneath the main hall of Merethrond","'You see, I feel as if I've only just realized I've not had more than a moment or two afore tonight to think about what I left behind at home in the Shire. I wonder how my family is... and I wonder if the Cottons think I'm ever coming home. If I were them, I'd be of half a mind to believe me dead!\
\
'I miss the Shire just as much as Mister Frodo, but I'll have an awful lot to explain to Rosie when I get home.\
\
'It's a difficult thing, ${PLAYER}. These worrisome thoughts of home are heavy on my heart, and I wish I knew how to press on in spite of them.\
\
'I hope you don't mind me saying so, but you've always seemed so determined... at least to me! Could you help me to push away these thoughts so I can enjoy myself tonight?'","A Long-awaited Banquet -- Samwise Gamgee","Meet Samwise Gamgee in a small alcove in Merethrond","With the One Ring destroyed and the Enemy undone, the Free Peoples of Middle-earth gather to Minas Tirith for a grand banquet commemorating the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar to Queen Arwen Undómiel. Among the many in attendance, there sits a hobbit of some renown -- Samwise Gamgee.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","'A fine evening, it is.\
\
'Say, ${PLAYER}, I'd like to have a word with you in someplace a bit more quiet. There's an alcove down the stairs across from this table, so I hear.\
\
'Would you meet me there? It's not a conversation befitting this table, if you understand my meaning.'","Samwise Gamgee can be found in a small alcove of Merethrond, across from the High King and High Queen's table and down the stairs.\
\
Samwise Gamgee has asked you to accompany him to a small alcove in Merethrond where he wishes to speak further to you.","Samwise Gamgee can be found in a small alcove of Merethrond, across from the High King and High Queen's table and down the stairs.\
\
You have found Samwise Gamgee in a quiet alcove beneath the main hall of Merethrond. You should talk to Samwise Gamgee.","Aid Samwise to dispel worrisome thoughts of the Shire (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Samwise Gamgee can be found in a small alcove of Merethrond, across from the High King and High Queen's table and down the stairs.\
\
You have helped Samwise dispel his worrisome thoughts of the Shire. You should talk to Samwise Gamgee.","Samwise's worrisome thoughts can be found throughout Merethrond.\
\
Samwise Gamgee has begun to worry about the friends and family he left behind in the Shire. You should help him dispel these worrisome thoughts.","'Oh, thank you. Now if you don't mind me saying so, I've a banquet to attend!'"},
[495]={"'I knew it.\
\
'There were definitely several inconsistencies in many of the reports of this hammer's existence.\
\
'So now our best lead takes us up north to Jeb Khâtel.\
\
'I must ask you this last favour, because though the journey seems fraught with danger, I see in you a capable leader.\
\
'Come back with this hammer, or come back alive. I will not allow another blind rush into darkness, with your life being forfeit.'","'A large hammer? I seen that, yea. Massive one isn't it?\
\
'You'll find plenty of stolen goods and contraband in the shallows, I reckon.\
\
'Lots of people lose their stuff around those parts all the time. I'm sure you can find your hammer there.'","You've gathered as much information as you can","You've gathered all the information you can from the townsfolk of Halrax. You now have a lead. You should talk to Ithurga.\
\
Ithurga can be found in Halrax.","All the witnesses had varying tales, but a professor has told us Shereb knows of this hammer.\
\
You can find Shereb in the most isolated part of Halrax.","'You're looking for Marâkh, Mother of Tempests?\
\
'That is quite the endeavour you've undertaken. You know, many historians will argue the very existence of such a thing... but I place evidence high on my list, and where there is the mark of such a weapon existing, I cannot be but consumed by the possibilities.\
\
'My good friend, who does most of the travelling so that I may have the most accurate information, may have something for you. His name is Shereb.\
\
'You can find Shereb in the most isolated parts of Halrax.'","'You have my gratitude for helping my man out there. I'm afraid it was for naught.\
\
'It's as I feared. It's a replica. There have been numerous accounts from the folks in town of having seen this thing.\
\
'The only issue is that by all those accounts, none lead here.\
\
'Why don't you go around and confirm all of the reports? Else we done all this for a novel trinket and nothin' more.'","'A hammer? Well, if I recall correctly, I heard tale in the tavern of a man passing through the shallows coming from the north.\
\
'Talk of a wild freak of nature swinging around a hammer. Sadly, I have no more information for you.'","Ithurga suspects this is a replica and wants you to confirm all the rumours about this hammer from the town's residents.","Confirm witness accounts (${CURRENT}/8)","'A giant hammer? Well, you must be talking nonsense.\
\
'That is the stuff of legend here on the isles. No one has seen the real one in ages.\
\
'If I recall the texts correctly, it was Marâkh, Mother of Tempests. But honestly, a hammer controlling the storms? I am unconvinced such a weapon exists.'","A Long-forgotten Relic","'A mythological hammer, you say? Well, I have my fair share of tools working on cultivating the harsh land that is these islands.\
\
'But never had a need for a giant hammer. Nope. Just me and my herbs.'","'A hammer? You think I get out lookin' for hammers?\
\
'I only have one job in this town and that's not to look for hammers.'","Talk to Ithurga","'A mythical hammer? Dunno know what yer talkin about.\
\
'If ye be needin' a smithy, we gots plenty.'","Confirm witness accounts 7/8","You delivered what seems to be a replica of a forgotten myth.","'I knew you'd be here sooner or later.\
\
'The town stirs at the possible mention of Marâkh, Mother of Tempests.\
\
'But this isn't a weapon you can just go and retrieve. It's risky.\
\
'In case I can't convince you to give up your chase - there exists an island in Jeb Khâtel, past the shallows to the north-west.\
\
'I warn you, this will not be journey free of hardship. Prepare yourself accordingly.'"},
[496]={"You recount all that you saw to Gondrad and his face slowly twists into a frown.\
\
'I see two reasons to be perfectly miserable, ${PLAYER}. First and foremost is that these men are truly as numerous, ruthless, and fell as we had feared. And secondly - you found no better reason to turn back and go home without completing the deal.'","'There is no way out of this, I am afraid. We must march right up to the camp and deliver the ransom... and if we are lucky, walk out with our hides!'","In short time, the Variags have erected palisades and watch-towers","You have the ransom Jarl Akhiz demanded for two of Lady Glánhar's sons.","Meet Gondrad before Jarl Akhiz's camp at Bâr Nadhron.","The manor of Bâr Nadhron looms above, ruined. The cellar likely lies beneath","'We have both parts of the ransom now, so I suppose we must press on. To Bâr Nadhron, ${PLAYER}, though I have an ill feeling about this!'","A Look Before the Leap","Explore the various entrances of Jarl Akhiz's camp in Bâr Nadhron.","'Look at that! This Jarl could certainly take Ost Rimmon. I wonder if he knows it?\
\
'Now, I have been pondering what Lady Glánhar said about caution. Call me coward and cuff me on the ear, but I would scout around the edges of the camp and see what may be seen, if I were you.\
\
'As for myself, this is as close I have courage to go!'","The Variag camp is fully manned and armed - and well-guarded","Explore each entrance of the camp (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Lady Glánhar bade us to use caution and wit. If stealthily scouting out their camp is not caution, then I am a hapless fool. Well, most likely, I am a hapless fool all the same.'","The sheer number of arrows and corpses tell a tale of capture by brutal force","Bâr Nadhron has been burnt, and no doubt pillaged, ruthlessly","Return to Gondrad","Return to Gondrad just outside the camp at Bâr Nadhron.","Meet Gondrad at Bâr Nadhron"},
[497]={"A Looming Enemy","The shore is littered with the bodies of Orcs that drowned while fleeing the battle...","Patrol the shores of the Anduin to the north of Osgiliath","You discover the mangled remains of a Ranger who appears to have fallen a great distance...","Patrol the foot-hills of the Ephel Dúath to east of Bâr Aroth","Although the battle is ended, Thurindol fears that the Enemy will soon muster more of his forces against Gondor within North Ithilien.","'After the great battle, we had much to consider, my friend.\
\
'The Orcs claimed Bâr Aroth and from the north, the Khundolar struck and made inroads from Dagorlad.\
\
'Where the rest that fled the battle have gone I do not know for certain, but I fear many may have found new refuge within North Ithilien.\
\
'In these dark times, I count myself fortunate to have your trust and I give you mine in return.\
\
'I would ask that you search the shores of the Anduin to the west, the hill-top to the north of Bâr Aroth, and the foot-hills of the Ephel Dúath, the Mountains of Shadow, for signs of our foes.\
\
'When you have finished your patrol, meet me to the north at the old baths of Aelin Veren, and it is there we shall speak more on what is to be done in the coming days.'","Bâr Aroth can be found on a hillside to the north of the Cross-roads in North Ithilien.\
\
Thurindol has asked you to assess the Enemy's presence in North Ithilien before you continue your journey to the refuge.","A heavy shadow hangs over you, but you cannot spy what might have cast it...","Patrol the hill-top to the north of Bâr Aroth","'While I am gladdened that many Orcs failed in their crossing of the Anduin, I fear we will not soon see the last of the Enemy's wraiths and their terrible, flying beasts.\
\
'We shall have to use greater caution in our movements, lest we be discovered from above. For my part, I am glad that you remained hidden from their sight, my friend.\
\
'I shall bring these tidings to captain Anborn at Henneth Annûn.'","Thurindol can be found at Aelin Veren.\
\
You have scouted the lands surrounding Bâr Aroth and should bring news to Thurindol at Aelin Veren.","Talk to Thurindol at Aelin Veren"},
[498]={"Hablar con Avorthal","Ayuda a Erfith con 'Un trato que salió mal'","'¡Saludos! ¿Te envían los Fronteros de esta tierra?\
\
'Soy Avorthal, y el compañero con el hacha es Athal. No solemos viajar más allá de las tierras de Ered Luin, pero este asunto es bastante urgente. Hace no mucho, nuestros dos pueblos casi entraron en guerra por una disputa orquestada por Skorgrím Duramano y los de su ralea. Mi padre, Cardavor, resultó herido en la batalla y Skorgrím huyó de Ered Luin, pero todavía hay otras amenazas.\
\
'De todas formas, me temo que mi compañero y yo no hemos venido para una alegre misión. Se han avistado trasgos cruzando el río Lune hacia las ruinas de Lhúngobel y es posible que intenten interferir en los asuntos de la Comarca. Además, hemos capturado a un Duramano, pero no esgrime ningún arma contra nosotros y nos pide ayuda.\
\
'Admito que es algo inusual. ¿Hablarás con el Duramano y nos ayudarás a librar a la Comarca de estos trasgos?'","'Incluso aunque Skorgrím amenazó la vida de mi padre, no pensaría en buscar venganza contra todos los Duramano. Es lástima lo que merecen... no mi ira. Una oscuridad ha atrapado a su gente, ¡con el rostro de su antiguo señor!\
\
'Por nuestra parte, Athal y yo continuaremos vigilando Ered Luin. Si los Duramano han vuelto realmente a Sarnúr, sin duda volveremos a llamarte. Sobre los trasgos, ¡expulsaremos hasta el último de ellos!\
\
'Tienes mi agradecimiento, ${PLAYER}.'","Avorthal se encuentra en una colina junto al camino cerca de la frontera de Ered Luin con la Comarca Allende.\
\
Has ayudado a Avorthal y a Athal a expulsar a los trasgos que cruzaron el río Lune, a liberar a los compañeros de Erfith que buscaban la paz, y averiguado el plan de los Duramano para convocar a sus malvados aliados a la antigua fortaleza de Sarnúr. Debes hablar con Avorthal.","Una amenaza inminente","Athal y Erfith se encuentran en una colina junto al camino cerca de la frontera de Ered Luin con la Comarca Allende.\
\
Avorthal te ha pedido que ayudes a Athal y al Duramano Erfith a expulsar a los trasgos que han cruzado a la Comarca Allende.","El elfo Avorthal y el enano, Athal vigilan de cerca Ered Luin y las tierras circundantes.","Ayuda a Athal con 'El Cazarrecompensas de Lhúngobel'"},
[499]={"'Este acertijo me tiene perplejo. Lo siento.'","'Te di el acertijo de Berenin, ${PLAYER}. Resuélvelo, y sabrás la ubicación de otra de las llaves del legado que Berenin me dejó.'","'¡Conozco la respuesta a este acertijo, ${PLAYER}! ¡Estás buscando la estatua del Toro Bramador, quien le voló la cabeza al malvado Golfimbul hace mucho tiempo y de paso inventó el juego del golf!\
\
'La estatua del Toro Bramador está en Tejonera, en los Campos Verdes, en la Comarca.'","Isferon te dio el primero de los acertijos de Berenin.\
\
Isferon espera que puedas descubrir la solución al acertijo de Berenin y recoger la primera de tres llaves en el lugar que se describe.","Lleva la segunda llave de Berenin a Isferon.","Voluntad de un Sabio","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir? La cueva no está lejos de aquí, y entonces sabremos qué secretos dejó Berenin bajo mi cuidado.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario, y no puede completarse con una Comunidad.</rgb>","'Los hobbits tienen una leyenda sobre uno de los suyos que mató a un trasgo de un solo golpe con una porra. Podría ser que este acertijo se relacione con esa leyenda, aunque no conozco los detalles.'","'¡Creo que sé la solución! Parece que el viajero comenzó en el Poney Pisador y luego caminó un día completo hacia el este. ¿Qué hay a un día de viaje al este de Bree? La Posada Abandonada.\
\
'¡Y además, la posada tiene un gran agujero en el techo! ¡Desde cierto punto de vista, eso suena como una ventana que no se puede cerrar!'","'¿No habrás perdido la llave, verdad?'","'No conozco la respuesta a este acertijo. Lo siento.'","'Este acertijo parece referirse a las Montañas Azules, conocidas en élfico como Ered Luin. Creo que ese es el significado de \\qella corre por lo azul;\\q si puedes descifrar el resto, deberías poder resolverlo.'","'Este acertijo parece referirse a las Montañas Azules, llamadas Ered Luin por los Elfos. \\qElla corre por lo azul\\q me suena a una referencia a las Montañas Azules.'","'No conozco el acertijo, pero si caminas \\qmedio día hacia el sol y medio día alejándote del sol,\\q habrás recorrido un día de viaje, pues si comienzas por la mañana, la mitad del día te acerca al sol y la otra mitad lo ves hundirse detrás de ti.'","Isferon te dio el tercero de los acertijos de Berenin.\
\
Isferon espera que puedas descubrir la solución al acertijo de Berenin y recoger la última de las tres llaves en el lugar que se describe.","'¡Creo saber algo sobre este acertijo, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}! \\qUn poderoso golpe\\q solo puede referirse a Toro Bramador Tuk, quien de un solo golpe le arrancó la cabeza a Golfimbul.\
\
'Todo el evento se recuerda por la estatua de Toro Bramador que se encuentra en Tejonera, en los Campos Verdes.'","'Nunca había oído este acertijo. ¿Algo relacionado con trasgos? ¿Dónde hay trasgos?'","'No sé mucho sobre el resto, pero suena como que \\qel hombre dejó su caballo\\q implica que alguien comenzó en el Poney Pisador y luego fue a algún lugar.'","'Te di el segundo de los acertijos de Berenin, ${PLAYER}. Resuélvelo, y sabrás la ubicación de otra de las llaves del legado que Berenin me dejó.'","Lleva la tercera llave de Berenin a Isferon.","'¡Encontraste la primera llave, ${PLAYER}! Estoy impresionado, pues ciertamente lo estaba pensando de forma equivocada. \\qElla corre por lo azul\\q me parecía una nube en el cielo, y desde ahí ya iba por mal camino.\
\
'Pero estas son las Montañas Azules, si recuerdas uno de sus nombres, y desde ahí no es tan difícil. Berenin siempre veía las cosas con más sencillez que yo. Recuerdo que solía reprenderme por complicar demasiado las cosas — este acertijo suyo parece una lección, ahora que lo pienso.\
\
'Me pregunto qué hay dentro de las cajas que dejó bajo mi cuidado cuando zarpó hacia el Oeste. ¡Quedan dos acertijos, ${PLAYER}! ¡Resuelve este, y estaremos más cerca de descubrir el legado que Berenin me dejó!'","'Este es un acertijo interesante. No puedo descifrar mucho, pero creo que \\qen una mano, un guardián silencioso\\q casi con certeza se refiere a una estatua de algún tipo.'","Resuelve el tercer acertijo de Berenin y recoge una llave del lugar correcto.","Resuelve el primer acertijo de Berenin y recoge una llave del lugar correcto.","'No sé la respuesta a este acertijo. Mis disculpas.'","'El único caballo por aquí es el del Poney Pisador, en Bree. Suena como si alguien hubiera comenzado allí, en todo caso. Lamento no saber nada sobre el resto del acertijo.'","'¿Has oído hablar de mi enigma, ${PLAYER}? No sé por qué no puedo descubrir la solución — ¡yo, que he estudiado las artes de la llama y la ceniza, y los misterios del tizne y el carbón!\
\
'Mi amigo Berenin perdió la esperanza en la Tierra Media y zarpó hacia el Oeste hace algún tiempo. Me dejó tres pequeñas cajas, y dijo que cuando pudiera resolver los acertijos que dejó en mi poder, podría abrirlas. Me duele que Berenin se haya ido y quisiera saber qué secretos me dejó, pero no soy capaz de resolver los acertijos. Mis intereses principales son los ungüentos y las mezclas, no los juegos de palabras ni las trivialidades.\
\
'Estoy seguro de que Berenin dejó las llaves de cada caja en los lugares que resuelven cada acertijo, pero no sé dónde pueden estar. Te daré el primer acertijo, y si puedes traerme la llave, entonces te daré el segundo, y así continuaremos hasta descubrir qué secretos me dejó Berenin cuando zarpó hacia el Oeste. ¡Te doy el primer acertijo y te deseo buena fortuna al descifrarlo!'","Habla con Isferon y viaja con él a la cueva.","'No estoy seguro sobre este acertijo. \\qNingún Hombre\\q, debe referirse a un Elfo, enano o hobbit, pero nunca he oído de un enano o Elfo que encaje.'","'No conozco la solución a tu acertijo, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} mío.'","'No puedo agradecerte lo suficiente, ${PLAYER}. Escuchar las palabras de Berenin trajo una alegría a mi corazón que no sentía desde hace muchos años, y conocer mejor sus pensamientos es el mayor secreto que tu ayuda podría haberme traído.\
\
'No soy tan hábil con las palabras como tú, ni como lo era Berenin, pero con las llamas danzantes no tengo igual. Quizás pueda enseñarte algo a cambio de la alegría que me has traído, ${PLAYER}. No es mucho, pero espero que te ayude en tus viajes.'","'Me encantan los acertijos, ¡pero nunca había oído este antes!'","'Este acertijo es difícil, ${PLAYER}. ¡No tengo idea!'","Isferon está en el refugio de Duillond, en Ered Luin.\
\
Ahora que has resuelto el segundo de los tres acertijos que le dio su amigo Berenin, deberías devolver la llave que encontraste a Isferon en Duillond.","'Este acertijo me tiene desconcertado, a${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Lo siento.'","'Si comienzas por la mañana y caminas medio día hacia el sol, durante la otra mitad el sol se hunde detrás de ti.\
\
'No sé qué significa el resto del acertijo.'","Un Sabio busca resolver todos los misterios del mundo, pero si decide compartir las soluciones con otros, eso suele ser una característica definitoria.","'Creo que sé la solución, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Parece que el viajero comenzó en el Poney Pisador y luego caminó un día completo hacia el este. ¿Qué hay a un día de viaje al este de Bree? La Posada Abandonada.'","Isferon está en el refugio de Duillond, en Ered Luin.\
\
Te has convertido en parte de la búsqueda de Isferon para descubrir el legado de su amigo Berenin resolviendo los acertijos que dejó, y ahora Isferon espera viajar contigo a la cueva donde guardó las cajas cerradas de Berenin.","Isferon te dio el segundo de los acertijos de Berenin.\
\
Isferon espera que puedas descubrir la solución al acertijo de Berenin y recoger la segunda de tres llaves en el lugar que se describe.","'Te di el tercero de los acertijos de Berenin, ${PLAYER}. Resuélvelo, y sabrás la ubicación de otra de las llaves del legado que Berenin me dejó.'","'Un acertijo interesante, ${PLAYER}. ¿Podría ser que \\qella corre por lo azul\\q se refiera en realidad a las Montañas Azules? Esta zona puede ser llamada Ered Luin por los Elfos, ¡pero su nombre correcto es Montañas Azules!'","'No estoy seguro sobre este acertijo. \\qNingún Hombre, él\\q debe significar que no estás buscando en Breeland, al menos. Esto debe referirse a un Elfo, enano o hobbit.'","'Nunca había oído este acertijo antes. Tal vez Bilbo tenga mejor fortuna para descifrarlo.'","'Esta es la última llave, , ¡y ahora podemos abrir las tres cajas que Berenin dejó para mí! Las he guardado en una cueva cercana para mantenerlas a salvo, una cueva que exploré con Berenin hace mucho tiempo. Recuerdo que el agua en las paredes hacía una especie de música al caer en charcas en el suelo... aunque la cueva ha estado seca y vacía durante muchos años.\
\
'Ahora tú también eres parte de esto, . Avísame si estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir, y podremos viajar juntos a la cueva y descubrir qué secretos dejó Berenin.'","Isferon está en el refugio de Duillond, en Ered Luin.\
\
Ahora que has resuelto el último de los tres acertijos que le dio su amigo Berenin, deberías devolver la llave que encontraste a Isferon en Duillond.","Isferon está en Duillond, el refugio en Ered Luin.\
\
Descubriste el legado de Berenin: un deseo de no ser olvidado por su amigo y de participar en un último juego de acertijos. Ayudaste a Isferon a no perder de vista la memoria de su amigo. Isferon está esperando para hablar contigo nuevamente.","'¡Este acertijo me tiene perplejo! ¡Lo siento!'","'¡Este acertijo me parece muy fácil, ${PLAYER}! ¡Piénsalo! \\qElla corre por lo azul\\q casi con certeza se refiere a las Montañas Azules, conocidas entre los Elfos como Ered Luin. \\qLa sombra del paso\\q tiene que ser un puente, y en los acertijos \\qun guardián silencioso\\q casi siempre es una estatua.\
\
'¡Solo necesitas buscar cerca de una estatua bajo un puente largo en Ered Luin para encontrar la solución a este acertijo, te lo aseguro!'","'¡Este acertijo es desconcertante, ${PLAYER}! ¡Lo único que se me ocurre es que \\qla sombra del paso\\q podría ser un puente! ¿La solución podría estar bajo un puente?'","Resuelve el segundo acertijo de Berenin y recoge una llave del lugar correcto.","Isferon está en el refugio de Duillond, en Ered Luin.\
\
Te han dicho que Isferon tiene un enigma que no puede resolver. Como Isferon es un Sabio muy erudito, este enigma debe ser realmente difícil.","Isferon está en el refugio de Duillond, en Ered Luin.\
\
Ahora que has resuelto el primero de los tres acertijos que le dio su amigo Berenin, deberías devolver la llave que encontraste a Isferon en Duillond.","'Este acertijo me tiene desconcertado. ¿Por qué alguien querría recordar a los trasgos? ¿Y qué es eso de \\qun poderoso golpe?\\q ¿Alguien mató a un trasgo? ¡Eso sí que lo apruebo!'","'Me sigues sorprendiendo,  — ¡eres ${PLAYERNAME:un Sabio más erudito[m]|una Sabia más erudita[f]} que yo, eso está claro! Quizás pueda enseñarte algo sobre el movimiento del fuego, pero para resolver acertijos eres mucho mejor que yo.\
\
'Berenin era igual — solía plantearme entretenimientos confusos para que intentara descifrarlos, y solo lograba resolverlos en raras ocasiones. Siempre estaba dispuesto a darme pistas cuando me alejaba demasiado del corazón del asunto, y su risa ante mi confusión siempre era cálida — nunca había burla en ella. Había olvidado el sonido de su risa hasta ahora.\
\
'Queda un acertijo, . ¡Estoy seguro de que Berenin estaría impresionado con tu resolución de los dos primeros!'","'Isferon, en el refugio de Duillond en Ered Luin, ha recibido un enigma que espera que un verdadero Sabio pueda resolver. Ha guardado los detalles para sí mismo, pero si lo buscas, estoy seguro de que el enigma te interesará.\
\
'El propio Isferon es un Sabio muy erudito... me pregunto qué clase de enigma podría escapar a su comprensión.'","Lleva la primera llave de Berenin a Isferon.","'No conozco la solución a este acertijo, aunque quizás si puedes pensar en algún lugar donde se recuerde a los trasgos, podrías estar en lo cierto.\
\
'Pero ¿por qué alguien querría recordar a los trasgos?'","'Este acertijo me intriga. Quizás la \\qsombra del paso\\q se refiera a la sombra bajo algún tipo de puente.'","'No conozco la respuesta al acertijo, pero quizás Bilbo tenga mejor suerte para descifrarlo.'"},
}
